{"doc_id": "doc302", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The first five seasons of Prison Break have been released on DVD and Blu-ray in Regions 1, 2, and 4. Each DVD boxed set includes all of the broadcast episodes from that season, the associated special episode, commentary from cast and crew, and profiles of various parts of Prison Break, such as Fox River State Penitentiary or the tattoo. Prison Break is also available online, including iTunes, Amazon Video, and Netflix. After the premiere of the second season of Prison Break, Fox began online streaming of the prior week's episode, though it originally restricted viewing to the United States.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 653841413, "similarity": 0.9819078947368421, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5a09a4d4c00fc8b1edcbfb50fb8d007e492c6e99662773fda3efebb6437a7ec8", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "five", "matched_aliases": ["five"], "query_id": "test15", "question_hash": "39773c5886c00e1d3332f2a1c98bcc65e6fb749e818b9391b6fb82ae508c82bf", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ab5f0a44f6f0bb1490bd3061b4e0abd0636c686055c57dd5be622750510e1682", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 155154925, "similarity": 0.1951219512195122, "source_content_hash": "277f0900d2f420e004f06cbd5942dfd66cc365a69fd7e6bb3069d1953bb36b6c", "source_hash": "09383ff7993fd44a8a3c17524505355c696f675ded0a35063c1ce500fd15f331", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "73876bbfd9eec93e8bb5ed257e618a99a3ec8ecffce6b60cd13256c2ad1d6d2c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc305", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "By August 1945, the Allies' Manhattan Project had produced two types of atomic bomb, and the 509th Composite Group of the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) was equipped with the specialized Silverplate version of the Boeing B-29 Superfortress that could deliver them from Tinian in the Mariana Islands. Orders for atomic bombs to be used on four Japanese cities were issued on July 25. On August 6, one of its B-29s dropped a Little Boy uranium gun-type bomb on Hiroshima. Three days later, on August 9, a Fat Man plutonium implosion-type bomb was dropped by another B-29 on Nagasaki. The bombs immediately devastated their targets. Over the next two to four months, the acute effects of the atomic bombings killed 90,000–146,000 people in Hiroshima and 39,000–80,000 people in Nagasaki; roughly half of the deaths in each city occurred on the first day. Large numbers of people continued to die from the effects of burns, radiation sickness, and other injuries, compounded by illness and malnutrition, for many months afterward. In both cities, most of the dead were civilians, although Hiroshima had a sizable military garrison.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1891090301, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "33e893887641df06f5c2b2fea5bf0861c1e726c4ea14e0b0263271498dfceee2", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Little Boy", "matched_aliases": ["Little Boy"], "query_id": "test16", "question_hash": "9a739edbad08cd71e49ca455063d84b3d0b82490917c9f61682d62d97ccaad8b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "661165b468382cbe48bec80e038ab2fbd975ea40a0adfccf9d03a414ab5fe70f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1993784779, "similarity": 0.2928416485900217, "source_content_hash": "fe0d56e3a89c106d92808e0a49157005a98036d2c5db6ec79fda8a630054c9eb", "source_hash": "c3cd012ed1a319b10e0e6db55c3ec361660de45403c9293c0fd2ddacbc32e3bd", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "8533abd0f782eb62f51884aed1a60d63c5a2c102f6df2d4c7f5837b2cdb794d7", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc565", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The mammalian sperm cell consists of a head, neck, a midpiece and a tail. The head contains the nucleus with densely coiled chromatin fibres, surrounded anteriorly by an acrosome, which contains enzymes used for penetrating the female egg. The neck contains the sperm centriole. The midpiece has a central filamentous core with many mitochondria spiralled around it, used for ATP production for the journey through the female cervix, uterus and uterine tubes. The tail or \"flagellum\" executes the lashing movements that propel the spermatocyte.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1944801355, "similarity": 0.997250229147571, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "4267336c9f9a3bfd3213e31c7617db4f72621163f6f2bb1ebcd20a228afb0faa", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "midpiece", "matched_aliases": ["midpiece"], "query_id": "test19", "question_hash": "bc7c52bd0855ff720f8e131e41e68bbe3765d7513274f56cdea2bac979cc095f", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "172b15148f99a8d7ade4a4a45da553ee4769792e85cf20edb7bd51221e669e9b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2013428092, "similarity": 0.12419700214132762, "source_content_hash": "001794e4811ee482d5f6731632c8b0a3d1fcf025e1d404885e7d279dfb301894", "source_hash": "1de3bf75a3a1c058a88b01881229459b3de577938e4a57cf12bbd823c2095fd6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "40b005bfcc62e7fcce346dfe050b94fd097e36b16a7e2e388c7cf5ffa9027ca4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc579", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Motile sperm cells typically move via flagella and require a water medium in order to swim toward the egg for fertilization. In animals most of the energy for sperm motility is derived from the metabolism of fructose carried in the seminal fluid. This takes place in the mitochondria located in the sperm's midpiece (at the base of the sperm head). These cells cannot swim backwards due to the nature of their propulsion. The uniflagellated sperm cells (with one flagellum) of animals are referred to as spermatozoa, and are known to vary in size.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 416762294, "similarity": 0.9846984698469847, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e3a7a23443973a2431739f07b7652dc15175db3f68947c17cbc750caefdbb584", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "midpiece", "matched_aliases": ["midpiece"], "query_id": "test19", "question_hash": "bc7c52bd0855ff720f8e131e41e68bbe3765d7513274f56cdea2bac979cc095f", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "220ca102090dd6bf914a97034958cbcd22ba5b25e7f2455cc652eccc1993a5e8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 400662951, "similarity": 0.046511627906976744, "source_content_hash": "63ec59e8a224910083a7f4353595de49dee62d536e05ab2eff50f35b197ff804", "source_hash": "275251ee033e715330b17b0597cae0d6e0ddc92d4782fb08758828f7f9b34f05", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "aeed2e76898db253038efb66f4ad0cbc6f35e9bdd640a887d32fbb01911b52d0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc618", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "An equilateral triangle is the most symmetrical triangle, having 3 lines of reflection and rotational symmetry of order 3 about its center. Its symmetry group is the dihedral group of order 6 D3.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 171821929, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "552a16e937b390500dc2c8f8a0f624cb4ba593a6ba589f33870c6fabcefda3e3", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "3", "matched_aliases": ["three"], "query_id": "test20", "question_hash": "e1b293062aec9cc2a87cffa66495e5d8ae61d131c8aca07deef04e67c7a4ab87", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "23c3807cd47e80d3f391275e869257eb0b5947c5050723326a0929458671d948", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 601351570, "similarity": 0.11068702290076336, "source_content_hash": "fe50735efffaa58fb3344c118e469eca8be09f08048966ca00e299a26251c1ec", "source_hash": "7f4dd83ee7511f027c56c3c7d0f00ca0921187cca69fe886dd981a2f2a29b7ec", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "16c848fc8f44574e3b593ef261ac0682591da1f57c34eabb30fec01f331313d2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc658", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Sharecropping is a form of agriculture in which a landowner allows a tenant to use the land in return for a share of the crops produced on their portion of land. Sharecropping has a long history and there are a wide range of different situations and types of agreements that have used a form of the system. Some are governed by tradition, and others by law. Legal contract systems such as the Italian mezzadria, the French métayage, the Spanish mediero, or the Islamic system of muqasat, occur widely.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1216566416, "similarity": 0.9833169774288518, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7f78fcc938d5912fd5600fab61325a7800702461afbf13d58c2174ee3cd5e71f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Sharecropping", "matched_aliases": ["Sharecropping"], "query_id": "test24", "question_hash": "559e3e55e17f697187dfc2762aa2faa49716c78a0bf925c0e9718c60eee9a217", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "afce9045bbd8902c2cb3b9b02da782a79b33a7f60ecd269469e258bb4fface3d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1102968560, "similarity": 0.20437956204379562, "source_content_hash": "31a32716fb0b0a8997fb782607732b5c46a308064acf701983d8bab0df9c1e76", "source_hash": "0fbcc4c279c1cfde5b8ea76e8e1ba515b612219534063d7480732caff7e4efdb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a146d0c11b5afd58008f4be683e50f7ffc57a31fe7a216b3e1c75487b2d48747", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answe