{"doc_id": "doc2254", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The music to \"Man Gave Names to All the Animals\" is reggae-inspired. The lyrics were inspired by the biblical Book of Genesis, verses 2:19–20 in which Adam named the animals and birds. The lyrics have an appeal to children, rhyming the name of the animal with one of its characteristics. So after describing an animal's \"muddy trail\" and \"curly tail,\" Dylan sings that \"he wasn't too small and he wasn't too big\" and so that animal was named a pig. Similarly, the cow got its name because Adam \"saw milk comin' out but he didn't know how\" and the bear got its name because it has a \"great big furry back and furry hair.\"", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1120216972, "similarity": 0.9825396825396825, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f39bf19be17e723ebc68b01bf3220370e7fc86fa8cfed29a56244962ba740d46", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Adam", "matched_aliases": ["Adam"], "query_id": "test74", "question_hash": "45c100d853b49a2bdd52a19e2b4e10cd832c5dd86969f5e81dd558872e21efb5", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3dbce71f922c4998bc1f9e3d9d090c68232fa2f7259b9f73cbc92daef87ce6a0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1607803534, "similarity": 0.09771986970684039, "source_content_hash": "acb2cb95dd7e6ee151463afb1b4e94e100449d7ed376b89bd472e37fea4b268b", "source_hash": "8df179115090bf92a4b121d76db24d85edcf7c6293bf761debb31b67b324885c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "082e7255612552d16b33b0a5c72776a3856b7128c0a59985276b894b4d3af8c1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2262", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "After a player has been designated for assignment, the other 30 NHL teams can put in a claim or waive their claim for that player. The claims process starts at noon Eastern Time and ends 24 hours later. If only one team makes a claim for the player, then he will be transferred to the claiming team. If more than one team makes a claim, then the player will be transferred to the team having the lowest percentage of possible points in league standings at the time of the request for waivers. When a waiver claim has been secured, the claiming team must pay a transfer fee to the original club, though this fee is not counted against the salary cap. If waivers are requested outside the playing season, or before November 1, then the player shall be transferred to the team with the lowest points in the preceding season.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1927096233, "similarity": 0.9524361948955916, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "During the NHL waiver process, designated players face a 24-hour window to be claimed by other teams. This timeframe begins at noon Eastern Time and concludes the next day. If a single team successfully claims the player, they are awarded his rights; however, if multiple teams compete, the transfer goes to the team with the lowest projected points in the league standings. Once a claim is secured, the claiming team must pay a transfer fee to the original club, which does not impact the salary cap. It is important to note that if waivers are requested outside the playing season or before November 1, the player is transferred to the team with the lowest points from the previous season.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1506438351, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "2b4c03351fb393689874ac6dd0fd5db21210a4335e44a5084bfbb10cc3f5b4d1", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "24 hours", "matched_aliases": ["24 hours"], "query_id": "test75", "question_hash": "a9715bf40246e75d11fd429e8f941f97a9ad9cb607ef4fc7855ec32698c663ad", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "28b7e49cfcf685c9c4e91ab50dfcb6c10c6891a20388633c7c79bc4a3dcd6bd1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 982662704, "similarity": 0.880292733925771, "source_content_hash": "0c71a1861c3f5151500db17d1cd2e0843614fd11f0bcc71df528f0825c76fb8e", "source_hash": "5b818bca9810076a4e963e2e29cf72f3ab1b1234c770073fb4291710a76e5a9c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "081f10cbd4226e7d08321083ecbe08126fef26ca63d440b91fc3bd7751263164", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
