{"doc_id": "doc2319", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Thespis was a singer of dithyrambs (songs about stories from mythology with choric refrains). He is credited with introducing a new style in which one singer or actor performed the words of individual characters in the stories, distinguishing between the characters with the aid of different masks.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2074211631, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e19fbdee66e671b5bccf9b0b961fb59722db92827183baf6e5e9e11ce202d95d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Thespis", "matched_aliases": ["Thespis"], "query_id": "test77", "question_hash": "6d62c20a8660fa2984701d3d2366e0fc665a429e4b48b4d12f20809b40ad2c6a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "10f6dfc6295e7d30f14b6c4b3b88599f5f518ffb426a8eedae5d340cd1e442cf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 889481590, "similarity": 0.03183791606367583, "source_content_hash": "14540dadc67a1e5cf58edadcefb0668b35540b7f2d928dafd16c22291e941da2", "source_hash": "834408d607ba85dd000f48dc67be8153fc52b8a892e35e50cf9a35ce94470a75", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bfd9de226cafe01a42ad2cdc4691a889684002d361cf4849e2c5c16ee56c53da", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2368", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"I Wan'na Be like You\" is a song from Walt Disney's 1967 film The Jungle Book. The song was written by songwriters Robert and Richard Sherman and was performed by Louis Prima.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 6803750, "similarity": 0.9915014164305949, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9be87083008a7984a3aab412c2834453d434f694e2a3dcd581da762d804e5826", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Louis Prima", "matched_aliases": ["Louis Prima"], "query_id": "test79", "question_hash": "088bc6ab9a017be2421375bd593f6b512f9ca3508ff8994cd73be7336860d657", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e9d8af551bbbddb9b9c7ef31fffab66580c5abfbcb20995dd90d5316556982cf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 338225899, "similarity": 0.8228882833787466, "source_content_hash": "73955d7684c622de2075a70e2db7e7d7f9a7f68588e636a0d3b0108d9e4a1c84", "source_hash": "407f344d1cd6f90311e97db8c8668162dcd8630209d177f2f4c36c649ce6066a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "63b5d74db361d05f484098b9254354a4ca881a71c8433a92ca39bf6fbaaff6e0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2604", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On Founder's Day, Anna gives Jeremy a vial of her blood, telling him that if he drinks it he will die and become a vampire. She goes to the remaining tomb vampires, then reveals their plans to Damon, possibly to protect Jeremy. Damon warns her about the device; she is protecting Jeremy when John Gilbert sets it off, and was immediately incapacitated. A policeman finds her with Jeremy, injects her with vervain and takes her to the Gilbert building to be burned with other vampires, repeating the 1864 plan to eradicate their kind. When John Gilbert sees Anna lying in the building with the other vampires, he stakes her; her body is burned with the others. Damon sees this and later tells Jeremy how Anna died, regretting that he wasn't able to help. Jeremy questions whether it would be better to be a vampire and Damon admits it would be easier to turn the emotions off. Later, Jeremy drinks Anna's blood and takes all of Elena's sleeping pills.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 428063239, "similarity": 0.9973725696269049, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "On Founder's Day, Anna gives Jeremy a vial of her blood, telling him that if he drinks it he will die and become a vampire. She then goes to the remaining tomb vampires, where she reveals their plans to Damon, possibly to protect Jeremy. Damon warns her about the device; she is protecting Jeremy when John Gilbert sets it off, and was immediately incapacitated. A policeman finds her with Jeremy, injects her with vervain and takes her to the Gilbert building to be burned with other vampires, repeating the 1864 plan to eradicate their kind. When John Gilbert sees Anna lying in the building with the other vampires, he stakes her; her body is burned with the others. Damon sees this and later tells Jeremy how Anna died, regretting that he wasn't able to help. Jeremy questions whether it would be better to be a vampire and Damon admits it would be easier to turn the emotions off. Later, Jeremy drinks Anna's blood and takes all of Elena's sleeping pills.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1960221310, "similarity": 0.9576581285938317, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "d0d61e42f240d906e02c97ae8dbf5188affb55260516393ac0d4ae256fe3c78a", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "the Gilbert building", "matched_aliases": ["the Gilbert building"], "query_id": "test83", "question_hash": "d5046d88cc48ae9046c645958d9e838012af83efd5d3876bb40c17b973322498", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "086129e9ef3703ae5693a02f915c222f3438c8f571c1f9ef3d6237d807f0c513", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1190516357, "similarity": 0.22354694485842028, "source_content_hash": "5b5916cca107e139d00c4d6f87be0b6fd9de0f117c76c404e3d9823aff73cec6", "source_hash": "8fe2afcfef6299472a890028ad8c1924baf5b2da2b58a86dc71f51191fdeb223", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a94a87c6f5145e7a1d885fb511469ebbea30aaac4cb18affa1d51251399b16b0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2628", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Articles of Confederation, formally the Articles of Confederation and Perpetual Union, was an agreement among the 13 original states of the United States of America that served as its first constitution. It was approved, after much debate (between July 1776 and November 1777), by the Second Continental Congress on November 15, 1777, and sent to the states for ratification. The Articles of Confederation came into force on March 1, 1781, after being ratified by all 13 states. A guiding principle of the Articles was to preserve the independence and sovereignty of the states. The federal government received only those powers which the colonies had recognized as belonging to king and parliament.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 231101724, "similarity": 0.9957507082152974, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d0794dc4dcd87e62b3c6751109c15c5cbddc5234326a872fd324419ee31cdcff", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the states", "matched_aliases": ["the states"], "query_id": "test84", "question_hash": "751c8d9efe4acbf22233ac5daeac9b029112f164e21c7f49f2fbee087d53b87b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f2fd788a3e2130735ecb3761b9094c7adffff6f4b46fb238b7e4cb1918ea2217", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 654012370, "similarity": 0.2, "source_content_hash": "47fe41a5f1ced40d77cca9b1e21cd3422a5908a5dbfad1e87e63fd8131f1bf01", "source_hash": "4d6ca47a505867c4208c01beb30409920891e62b448509c341d8c6c2d161e9ba", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6d0755bc409359dc10a38f6ae5867b8acb85b36757232ea417ee21516878f9e6", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2735", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In 1871 A.D. Pt. Buddhiballav Pant opened a debating club. When Sir William Muir, the then provincial Governor, came here he was highly pleased with the working of this club. It is said that he also advised to open a press here and publish a newspaper. Mr. Pant, as advised, opened a press here and started publishing a weekly magazine Almora Akhbar. Almora Akhbar was the oldest Hindi weekly of this province. In 1913 A.D. Badri Datt Pandey took over the editing work of the magazine. Almora Akhbar made much progress; The number of its customers rose from 50-60 to 1500; however, it was closed in 1917. In 1918 one of the partners purchased the Debating Club Press and named it Vindhyavasini Press. From 1922 A.D. a weekly named Zila Samachar began to be published. Later on it came to be called Kumaun Kumud and was still being published till the late 30's.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 633225509, "similarity": 0.9778283115406481, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a2fd55f5ad0b71713b5b229a41b4777fe6da789188fd89a8c5fb153dffa0f5b5", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1871 A.D", "matched_aliases": ["1871 A.D", "1871"], "query_id": "test85", "question_hash": "0f06f9a6d97d0cc141875ed124020364d3d3b0e012f11797882c7853f69c8a69", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d270cb5271f22712ed5356b892ea9c3da2f22c2474f7edffb6c6dc65025a8b20", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 899489191, "similarity": 0.162203519510329, "source_content_hash": "c06a4a3eaa8d5cba15dc4b70f4d0fd193e88b6ed57cf6bcc100126dde9ba5e2e", "source_hash": "9e58b613f983588fbb6a59298e1092dc255b07b0e1bdf85aefc0dd9635883bb0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b919a0731b590bd0ac945c693155e3150eca2c6b47c3b52ad45d94e616e75342", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2746", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The New England Patriots have appeared in the Super Bowl ten times in franchise history, the most of any team, eight of them since the arrival of head coach Bill Belichick and quarterback Tom Brady in 2000. The Patriots have since become one of the most successful teams in NFL history, winning 15 AFC East titles in 17 seasons since 2001, without a losing season in that period. The franchise has since set numerous notable records, including most wins in a ten-year period (126, in 2003–2012), an undefeated 16-game regular season in 2007, the longest winning streak consisting of regular season and playoff games in NFL history (a 21-game streak from October 2003 to October 2004), and the most consecutive division titles won by a team in NFL history (won nine straight division titles from 2009 to 2017). The team owns the record for most Super Bowls reached (eight) and won (five) by a head coach–quarterback tandem. Currently, the team is tied with the 49ers and Cowboys for the second most Super Bowl wins with five, after the Steelers, who have six.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1399354758, "similarity": 0.9942965779467681, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "cd281310d801be14843243f71d35058774da918d2dd221a7bd94378d47782300", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "10", "matched_aliases": ["ten", "ten times"], "query_id": "test86", "question_hash": "e6b78a3c0457f83ec1792b2ef0d5175e31bcd7c848fac594bea41130969178fa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c7d32e51d62ae21025172ab30a565ae66a4ebcaa4e5ac064f2f308fb97398098", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2017652174, "similarity": 0.6494392979034618, "source_content_hash": "ac9c678e1abc970cb96c2ca6819822d92a13def6126573c150d5a7dedbd6d050", "source_hash": "21f07a18cefcab95ab992edcbbfa602d678fa73c85dc355da7b5da8ce716ac89", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "72a8d326cbad35d8eb0a3d99e0ef2ef884851756d89ddd84785b73d41520c1eb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
