{"doc_id": "doc2892", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "8cbda9c054f9d2bb02cf0f2ca550f71bc5bea131fb839ca6d885c5c812cd4b9f", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "an edible tuber", "matched_aliases": ["an edible tuber"], "query_id": "test89", "question_hash": "1be9d5c529862ed64f8df62043ccd698f7412bbb79bf5ec47aa046d7104dd920", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "658fe482d6f0e436958b5173466e85da3743e7b4faac408dbee81bbcbfea269c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1167669345, "similarity": 0.27631578947368424, "source_content_hash": "3ad0a66d36e75f0847f266acd49ec7466a4404943510ff36a9395d8aba4a6ab5", "source_hash": "9e941425f2284e8f46bdcbb9de386862f0f6dd697d436032bb7ac728c7714834", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a709d8b80665e03d68244473aa56659dfb815db7b04bc440825e6c4f51145606", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc2961", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Balaam sends back word that he can only do what YHWH commands, and God has, via a nocturnal dream, told him not to go. Balak consequently sends higher-ranking priests and offers Balaam honours; Balaam continues to press God, and God finally permits him to go but with instructions to say only what he commands. Balaam then sets out in the morning with the princes of Moab. God becomes angry that he went, and sends the Angel of the Lord (Numbers 22:22) to prevent him. At first, the angel is seen only by the donkey Balaam is riding, which tries to avoid the angel. After Balaam starts punishing the donkey for refusing to move, it is miraculously given the power to speak to Balaam (Numbers 22:28), and it complains about Balaam's treatment. At this point, Balaam is allowed to see the angel, who informs him that the donkey is the only reason the angel did not kill Balaam. Balaam immediately repents, but is told to go on.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1410560112, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Balaam, a figure from the biblical narrative, receives a clear directive from YHWH to refrain from traveling, a command communicated through a dream. Despite Balak's attempts to hire higher priests and offer Balaam honors, God ultimately permits the journey only after Balaam agrees to speak only what is commanded. Upon setting out in the morning with the princes of Moab, God becomes enraged at the incursion and dispatches the Angel of the Lord (Numbers 22:22) to stop him. Initially, the angel is perceived solely by the donkey, which attempts to evade the divine messenger. When Balaam begins to punish the animal for its refusal to move, the donkey miraculously gains the power to speak, expressing its distress over Balaam's mistreatment. At this critical juncture, Balaam is permitted to encounter the angel, who explains that the donkey was the sole reason the angel spared Balaam's life. Consequently, Balaam repents but is instructed to continue his journey.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1633686052, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "f2ba94dc6a9f7ac198366954b8db199263df107c23ce8685d03486f09f537a71", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Numbers 22:28", "matched_aliases": ["Numbers 22:28"], "query_id": "test90", "question_hash": "1911bfaae8abf9c5c5bb55b881d1ca74beeadd529e5fd0dc44b782b130c52361", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f0a680e904bb7ca0547ed623124bfec613d96ebf7e3be77a2a688bb61706f3c1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 810915052, "similarity": 0.0395738203957382, "source_content_hash": "113bcd32773704d2703b940043dbdaede343b478373305fa4516ca79b56561e8", "source_hash": "a5ded3a20889638f3a173b5682da51fda92cdfd039bff4b933ea56bc387e9b94", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "031dfebf5c30d3e08d173f6d805b6a47f0e5db2dfd27270fe18f569e00c08b26", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
