{"doc_id": "doc6514", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In 1664, an English naval expedition ordered by Prince James, Duke of York and of Albany (later King James II & VII) sailed in the harbor at New Amsterdam, threatening to attack. Being greatly outnumbered, Director-General Peter Stuyvesant surrendered after negotiating favorable articles of capitulation. The Province then took a new name, New York (from James's English title). Fort Orange was renamed Fort Albany (from James's Scottish title). The region between the lower Hudson and the Delaware was deeded to proprietors and called New Jersey.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 852501347, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b6673e2733461752eca815ac4f3ece0ca693f5874151f1522bc5e92abbbd8f4b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "England", "matched_aliases": ["English"], "query_id": "test178", "question_hash": "19c2110426fe2b54b8a969f940f932b81c8b3e02fdf97ee486285bac6d83c062", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "93a2641250845d56fb83f914b433504837843db590654291b920de6f89283b8e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1556621153, "similarity": 0.10223642172523961, "source_content_hash": "1ce3a2140bc0556f7c4f786d504f94e2730b5bb8bcf087d7cc67e36bad8f5cb1", "source_hash": "bf950d30408d7c2d6cf6badca4109e61df1a109fc708be2fb066cff65bbc2bd2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c122a0f453cca30edd30563d9eb3098dd452b3457e7647f5d85476d85aa34dac", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6516", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "From 1673 to 1674, the territories were once again briefly captured by the Dutch in the Third Anglo–Dutch War, only to be returned to England at the Treaty of Westminster. In 1674, Dutch navy captain Jurriaen Aernoutsz also briefly captured two forts in the French colony of Acadia, which he claimed as Dutch territory the new colony of New Holland. However, Aernoutsz's appointed administrator, John Rhoades, quickly lost control of the territory after Aernoutsz himself left for Curaçao to seek out new settlers, and with effective control of Acadia remaining in the hands of France, Dutch sovereignty existed only on paper until the Netherlands surrendered their claim in the Treaties of Nijmegen.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1581084663, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e644dc2850c77bf98e1ba2cae670e5028a20f3af6f5cf8bec96f715b61088f12", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "England", "matched_aliases": ["England"], "query_id": "test178", "question_hash": "19c2110426fe2b54b8a969f940f932b81c8b3e02fdf97ee486285bac6d83c062", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b3cdc7c36aa9bc93ac29ca7555e1b1f0af69e960913548da2450f3c462296711", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 532436011, "similarity": 0.09946442234123948, "source_content_hash": "cad1ab28d2d24627287afa3818a1def97345e900114e6a485d041a24896b6bb5", "source_hash": "43fd767ea9dff24da903d327bcca532bd77338db4f25c6e4d811bba507fb8103", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3014518c7138f4b1ea68a0eb2eae6754a4af395ffb98c9e09b0e2ceaf6257f29", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6531", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Article Two of the United States Constitution establishes the executive branch of the federal government, which carries out and enforces federal laws. The executive branch includes the President, the Vice President, the Cabinet, executive departments, independent agencies, and other boards, commissions, and committees.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1118903789, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "8fbf7fb3dfa40361ee2b790d5a33f81bf39b425e891fa9a75c3c813fb9925501", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Article Two", "matched_aliases": ["Article Two"], "query_id": "test179", "question_hash": "91d3f8df2312abe90d1af282eb40ca7ae6ce4760e5e819c7ac9807fbc7b512b5", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "69ea80e5eda1bf3de78e88c59b42e77cc69670e6baed69b3399b54171252e23d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2013529516, "similarity": 0.5760709010339734, "source_content_hash": "9082a899279e9cb207d68332e55b5c41240c0edcdc0a9ec19b1bbb8597d6a301", "source_hash": "8ec3ceb23f1a7eb7f86c01e41674e0e1bdbe1fdb2690d7c0710fad89b5397547", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b3afa11eb8d6eeefa751ec6be0959354589ed7285b7861c6984b24ed9f480ecb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6608", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "8802e2c08758e5dcd050e7253b1ecc852fde11204b5dbff448bc2c288caf2aaa", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "2018", "matched_aliases": ["2018"], "query_id": "test180", "question_hash": "03a189b0e767f9fb10f626d2503a26980dbb955a621fd8600543079c8130e608", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "52b9a72ce90c6b99b39fc7e8053f71acab12f9a40995dce7126622e82bba0b15", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 435287227, "similarity": 0.48695652173913045, "source_content_hash": "c974aa01128291dbdde417e12a0e4ac28c7a252991c190b30511e1724151c119", "source_hash": "f862b2a5cf72ea32954239830c816cb16442b54a598626ed0b90491ffd7a4478", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0a544e19a4d69de2cdcd7e4b3c8c686a4736ae1ec6354b839fe7ecdc2b8f70b8", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6649", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "While the phrase is commonly attributed to Queen Marie Antoinette,[1] there is no record of her having said it. It appears in book six of Jean-Jacques Rousseau's Confessions, his autobiography (whose first six books were written in 1765, when Marie Antoinette was nine years of age, and published in 1782). The context of Rousseau's account was his desire to have some bread to accompany some wine he had stolen; however, feeling he was too elegantly dressed to go into an ordinary bakery, he recollected the words of a \"great princess\":[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1341136969, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "940486fa525d1c6b3a20ef2d1fa42a0ed6a38ca976f03605cba8dfec34b5f7dc", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Jean-Jacques Rousseau", "matched_aliases": ["Jean-Jacques Rousseau"], "query_id": "test182", "question_hash": "354dbadbf2e622f83c424263b8e9e586cb637eded1c0e8bffcfabd59a940f1f6", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5f4ed1b107eeb8419c9516d396cbf467820c7b743135cb3c08ca036b1075b3e4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 545603772, "similarity": 0.3421828908554572, "source_content_hash": "384769500c2db73bf70ee76b9513f2b31a5b7df1857b2832e65231acda75cf48", "source_hash": "6016d4cabdc8b8fa6b6fa440999d31f19d8ab5da52981a4d5e8302a07deaac8b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b5e1b1283189d39db557bba683dc710dea4d8d2f064904842b74f3b2b44a221e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6672", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the developing B cell, the first recombination event to occur is between one D and one J gene segment of the heavy chain locus. Any DNA between these two gene segments is deleted. This D-J recombination is followed by the joining of one V gene segment, from a region upstream of the newly formed DJ complex, forming a rearranged VDJ gene segment. All other gene segments between V and D segments are now deleted from the cell's genome. Primary transcript (unspliced RNA) is generated containing the VDJ region of the heavy chain and both the constant mu and delta chains (Cμ and Cδ). (i.e. the primary transcript contains the segments: V-D-J-Cμ-Cδ). The primary RNA is processed to add a polyadenylated (poly-A) tail after the Cμ chain and to remove sequence between the VDJ segment and this constant gene segment. Translation of this mRNA leads to the production of the Ig M heavy chain protein.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 170871156, "similarity": 0.9988876529477196, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "883d6122ddd64e1ff21f72ae9d21db8321ee497af17f0143a9eb69c191f2930c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "V", "matched_aliases": ["V"], "query_id": "test183", "question_hash": "2556e479a7d3a163883530010aaa3a7b7e7bed2367ac239fec572bea60647ffa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "551d19629b244ff0ce36ee29808e264ebcc8c5e6207acdcf859715dc3649135f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 881583084, "similarity": 0.31685393258426964, "source_content_hash": "15bc924917c6f271286a3da358334fcba4c12048c7434162c67a947589a1eb68", "source_hash": "22d19220bf32cffd2c7987cca8b5e7738b484af5a352a165af876808fd8affd1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "fd214b8edd07b77db6c8bb9f989873aadf5345850ec2845ef08c5d5bc28eebff", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc6686", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The current territories of Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Maldives, Nepal, India, Pakistan, and Sri Lanka form South Asia. The South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC) is an economic cooperation organisation in the region which was established in 1985 and includes all eight nations comprising South Asia.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 944550806, "similarity": 0.99079754601227, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9a2e1a3ae7e6e75a89757cc1bbddfed83dfb908279f9a2d0616cf652f2bd058e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "South Asia", "matched_aliases": ["South Asia"], "query_id": "test184", "question_hash": "0707078de8864bbb243d5187b20508d062335cca581bd6ddcded6f2be71ee0d4", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5019c444f5cb41ca36941bc7b43b251426c558e68e67a07b24f8119868c79820", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 699577689, "similarity": 0.3828016643550624, "source_content_hash": "625f32505777eabad980a7371fef800e9c82657bfb4865d3048187399c988ede", "source_hash": "b65b916e4b1e4d0bee4090260e9f66d1bee17c4105d2f66b3365e91cd14112c5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "991fec99ebe119bc3f138ef78b60ac22e89f3c7db76a96722d04bbb087d3b2af", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
