{"doc_id": "doc7351", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The fifth Volume premiered on October 14, 2017, a date which was first announced at the RTX Austin 2017 event. The episodes are released to Rooster Teeth FIRST members Saturdays at 10am CT, then to Rooster Teeth registered members the following Tuesday, and to the general public the following Saturday.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 709623937, "similarity": 0.9869706840390879, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "fc7913d76ac72139ca080abd69b7ea08849f45b62e0cba9fc76a5f1c79c8d5aa", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "October 14, 2017", "matched_aliases": ["October 14, 2017"], "query_id": "test201", "question_hash": "ea529072f61288ef99a9bc0785fe8614f1f7e821f78caafd1c06c0cf4f4babc2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "edea91e41b1d5f42c43e070cd647f31a7c1cd3470f83d808fa83638defccfdc0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 463995005, "similarity": 0.9259259259259259, "source_content_hash": "c0e1e8195ef35944f1d16a0bb915cbc39d0ffffbee43d40a8a81053e3d8d78a6", "source_hash": "9cf00264bb1fa6b249a6bb2db10d172237b1e0e75c9eeae65d2e707ba13000e2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "69e23c2ef2f7099fd832e49116be419f0efc566182f7c36678b36b692494cd77", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc7389", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas\n\nBruno is a 9-year-old boy growing up during World War II in Berlin. He lives with his parents, his 12-year-old sister Gretel and maids, one of whom is called Maria. After a visit by Adolf Hitler, Bruno's father is promoted to Commandant, and the family has to move to \"Out-With\" because of the orders of \"The Fury\" (Bruno's naïve interpretation of the word 'Führer'). Bruno is initially upset about moving to Out-With (in actuality, Auschwitz)[4] and leaving his friends, Daniel, Karl, and Martin. From the house at Out-With, Bruno sees a camp in which the prisoners wear striped pyjamas. One day, Bruno decides to explore the strange wire fence. As he walks along the fence, he meets a Jewish boy named Shmuel, who he learns shares his birthday. Shmuel says that his father, grandfather, and brother are with him on this side of the fence, but he is separated from his mother. Bruno and Shmuel talk and become very good friends, although Bruno still does not understand very much about Shmuel and his side of the fence. Nearly every day, unless it's raining, Bruno goes to see Shmuel and sneaks him food. As the meetings go on, and Shmuel gets more and more skinny, Bruno's naïveté means he never realizes he is living beside a death camp.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1744409802, "similarity": 0.9872611464968153, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5a6062c8c517aff2b5576d883a4c8b6cae37dcb6ca8f7342904df674a8adbee6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "World War II", "matched_aliases": ["World War II"], "query_id": "test204", "question_hash": "4960d180cc03a8e35109bd7af78832f0da3b8a8caa28aa20e5862e11fbb77160", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "41b391e638fea233569d8c60fa5f9c04bc49759f5b2771bf34d1ccf7774a2d97", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 273231608, "similarity": 0.02787769784172662, "source_content_hash": "04d2a105e0f0fe8645f1d42bc7f30d49104909abcc5077b17a3fa1e6d17a23bf", "source_hash": "f73350a99334f94d60c784859aa5eafd608ac34293f4da330163e1b92a28768c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "517aa1f0b0ceace98730592ed51fdc48b88b6b46ae944c5918f7bfdea6c79898", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc7543", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"What Child Is This?\" is a Christmas carol whose lyrics were written by William Chatterton Dix, in 1865. At the time of composing the carol, Dix worked as an insurance company manager and had been struck by a severe illness. While recovering, he underwent a spiritual renewal that led him to write several hymns, including lyrics to this carol that was subsequently set to the tune of \"Greensleeves\", a traditional English folk song. Although it was written in Great Britain, the carol is more popular in the United States than in its country of origin today.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1787283911, "similarity": 0.9973238180196253, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "3bc22d7479883c03c1f67f5d27b273da660d7f2cbf23e4968e00262d7d297839", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "William Chatterton Dix", "matched_aliases": ["William Chatterton Dix"], "query_id": "test208", "question_hash": "1e5a3a959b8d31d303511c1073d340376dcf0b7621ec6113d65893b6abdd40c3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f49aecb82b3531c13730121929b5c94e820c8e4fd26c6094c2b67f136b0b3ea4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1693871627, "similarity": 0.04783599088838269, "source_content_hash": "c4b55d342d542cdd841faf04a3e2db400a913b5bab8d61b95ee5f117f94b88ef", "source_hash": "40e0f52720609de00728111774bd6160a0e6ce2c5cef1a94136efa6983fae864", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b8ea82079d6d817069b749ea6406434be03899415c79a0929fd9e0e5fe1233d8", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8f