{"doc_id": "doc10019", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The economy of the Ming dynasty (1368–1644) of China was the largest in the world during that period. It is regarded as one of China's three golden ages (the other two being the Han and Song periods). The period was marked by the increasing political influence of the merchants, the gradual weakening of imperial rule, and technological advances.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1432327585, "similarity": 0.9942363112391931, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Ming dynasty (1368–1644) represents a significant era in Chinese history, as it was the largest economy in the world during that time. This period is often cited as one of China's three golden ages, alongside the earlier Han and Song dynasties. A key feature of this era was the growing political sway of merchants and the accompanying gradual decline in imperial authority, alongside notable technological advancements.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1665706506, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "2c32f098458cba466124ec8eb085ebf4ee51633690bd45bf2c93bf9634ae95fd", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "imperial rule", "matched_aliases": ["imperial rule"], "query_id": "test269", "question_hash": "e717a9783b40071a8f5d9b77fc4f3e648e9be2423d8f3cd3b35757e3ae5ae6a2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b7f12cb0f1b00224a513077f741b0cb31457234b8792007c883aa0f6e6c22ee0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1471482801, "similarity": 0.2819843342036554, "source_content_hash": "da68d76324ce48e52ada29adbd776c3f23c181fcea06bcab29b2740b1998c993", "source_hash": "37253a9c1b9a9a3c3ba9980ec596abde610a8bcbc6f497c03402533128ccaeca", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4c69df51f0c8ecea9c08885b2b26c5e6e630813c714f3c9b72e9