{"doc_id": "doc10703", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Hurricane Charley was the third named storm, the second hurricane, and the second major hurricane of the 2004 Atlantic hurricane season. Charley lasted from August 9 to August 15, and at its peak intensity it attained 150 mph (240 km/h) winds, making it a strong Category 4 hurricane on the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Scale. It made landfall in southwestern Florida at maximum strength, making it the strongest hurricane to hit the United States since Hurricane Andrew struck Florida in 1992.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1223625907, "similarity": 0.9938775510204082, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "428a524196d7b5d6657c94ccaee15a912d538825b38473557d149a457240d517", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "4", "matched_aliases": ["4", "Category 4"], "query_id": "test283", "question_hash": "14bd37b97eacd65a63d2d2abeb9ae423924166494b8623f4b54c63809b95d309", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "46843993d1859ff7bdadbf765fee234ce6274f60131da862534181b7e07c0925", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 3395973, "similarity": 0.3114754098360656, "source_content_hash": "9b4d3c23d6a9b1fc32e9b331b5a685dd3559d1ac10e6f7eca3d8467f7c448c22", "source_hash": "69b1a400f890857bfb3f4e46930116bd77ea77f9eb90d96a6ebd8d18cc07fbfb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "91d527291ec7fae49e258afbed022f183798703182d13d718717d8b54ac518fc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10708", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "76d1dbe7f537a9627df2292c0d12b776006b0e7e07de83cb49c0b6d16ddc007c", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "4", "matched_aliases": ["4", "Category 4"], "query_id": "test283", "question_hash": "14bd37b97eacd65a63d2d2abeb9ae423924166494b8623f4b54c63809b95d309", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ffe48d1dc038104351643bb811e6ca62d7bac0562b807009168124b07b4b1fdc", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1513426051, "similarity": 0.6258565555047967, "source_content_hash": "006ddcc0b0a9b7705a2d289b328fdfbc1e13945e78d9bcc0ebe15cd805d7a225", "source_hash": "1f0cede19ca98f8dc3b0b3461b061679d89b74f8c87ec1b55ca0a4d340c8f8ce", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b30987dc96ea2406a3db9f7c0771bba30d14767bf9f0406b25c54e53f828660e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10834", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The starting five from each conference consists of three frontcourt players and two guards, selected by a combination of fan, player, and media voting. In 2017, the NBA moved from a pure fan vote to a weighted process wherein fan voting accounts for 50% of the total and player and media voting account for 25% each. The league made the change in response to social media campaigns that resulted in mediocre players such as journeyman Zaza Pachulia nearly being voted as All-Star starters over more deserving players. Prior to 2013, fans selected two forwards and one center instead of generic frontcourt players. The NBA in 2003 began offering All-Star ballots in three languages—English, Spanish and Chinese—for fan voting of the starters.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 760559333, "similarity": 0.988, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The All-Star Game is a prominent basketball event where the starting lineup is chosen through a voting process involving fans, players, and media. While the league initially allowed fans to select two forwards and one center, this system was modified in 2017 to include player and media contributions, with fan votes now accounting for half of the total selection. Consequently, the answer to who holds the most votes for the All-Star Game is determined by a combination of these three groups, with specific percentages assigned to each based on the voting method used.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1883320254, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "cb9227ab7a406080746b5536e52e0cf826f9427250147da79b6b75136a84a419", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "fan voting", "matched_aliases": ["fan voting"], "query_id": "test286", "question_hash": "9848d4a1f537027484d7ca3a389b8be5fb37e569ca7c485e82c5c33b0fcabdc9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d320df02ba64540220d9a794c470487d5656e6199917624d4fa16f0a5784ea65", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1607383090, "similarity": 0.3117338003502627, "source_content_hash": "80d542857c4ab3bcba49b61d5bb7ba0954dcea5540ee508e8db45ffb5d8339a9", "source_hash": "74fca5a82020f55b34c1fe5f16904baede59c0a4fb881f1a2c3caf78a735fd0e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7a52f1894ac1a787421b1dacf05e35a790c30b130fdef0376df93f122188ea1c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10875", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Mad Max is a 1979 Australian dystopian action film directed by George Miller, produced by Byron Kennedy, and starring Mel Gibson as \"Mad\" Max Rockatansky, Joanne Samuel, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, and Roger Ward. James McCausland and Miller wrote the screenplay from a story by Miller and Kennedy. The film presents a tale of societal collapse, murder, and revenge set in a future Australia, in which an unhinged policeman becomes embroiled in a violent feud with a savage motorcycle gang. Principal photography took place in and around Melbourne, Australia, and lasted six weeks.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2047145004, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "dbc8986eee9d162ea8760a044e8de6243114e2389979706d222ef5a1e91597d4", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "12 April 1979", "matched_aliases": ["1979"], "query_id": "test289", "question_hash": "89c0833d30905cbd56397fcd33d0c4cd322404e6328e62b496638eec4c482beb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "33039ade16bdaa0891348ee018d6f2cda3cce536b27016fd558619618a63d8e6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 577381182, "similarity": 0.41168996188055906, "source_content_hash": "d4e3fc36debdf95b47397c788febd40e541df3d7c0ff2ddc098f98e250748721", "source_hash": "d94582aaa78986e16babe96164ded0d3550fb3f1a22e11e92bc0299cb9e1dfca", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b315c11e207476196f24323c4ca0f5beb6cb7af37598c776d672be58d4f9c8f7", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10876", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The film initially received a polarized reception upon its release in April 1979, although it won three AACTA Awards and attracted a cult following, while its critical reputation has grown since. The film earned more than US$100 million worldwide in gross revenue. It held the Guinness record for most profitable film and has been credited for further opening up the global market to Australian New Wave films. The film became the first in the Mad Max series, giving rise to three sequels, Mad Max 2 (1981), Beyond Thunderdome (1985), and Fury Road (2015).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1824540696, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "dd98bd54572ea953fc24617e9540e4dbdfc4cc56bdf239547009e43d2d46c0bb", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "12 April 1979", "matched_aliases": ["April 1979", "1979"], "query_id": "test289", "question_hash": "89c0833d30905cbd56397fcd33d0c4cd322404e6328e62b496638eec4c482beb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "cd22190e4ab0ec76246838109b429a408faf092437009eec4f7dd2921cc9a723", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 644493434, "similarity": 0.6172839506172839, "source_content_hash": "a9c351b94594cdb2d196a51199df27e0ca3c0c8b0e168d02cb4b9b8e1a2ce641", "source_hash": "d11696e543d7aac4cad7aae3b9e45ef5b822b6abffc22cd97e7f1b9ef2a53cf6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "17f9581247dad097bf88aa33b518f2eeb036ef50fa78778bba5d94aad55f2aab", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10945", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Sympathetic nervous system stimulation causes vasoconstriction of most blood vessels, including many of those in the skin, the digestive tract, and the kidneys. This occurs as a result of activation of alpha-1 adrenergic receptors by norepinephrine released by post-ganglionic sympathetic neurons. These receptors exist throughout the vasculature of the body but are inhibited and counterbalanced by beta-2 adrenergic receptors (stimulated by epinephrine release from the adrenal glands) in the skeletal muscles, the heart, the lungs, and the brain during a sympathoadrenal response. The net effect of this is a shunting of blood away from the organs not necessary to the immediate survival of the organism and an increase in blood flow to those organs involved in intense physical activity.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1989579874, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ea0919b4273823053d6e66bc6368e7fd93ff412a1c886ab1a5d6a3ad9a99308c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "epinephrine", "matched_aliases": ["epinephrine"], "query_id": "test291", "question_hash": "d9f249e53e111b39e5cf2d9a25199aaefac738a59cc1c8561ca4ebcb036c4460", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4fde579ac4c39212065bb19e34347fb708089339a115e666067361c831554e4c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 227483057, "similarity": 0.20760233918128654, "source_content_hash": "e55c7cbbe6bcca85d26cd4dbcd98062cac2e16515b3dcf91cd3b284f33cea10e", "source_hash": "83cd5a4772142a074b39e1d43676b23d0724204708bcf5ab8697fcde699a159c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4ed512ebc1cbe849a61362e41c76d06220f0b5d3fba6bbbd459430972869af3a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc10953", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"People Are Crazy\" centralizes on the male narrator and an old man whom he meets in a bar. In the first verse, the two of them converse, which leads to the old man saying, \"God is great, beer is good / And people are crazy.\" They continue to converse throughout the second verse as well before parting ways. In the third verse, some time has passed, and the narrator reads the old man's obituary in the paper. He discovers that the now dead old man was a millionaire and \"left his fortune to / Some guy he barely knew\" (i.e., the narrator).[2] After this discovery, the narrator also declares that \"people are crazy.\" The song is in a 4/4 time signature and a moderate tempo, in the key of F major, using a main chord pattern of F–C–Dm–B♭. Currington's vocals range from B♭3 to D5.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1739676781, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6f4e700a9c43d5c3e221f96604cbdd87ba0afe12061117af7e2bcd7ae1f3869e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Currington", "matched_aliases": ["Currington"], "query_id": "test292", "question_hash": "b766fe08628ca22e3fc5789a4ab130b5819840b71cd228afa4a190fcad8c7e10", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e2d6c33d3c3909f702c0cdfac889906503db59e3acc6fc7e25ebc4e94e230a9b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1368327152, "similarity": 0.3119533527696793, "source_content_hash": "e9120637a5d586874b75e90f08e6739be9fdf43c4afe36013b57ec770739a10a", "source_hash": "94b3614ca23c644d2cb5bcdea3ab22950320fb3b9874ded5f911eb46d47fe551", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "32c77c9623975c863e09df2fc1930af3e38d9978b1eb6ef73bbdf540d47eaeba", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11105", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Islam and clothing: The Qur'an admonishes Muslim women to dress modestly and cover their breasts and genitals but it doesn't require covering the head.[3] The Qur'an explicitly states that \"O wives of the Prophet, you are not like anyone among women\"[4] and as such has separate rules specifically for the wives of the Prophet. Wearing hijab, or al-khimar, is considered by some to be obligatory in Islam[citation needed], as the quote states \"Tell the believing women to put their khimar over their bosoms\", all the major Arab translations and dictionaries agree that \"al-khimar\" means a veil or scarf that a woman uses to cover her head, and \"over their bosoms\" implies women should cover their breasts, necks etc.[citation needed]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 757765600, "similarity": 0.9861687413554634, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1817ffa1e26611d0f3ec314b7c82bb16190da494330be74a3607ff1328791090", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "hijab", "matched_aliases": ["hijab"], "query_id": "test295", "question_hash": "a214305bcae417e84a8abb0d6892df66eb235a4258011d5b6d4b6d525e015316", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "54fd4b9d1b77082e9ffaa0f1a5bc4ec730508c0b02812189174286125a23c2c8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 932613981, "similarity": 0.14948859166011014, "source_content_hash": "9b5c25783b24eec347fb842ae8313c765efb11e382fade54e21da214d8a79ee4", "source_hash": "0badb983a4c11e250cb88ccb8f79f351a17c5562e0a1b5024b4389f772a571c5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5a2c4b4d3732963bd996d6aefbe50eb3a7e2ccb0cc8e4c70a54ebe89a324a066", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_v