{"doc_id": "doc11853", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "dfe2834e3ef4de528b59fe66b39ff135ba480d3e524002e4fecc16a2004e703e", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "information", "matched_aliases": ["information"], "query_id": "test308", "question_hash": "d51d571b6a3930efea72765f9d993d7e842a35dcbaad721131cbbea72077f867", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "98be53aff26bd7b7d966bb85b9ce84b3945ec1b081634eab6272803e78b0770e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1097275976, "similarity": 0.6883852691218131, "source_content_hash": "c4b04503dad1cfa3c577cbaf480740a1bf56a5d1ef837127a963058c1aeee3a1", "source_hash": "3ecda7dcb8f72ac2549c4725a26a7421e46e4c5b9af8e4ebec764e10143e67fa", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "26512e7af214c32db75e7fde6b1fa861903d26c670013bd71d7d302a89072aa4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11854", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Content itself is what the end-user derives value from. Thus, \"content\" can refer to the information provided through the medium, the way in which the information was presented, as well as the added features included in the medium in which that information was delivered. The medium, however, provides little to no value to the end-user without the information and experiences that make up the content. Communication theory philosopher Marshall McLuhan famously coined the phrase, \"The medium is the message.\" In the case of content, the channel through which information is delivered, the \"medium\", affects how the end user perceives content, the \"message\".", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 996801649, "similarity": 0.9977255496588324, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ed1b6ec4e63d38245060197485f5f4b7108afd47604fa5e107220f94dd669cda", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "information", "matched_aliases": ["information"], "query_id": "test308", "question_hash": "d51d571b6a3930efea72765f9d993d7e842a35dcbaad721131cbbea72077f867", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "91b88911d1f28a24f105a5729e6c48925daa5ade0694c84da3ac00bb03c53091", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 753220467, "similarity": 0.042818911685994644, "source_content_hash": "02f55fe1ebe02deef62a8cd5435f3629aa33601542e04add0d197e4db4b0bf43", "source_hash": "3a9afb82bb0986b46a7b722ef64f22c846fd81be237b8cdb2ca1d715864a4a38", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "893fedf61999b2c254bb57dc8fb099df70946e1b589252616ac30e539378c29d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11864", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The two kingdoms of Upper and Lower Egypt were united c. 3000 BC, but each maintained its own regalia: the hedjet or White Crown for Upper Egypt and the deshret or Red Crown for Lower Egypt. Thus, the pharaohs were known as the rulers of the Two Lands, and wore the pschent, a double crown, each half representing sovereignty of one of the kingdoms. Ancient Egyptian tradition credited Menes, now believed to be the same as Narmer, as the king who united Upper and Lower Egypt. On the Narmer Palette the king is depicted wearing the Red Crown in one scene and the White crown in another, and thereby showing his rule over both Lands.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 262008847, "similarity": 0.9976359338061466, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2d281061cb07360a59557719f33ec418cc872a1a4470eec5af3e290a3269f494", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "3000 BC", "matched_aliases": ["3000 BC"], "query_id": "test309", "question_hash": "a9bf08faf3b17adadb4b41ddfe764b47a44c04795e56bdd7a6f9c41ae5512230", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3b3736d342027999747c2ae64ef926ba4cbd202a69578fdcf45ff3d5ae037c60", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 399267032, "similarity": 0.07428040854224698, "source_content_hash": "42c6805a93ca4ec3133b99eeae41bcfe5d108d7390f173ca147b1b7912d8d82a", "source_hash": "444ced3c687aed2327164a91e0920b8ff34298d03e5257c0da219b15621cb857", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "05274367630e82de25bde24453c47616be8fedf6b6f7ff8e921642c42f735a22", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11875", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Mercedes-Benz Stadium is a multi-purpose retractable roof stadium located in Atlanta, Georgia. This venue serves as the home of the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League (NFL) and Atlanta United FC of Major League Soccer (MLS), having replaced the adjacent Georgia Dome, the Falcons' home stadium for a quarter century from 1992 through 2016.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1311049328, "similarity": 0.9502923976608187, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "604bf6d90f52baef2afb460016222fef3a8693b13455bf55d5fa298c8a68db1e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Mercedes-Benz Stadium", "matched_aliases": ["Mercedes-Benz Stadium"], "query_id": "test310", "question_hash": "0a9ca38b272d7f31e45dfe7db87288f63b240b31cc05a4bd45297e6dd5a660f1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e8df9bbc6b539d55c5f212add803a9d5ee24e3583fe6a6de44535093848eabf9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 630960763, "similarity": 0.20985691573926868, "source_content_hash": "83fea496800ccd2d89dec8a6327ecdf471e8cb5ebb3ebeb9ad90aa2fb3fec4a6", "source_hash": "0bd96bfdcef030e8eb787836c282c1496e0ac6924e51ec8c420e1493e7a24b45", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c36626d77470a375233b67dad1a2bd5ddd0d0f0b13773572a2c887262143f0bd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11879", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": false, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In April 2012, Populous released a new price estimate of $947.7 million, which was significantly higher than the previous proposal of $700 million. In April 2012, The Atlanta Journal-Constitution reported that if a deal is reached, the new stadium's construction would be expected to begin in 2014, with the Falcons to begin regular-season play in 2017. The proposed location of the new stadium is a large parking lot in Atlanta's Vine City neighborhood, which is less than a mile north of the Georgia Dome's current location. Once construction is complete, the Georgia Dome would subsequently be demolished.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2112774436, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In April 2012, the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reported that if a deal is reached, the new stadium's construction would be expected to begin in 2014, with the Falcons to begin regular-season play in 2017. The proposed location of the new stadium is a large parking lot in Atlanta's Vine City neighborhood, which is less than a mile north of the Georgia Dome's current location. Once construction is complete, the Georgia Dome would subsequently be demolished.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2003805618, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "b054c13435bf33e22ef202a12dbd416b240d9be872d5bec7d672069a43902541", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Mercedes-Benz Stadium", "matched_aliases": ["Mercedes-Benz Stadium"], "query_id": "test310", "question_hash": "0a9ca38b272d7f31e45dfe7db87288f63b240b31cc05a4bd45297e6dd5a660f1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d1b256a134c031a29e5fe5ffcc65aee69353099413e8b7206b61cfdd08375c9f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 743688966, "similarity": 0.7533632286995515, "source_content_hash": "9cf4f91881887ff1