{"doc_id": "doc14321", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"My Bucket's Got a Hole in It\" is a song widely attributed to Clarence Williams, who obtained a copyright in 1933. The song became popular performed by Hank Williams for MGM and reached #4 on the country chart in 1949.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1662772683, "similarity": 0.9931662870159453, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d77a1e7e18749b0596e816164fff5177bd884f9d4537eb7673141c21c3d85430", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Hank Williams", "matched_aliases": ["Hank Williams"], "query_id": "test381", "question_hash": "896044897614f63a6821e87e035809cd2affbf2701d25e6fd1f121daf97f4d47", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d7a9e7897744a427f8102cdbef8d518a636840f2ff69ca39482d5969c7813461", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1694011138, "similarity": 0.31386861313868614, "source_content_hash": "9d0b99efd383e35b12123dff7dc67312de26f5587441226fcca821c76ef1a7b3", "source_hash": "b3c4398d46cfaa7870445a4376c1175e56d90a47f54e3373ee4bc3353d84de26", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0c2644ebe14ba33f7b6aff3325e12705470e03374159991cf6d16b5a1ef48b5e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc14343", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Ich bin ein Berliner\" (German pronunciation: [ˈʔɪç ˈbɪn ʔaɪn bɛɐ̯ˈliːnɐ], \"I am a Berliner\") is a quotation from a June 26, 1963, speech by U.S. President John F. Kennedy in West Berlin. It is widely regarded as the best-known speech of the Cold War and the most famous anti-communist speech. Kennedy aimed to underline the support of the United States for West Germany 22 months after Soviet-supported East Germany erected the Berlin Wall to prevent mass emigration to the West. The message was aimed as much at the Soviets as it was at Berliners and was a clear statement of U.S. policy in the wake of the construction of the Berlin Wall. Another phrase in the speech was also spoken in German, \"Lasst sie nach Berlin kommen\" (\"Let them come to Berlin\"), addressed at those who claimed \"we can work with the Communists\", a remark at which Nikita Khrushchev scoffed only days later.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 335383248, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a834dcd711193d1ffdd26f0f20e8a85a104fbc3d1166aca037159d943cc2b72d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "U.S. President John F. Kennedy", "matched_aliases": ["U.S. President John F. Kennedy"], "query_id": "test383", "question_hash": "46f47ecac3437bb1b35d02e058baebae2efdf9d2e8400670fc063b08079a4773", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e1b28436e28a95ec42a8ebc432379d2c2d393ffa972a76c736b510ec9ae9c58b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1760214711, "similarity": 0.0691114245416079, "source_content_hash": "291ce7692ec9260e64d90449d929af104a8126967b76e59a6384fd7eebc3530e", "source_hash": "69f70c1977721f9551542c0cf73baaa59f4d28fe5b56a63343fa586b407e2b89", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a7e8077d6f31a6bc3f89c160f2b2663d64a4c829a16104392ed20816858ab270", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc14383", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Fall of the Western Roman Empire marks the end of the last remaining Roman army in Europe. This event occurred in 476 CE, when the last Western Roman Emperor, Romulus Augustulus, was deposed by Odoacer. This deposition signaled the end of the Western Empire, as the remaining Roman military, political, and financial power had been negligible. The source text explicitly states that invading barbarians had established their own power in most of the area of the Western Empire, and that the Western Empire never had the strength to rise again.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1444762041, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Title: Fall of the Western Roman Empire\nRelevant dates include 117 CE, when the Empire was at its greatest territorial extent, and the accession of Diocletian in 284. Irreversible major territorial loss, however, began in 376 with a large-scale irruption of Goths and others. In 395, after winning two destructive civil wars, Theodosius I died, leaving a collapsing field army and the Empire, still plagued by Goths, divided between his two incapable sons. By 476 when Odoacer deposed the Emperor Romulus, the Western Roman Emperor wielded negligible military, political, or financial power and had no effective control over the scattered Western domains that could still be described as Roman. Invading barbarians had established their own power in most of the area of the Western Empire. While its legitimacy lasted for centuries longer and its cultural influence remains today, the Western Empire never had the strength to rise again.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1080820371, "similarity": 0.9781897491821155, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "0fd0a3567f736268d324433cfbc9ad3bebf2c57b242a60ccd5a9296ceb6739e8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Goths", "matched_aliases": ["Goths"], "query_id": "test385", "question_hash": "1335c2d4006ef47c56e23d940a641401a8395016a7b89044e6247f8dacc09c9c", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "86009e12d03040b0e0eb14e345449a376c790598a73f29f433dee1e5b5758d94", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1098546018, "similarity": 0.09345794392523364, "source_content_hash": "90ac8b1268573d2be7ff551cb88620482a7f2b342c5e251f390ed27e32505e07", "source_hash": "9082b3b10764670148f39761eb0e7e8357772b160b7842cb024c2edeef4eb58d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e32b18f271490d17415680f5c909c03994372ea4a648cda3eb9cf01e2c352a6d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
