{"doc_id": "doc15000", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On a surface level the poem explores a violation of nature and the resulting psychological effects on the mariner and on all those who hear him. According to Jerome McGann the poem is like a salvation story. The poem's structure is multi-layered text based on Coleridge's interest in Higher Criticism. \"Like the Iliad or Paradise Lost or any great historical product, the Rime is a work of transhistorical rather than so-called universal significance. This verbal distinction is important because it calls attention to a real one. Like The Divine Comedy or any other poem, the Rime is not valued or used always or everywhere or by everyone in the same way or for the same reasons.\"", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1270056802, "similarity": 0.9970717423133236, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "03cb4e24538ac5926bc832319f730274aaa428b7764312e379dcdc51ab609355", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "a violation of nature", "matched_aliases": ["a violation of nature"], "query_id": "test399", "question_hash": "4cf9f0dcbd1e610267a7708c79d3121a06cc545ec93169ad80642b33c228e20c", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "6ef653949d3cf66600e52449042cb461e90db0e924054e289281823b5692d73b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1792665319, "similarity": 0.0118946474086661, "source_content_hash": "870491ca13b33deb4dfaa8b147cef7b1984e5f14b78b16472356c7d8a77e7a28", "source_hash": "fde1cced886488b596cc86055efae0d9627ab438bee3f64db0a8b150c7f714d4", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b6efdf64a194fdb6c96d0cc55db7d594dfb0170b0f508ac96561ba984a4aaad3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage":