{"doc_id": "doc15016", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "17fa79ed39abc295ef5616620277706ff9ea2a13ce28b92988935f3710fc72a5", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "parthenogenesis", "matched_aliases": ["parthenogenesis"], "query_id": "test401", "question_hash": "9450d742b4f03ac18dfe627c15a2f903c74a8f516ba9ac19d6e253f7832a7c23", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8675d41f0e68558af8ffab217381203aa118bba53a1a2b5f9fa06063716b7a37", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 3832904, "similarity": 0.28594905505341, "source_content_hash": "f43e0209c672ab0eae08ac0be6eb2f4f0694139bcf7bb0d042f339da119fe7db", "source_hash": "e55a29604d8c20a5ce9b66b9b933a44895964cc9bc77cc26bf884c16af91aba6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a64a337df88bdb9fde37f19e7103acf6cfbdfdbd3a1591342d1123a82022d038", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc15047", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the late 19th century, the European imperial powers engaged in a major territorial scramble and occupied most of the continent, creating many colonial territories, and leaving only two fully independent states: Ethiopia (known to Europeans as \"Abyssinia\"), and Liberia. Egypt and Sudan were never formally incorporated into any European colonial empire; however, after the British occupation of 1882, Egypt was effectively under British administration until 1922.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 630837282, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the late 19th century, the European imperial powers engaged in a major territorial scramble and occupied most of the continent, creating many colonial territories, and leaving only two fully independent states: Ethiopia (known to Europeans as \"Abyssinia\"), and Liberia. Egypt and Sudan were never formally incorporated into any European colonial empire; however, after the British occupation of 1882, Egypt was effectively under British administration until 1922.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1602083976, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "13fecd700b6d665453c4e3c019341d567144f2554c8cad495f47f86023653dd8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "European imperial powers", "matched_aliases": ["European imperial powers"], "query_id": "test402", "question_hash": "2a938fb88809a012da67bc1ef2b9f8d7902c0a5e6b08514c2becc2536a5039d0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "dea248853b570e2d6a01938d756e1ae30dbb17fc5204ccc89227343a3b8ac7fa", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1103162910, "similarity": 0.3007518796992481, "source_content_hash": "baa83526129819736795de28b8d0edb48b075b84e0a06fb6eedab2782fae266a", "source_hash": "efa30a597b750e44fe804546bc7a765f8f1196d637fb3c6257ec