{"doc_id": "doc15659", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "At the time of the 1970 NFL–AFL merger, George Halas, head coach, founder and owner of the Chicago Bears, held the record for most wins as a head coach. He retired from coaching after the 1967 season with 324 wins, including six playoff wins. Twenty-eight years later, Halas was surpassed by Don Shula. Shula retired at the end of the 1995 season, after amassing 328 regular season wins and 19 playoff wins.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 525334213, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "At the time of the 1970 NFL–AFL merger, George Halas, head coach, founder and owner of the Chicago Bears, held the record for most wins as a head coach. He retired from coaching after the 1967 season with 324 wins, including six playoff wins. Twenty-eight years later, Halas was surpassed by Don Shula, who retired at the end of the 1995 season after amassing 328 regular season wins and 19 playoff wins.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 262327535, "similarity": 0.9839704069050554, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "c79322684b82930416ba46871b04af0470fd209dea8ccdec11065389a9299e9b", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Shula, Don", "matched_aliases": ["Don Shula"], "query_id": "test419", "question_hash": "ba55a89553fe0d6d4df217c43524624ec883aefa45d7c8d52a3aad8eeda779ee", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "030502c38c8439bc1383d62ad4b8ca54f42e20004b889411832f8ba6701bd99c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1985838272, "similarity": 0.39229843561973526, "source_content_hash": "62ac83b137da2c99c7649524a4db77216c898ff1742baa855a1b8efa46ad687b", "source_hash": "8e61d67919b8c085806250254137eb46bd890bc17223cbfa0ac9cd99bb80bc92", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e24bc14725edc98