{"doc_id": "doc17132", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Can't Take My Eyes Off You\" is a 1967 single credited to Frankie Valli. The song was among his biggest hits, earning a gold record and reaching No. 2 on the Billboard Hot 100 for a week, stuck behind \"Windy\" by The Association.[2] It was co-written by Bob Gaudio, a bandmate of Valli's in The Four Seasons. It was Valli's biggest solo hit until he hit #1 in 1974 with \"My Eyes Adored You\".[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 258686252, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "685337249aefb8f99b5a7db3b8389e9d5d33d6f0c242f5e3ceae36564eda715f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Frankie Valli", "matched_aliases": ["Frankie Valli"], "query_id": "test466", "question_hash": "aeef2529942beacf0435c883b00ce61b34a9d826ae007d5e2ecdba034bdff75b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "502084bef3b62908093aa3525b569dcf614eb7ab6a38ca517b73922cb6222db7", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1358894679, "similarity": 0.31029986962190353, "source_content_hash": "ae76f46ac2e6b141112a461b1274f9ff036c4ba028cdfe812b791fbacdccb74e", "source_hash": "c425c1f3b5c33c340d263196eefda8f783fee04b8f5018d0ccbf3952d11a61fd", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3515341b7b2cbb8ee0f4b89de95aa3f195d0520c72be0efc9b5d97f8d2f19617", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc17143", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Lake Placid, New York hosted the Winter Olympics in 1932 and 1980. During the 1932 games, the trails outside of the village served for the cross-country skiing events and the cross-country skiing part of the Nordic combined event. Lake Placid, St Moritz and Innsbruck are the only sites to have twice hosted the Winter Olympic Games.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 921075958, "similarity": 0.9802731411229135, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d8f1fe3d295c6f5c0d4862273685d5c5c2ab3baf9f9432fe2af7a66a665ae041", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "twice", "matched_aliases": ["twice"], "query_id": "test467", "question_hash": "f02fd0d63a0991acc42145aba678e659a5e12057404adc91d523240ff90dee67", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ca0205ba90fa61bb69e0c587839b8d7869bb3c82eb4af57897947347565bf911", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 563548768, "similarity": 0.26215644820295986, "source_content_hash": "cf31ddd0f8adc25d3ecd9794d4f3411e4f058e707f0f2ee613c5e58221f718f9", "source_hash": "2f1b6be4864a48ee0d4dbe2a861942bc297a8c4b64b8f646336968f3dd9c4280", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b489df6377a37b443c894b1c083ecde4af838ea165585703d3ca5b48a6ca6c1d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc17168", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The term hot rod seems first to have appeared in the late 1930s in southern California, where people raced modified cars on dry lake beds northeast of Los Angeles under the rules of the Southern California Timing Association (SCTA), among other groups. The activity increased in popularity after World War II, particularly in California, because many returning soldiers received technical training in the service. Many cars were prepared by bootleggers in response to Prohibition to enable them to avoid revenue agents (\"Revenooers\"); some police vehicles were also modified in response.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2049644926, "similarity": 0.9905902480752781, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "bf8c390b484bdae3ccaa40a458471281677b3c27f56b9485662ef1ec91759e59", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "southern California", "matched_aliases": ["southern California"], "query_id": "test468", "question_hash": "d4a5ca83853c3d83e6cf7e5b4b453c648f4c40afbf4f47d77783415187912af2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "befca5a286083ce51d4df1fe1b362fa02df51a5f99914d069bbdc6273f724a96", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1735523842, "similarity": 0.10918114143920596, "source_content_hash": "96492433b93640e886ef77883e4f20e773cd79a62b1dc016f620da65a8d82c7a", "source_hash": "4ed82d7501663e6a5c2c5622f7c4db47d466f05db054b78752ed8e0bd3d2d795", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6a43cfd94992ad9b1b7cac44f4d20b04bc13e5804483de675d6ad1668f573e96", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc17212", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Commander K. M. Nanavati vs. State of Maharashtra was a 1959 Indian court case where Commander Kawas Manekshaw Nanavati, a Naval Commander, was tried for the murder of Prem Ahuja, his wife's lover. The incident received unprecedented media coverage and inspired several books and films such as the 1973 film Achanak and 2016 film Rustom. Commander Nanavati, accused under section 302, was initially declared not guilty by a jury,[2] but the verdict was dismissed by the Bombay High Court and the case was retried as a bench trial. This was among the last cases to be heard as a jury trial in India, as the government abolished jury trials soon after in most cases except for Parsis who still have Jury Trials for their Matrimonial Disputes.[3] Nanavati was finally pardoned by Vijayalakshmi Pandit, newly appointed Governor of Bombay and sister of Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru.[4]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 462150106, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6a371d7706b28939d6e92664cc219dbbabcfde6f9fbadef88739738bd4ac17ed", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1959", "matched_aliases": ["1959"], "query_id": "test470", "question_hash": "90987960d74307df095ad2ea8d0d8beda4ffd405fb20d61a1e16a043ce3d06ce", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8fbde1ba5a0aad1f3479c89e166a22ed3c8c120beba8c0d85401f4611a639529", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 496394722, "similarity": 0.08534067446662079, "source_content_hash": "39b9c8e8b56b9831dade356e8a3e7c28cac9b53f00b6049a8f9b0e4ee6bff914", "source_hash": "42a84126b178f3d9814c4ad3cf07a72479f5981e2f1ba5139ece7f63ea665513", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c1e0f91d3da38c36befcb921f9c4c9aed5f68243d4368870d65b1faeae5d96ec", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"