{"doc_id": "doc17618", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The International Space Station (ISS) is a space station, or a habitable artificial satellite, in low Earth orbit. Its first component launched into orbit in 1998, and the ISS is now the largest human-made body in low Earth orbit and can often be seen with the naked eye from Earth.[8][9] The ISS consists of pressurised modules, external trusses, solar arrays, and other components. ISS components have been launched by Russian Proton and Soyuz rockets, and American Space Shuttles.[10]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1979862879, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The International Space Station (ISS) is a space station, or a habitable artificial satellite, in low Earth orbit. Its first component launched into orbit in 1998, and the ISS is now the largest human-made body in low Earth orbit and can often be seen with the naked eye from Earth.[8][9] The ISS consists of pressurised modules, external trusses, solar arrays, and other components. ISS components have been launched by Russian Proton and Soyuz rockets, and American Space Shuttles.[10]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1501703634, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "1b67bafd8a6e902b4938e5e2062954c39ba980ab1729e35be10c95bb8f9988e3", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "1998", "matched_aliases": ["1998"], "query_id": "test480", "question_hash": "f35eacd3ac1aff6219a645681383fad9a6b6d720d16bc38fe16d4358a11520c8", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "39ef7e3fd7d2f76de433994454fe46375346bb204c5e118d3848934d58c90a94", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 867205525, "similarity": 0.16017316017316016, "source_content_hash": "d1656390e250ec2e6b4e1ac49b3edc65234110619a690e0cf708cabe75f6a5ad", "source_hash": "0b181fd553bb61e1ecf08208be5fa7e94a7f86c634492d7dafaae