{"doc_id": "doc18440", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On July 22, 2017, David Ozer, president of IDW Entertainment, announced at the show's San Diego Comic-Con panel that the series had been renewed for a third season with the premiere scheduled for 2018.[21][22] Space announced on the same day that it had ordered 12 episodes for a third season, together with Syfy.[23][24] Andras credited Wynonna Earp's passionate fan base (nicknamed \"Earpers\") with gaining the renewal.[25][26]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1107905695, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "On July 22, 2017, David Ozer, president of IDW Entertainment, announced at the show's San Diego Comic-Con panel that the series had been renewed for a third season with the premiere scheduled for 2018. Space announced on the same day that it had ordered 12 episodes for a third season, together with Syfy. Andras credited Wynonna Earp's passionate fan base (nicknamed \"Earpers\") with gaining the renewal.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2004917981, "similarity": 0.9711538461538461, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "172eabd0ebb21c7ceff02f9e1f2363898a44f3df3333996c20d6f4626639898d", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "2018", "matched_aliases": ["2018"], "query_id": "test502", "question_hash": "6c733009cce88d2a3b85201e8438c92c973ae54cc792c8824d75d4cb73973770", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e63b8617e0fdf9b6256e6aa245a64641c8efcde6005533fcafea05cceeb2384c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 305391503, "similarity": 0.4876441515650741, "source_content_hash": "95e04753c02e6c0efa1245bf357aa59e9d1fee4f86132dcbbd436622d2029f7c", "source_hash": "1822b059356a39b14c4f4a81dc05daaa7e046b16bb9979ef0a5e39dbcbee2544", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1