{"doc_id": "doc19126", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Mission China was released on 8 September in 55 theaters of Assam and many other theaters in Delhi, Bangalore, Pune & Mumbai. The first, second and third day collection of the film was ₹ 39.97 lakh, ₹39.50 lakh and ₹ 49 lakh respectively, 4th day collection of Mission China is ₹ 39 lakh and 5th day collection is ₹ 39 lakh. The 1st week collection is ₹ 2 crore 40 lakh.[5] It is expected to be the biggest blockbuster in Assamese film history.[6][7] it collects ₹ 5 crore only in guwahati.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1839851118, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "497135fb78bb91e57af66de6a02bebc9ee9799394e058e53358d4d8c07501025", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "₹ 39.97 lakh", "matched_aliases": ["₹ 39.97 lakh"], "query_id": "test527", "question_hash": "f2375f8d2332bbff82242691d34345744da5c82b23e613370730ea0e80ba554d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "6be70bfaf9c91f63ef5f4fa707a5ce584b1f25b94fecc2c297c195c5a20a0fdf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1177119621, "similarity": 0.18458781362007168, "source_content_hash": "074f70f3104b7c935b1afb9afbd9e30174d8cfd9112deca89ad733ded0436b0c", "source_hash": "85f205d3f69c13e7d47253dd9be8bbf7fcc47fca381194aae1876ece8292be46", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9ee392bd33e8cd95058325851876be7d25fbfdd4a8393faee9f0c234f3fbf1a2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc19267", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Jyotirindra Basu (8 July 1914 â€\" 17 January 2010), known as Jyoti Basu[1], was an Indian politician belonging to the Communist Party of India (Marxist) from West Bengal, India. He served as the Chief Minister of West Bengal state from 1977 to 2000, making him the longest-serving Chief Minister in the country's history. Basu was a member of the CPI(M) Politburo from the time of the party's founding (The CPI(M) was formed at the Seventh Congress of the Communist Party of India held in Calcutta from 31 October to 7 November 1964) in 1964 until 2008.[2][3] From 2008 until his death in 2010 he remained a permanent invitee to the central committee of the party.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2059025924, "similarity": 0.9962321024868124, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b6ce75bfa049f2144fd8e2766cec2c5132bb3da3dcc4fa714c0d1e1d169a9f9a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Jyotirindra Basu", "matched_aliases": ["Jyotirindra Basu"], "query_id": "test532", "question_hash": "9793cd20e39501d3cd1c607fd333d495315d48897717db6cd204d18f9986991b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "42828b5a73c48d40ae8f941412bb69baff34dc65d84707e18c32681d2c022a1c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 209126874, "similarity": 0.2359249329758713, "source_content_hash": "aea672058c9b1f7320dca541276c9ef70f0a428565ce03f02627d27f01a66285", "source_hash": "72c4668e5dc70fa68c8d93c57db17738689f6ab51f89c097aeed5ea9ab1fa843", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "69a21a5f1abe678aa143d5501619621dcbf3f41bec7d8ab3a4519022f97ffff2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc19310", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The record for most runs scored by a team in a single inning is 18, set by the Chicago White Stockings (now the Cubs) against the Detroit Wolverines on September 6, 1883. The modern-day record is 17, achieved by the Boston Red Sox against the Detroit Tigers on June 18, 1953.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 195768643, "similarity": 0.9981851179673321, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "0c42932c1e1a821677542f181b7ddca753a2aaff0a2826958ed2b247323ab114", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "18", "matched_aliases": ["18"], "query_id": "test533", "question_hash": "40b185b9e7de9cbeed658b1a226e6b799b490e7e0694f6daf89fe5a84c434f53", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c7dc94c2e7a4aead82baed733c0601648e6d5676149aee8cd6e14bf70c26c9dc", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 955873644, "similarity": 0.778169014084507, "source_content_hash": "f035e55be616c5677181fea634ff2bd06dd6d7197606032f4758d8129bfcf2fe", "source_hash": "99a2ac72e02cd1bb7fc27de68522d8fb5614a783be945cde4d65cd00db1b7ddd", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2edf1a4c8bc692974b6c71c2310481542cf0b6e1ed84eb56ccd57688a400c888", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc19347", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Castles served a range of purposes, the most important of which were military, administrative, and domestic. As well as defensive structures, castles were also offensive tools which could be used as a base of operations in enemy territory. Castles were established by Norman invaders of England for both defensive purposes and to pacify the country's inhabitants.[6] As William the Conqueror advanced through England, he fortified key positions to secure the land he had taken. Between 1066 and 1087, he established 36 castles such as Warwick Castle, which he used to guard against rebellion in the English Midlands.[7][8]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 844390641, "similarity": 0.9975903614457832, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "0b8afa6f5f3dd93018b657169925c555c8d21e9c85aa51194a58d39ffee36a84", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Norman invaders", "matched_aliases": ["Norman invaders"], "query_id": "test535", "question_hash": "53b8e93da045b0fca24ec036c222258bf58d093ae8b0bb65c82ff2af36bec876", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c15a6a825ed8f07d1a1bdc57d94e22680fef4cdcbfc32dc7a1f4af4512b0a831", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2044083070, "similarity": 0.4061855670103093, "source_content_hash": "019ed726efa33838ed9923e92bb2db740ccc9958e032a968b129100eddb8fcfd", "source_hash": "d0c21188c914a10d1d466a5d0f5765fb9121d2d8a378d3426741c4b48efe1153", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ca3fab5d2eb19a66d3e9fcb35e75b4a039d4ace24d53987d05f8d5f0269b20f2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc19431", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Walter (Jonathan Goldstein) is Josh's father and Drake and Megan's stepfather. He is a meteorologist for a local TV news program in San Diego, but he is often wrong about the weather. Walter is often clumsy, out of date, and seemingly empty-headed. As a result, he lacks the respect of his stepchildren, who refer to him by his first name. When Megan calls him by his first name, he always asks \"When did she start calling me Walter?\" and Audrey replies \"I don't know.\" He is also clueless and skeptical in regards to Megan's pranks which have caused the boys a lot of punishments, although starting in the episode \"The Demonator\", Walter slowly begins to notice Megan's evil ways. A running gag involves a rivalry between him and Bruce Winchill, an unseen weatherman from another station. He hates that Winchill is so popular, as he is always right with his predictions, and even forbids the use of Winchill's name in the family home.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1737632995, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2d71934096c23092821984b3a443cf8f325287bbff31518107784c0d7eb442f8", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Jonathan Goldstein", "matched_aliases": ["Jonathan Goldstein"], "query_id": "test536", "question_hash": "1b4b53b8a0be245cc7373c228b0a8fc235568714518ccf110d8c86cf18a43e3b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "87b90ca725f84b323ceba2f62416f3cf1c8049110f43f0746f764d87bb49b4f7", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1401705821, "similarity": 0.06819672131147542, "source_content_hash": "d619d321711b921d7bc10ec2f57bf636d339defbc20cbdbf83a975b5d6f67fc5", "source_hash": "2300a39974e177b1d7024dfa61cbe96d4a93dee177b1076d063281fed9989f92", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d651ba6f2def211e