{"doc_id": "doc20088", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "205420a47a224af08053e09d00403c4244446cad7a29186fc2a51143d80d2352", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "13 February 2018", "matched_aliases": ["13 February 2018"], "query_id": "test550", "question_hash": "2de93df3d30f82b485f44bbfffecc757dbb0974e4dd7df08fb57ab3378992e71", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "430476f046278e90814b88d441b886007809bcf35cfe7e713fe96e3632c4cf2c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 728908696, "similarity": 0.2546816479400749, "source_content_hash": "a6f0df7fbd4be92b2b3f5c5c45fa809e3e9a6de71b396bded2fe2b21fa3e178f", "source_hash": "dd8513a1e506051bb64802e06078c58c3f815568454f7daf94c708fb443ae5d2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "46a42dc3698e9c89ff1f8369a50cbbc33fa34bc80bec7760c9ec512d3581edfa", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc20158", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "American foreign policy was largely determined by President Woodrow Wilson, who had shown little interest in foreign affairs before entering the White House in 1913. His chief advisor was \"Colonel\" Edward House, who was sent on many top-level missions. With the outbreak of war in 1914, the United States declared neutrality and worked to broker a peace. It insisted on its neutral rights, which included allowing private corporations and banks to sell or loan money to either side. With the British blockade, there were almost no sales or loans to Germany, only to the Allies. The widely publicized German atrocities in Germany Shocked American public opinion. Neutrality was supported by Irish-Americans, who hated Britain, by German Americans who wanted to remain neutral, and by women and the churches. It was supported by the more educated upscale WASP element, led by Theodore Roosevelt. Wilson insisted on neutrality, denouncing both British and German violations, especially those German violations in which American civilians were killed. The German U-boat torpedoed the RMS Lusitania in 1915. It sank in 20 minutes, killing killed 128 American civilians and over 1000 Britons. It was against the laws of war to sink any passenger ship without allowing the passengers to reach the life boats. American opinion turned strongly against Germany as a bloodthirsty threat to civilization.[38] Germany apologized and repeatedly promised to stop attacks by its U-boats, but reversed course in early 1917 when it saw the opportunity to strangle Britain by unrestricted submarine warfare. It also made overtures to Mexico, in the Zimmermann Telegram, hoping to divert American military attention to south of the border. The German decision was not made or approved by the civilian government in Berlin, the by the military commanders and the Kaiser. They realized it meant war with the United States, but hoped to weaken the British by cutting off its imports, and strike a winning below with German soldiers transferred from the Eastern front, where Russia had surrendered. Following the repeated sinking of American merchant ships in early 1917, Wilson asked and obtained a declaration of war in April 1917. He neutralized the antiwar element by arguing this was a war With the main goal of ending aggressive militarism and indeed ending all wars. During the war the U.S. was not officially tied to the Allies by treaty, but military cooperation meant that the American contribution became significant in mid-1918. After the failure of the German spring offensive, as fresh American troops arrived in France at 10,000 a day, the Germans were in a hopeless position, and surrendered. Coupled with Wilson's Fourteen Points in January 1918, the U.S. now had the initiative on the military, diplomatic and public relations fronts. Wilsonianism-- Wilson's ideals--had become the hope of the world, including the civilian population Germany itself.[39]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1788662573, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "820e33b3c07be6f56a48abb66770c9d3816eed8095994ce1db2f71bcccb3deef", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "neutrality", "matched_aliases": ["neutrality"], "query_id": "test553", "question_hash": "416730d803318786dbfea29a873bd86b1a1a120e1ae557343def657df2dcfeac", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a8e8f0be1e917f9f6a6eaddea4d95d883bdb357247123817e4327061bf2cb632", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 876832265, "similarity": 0.02659430122116689, "source_content_hash": "f58e72d487578565c8e993ef5564bea3f7f564501a2e61783d38af7a5e5cd7b9", "source_hash": "52ae2af6e45cb2bf7b17e2643c98c4fa26f563b122fadd8c821f0bc6cb195f46", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "84e25dc449fc1b4ce4b51b1ddfac2b628771cea4edc5a3c42208e0cc923a131c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc20225", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Vampire Diaries is an American supernatural drama television series developed by Kevin Williamson and Julie Plec, based on the popular book series of the same name written by L. J. Smith. The series premiered on The CW on September 10, 2009, and concluded on March 10, 2017, airing 171 episodes over eight seasons.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1151621749, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "72094d7fd93816b5081085ad840e0aea632ae3db2410bdbb1ff4e24dc197956a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "eight", "matched_aliases": ["eight"], "query_id": "test558", "question_hash": "760968d7cbaa5865482395fc13d9fd6fe58602dc704aa2784af956aa43010c04", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d400b58227f5dab6119d1546f4249c10a97c303407757769df447496ee38260f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 384659843, "similarity": 0.09213051823416507, "source_content_hash": "a45c6d2542bc2169fdddd259d72cf07685583a42c7fc15a7026b03d56e4902c7", "source_hash": "44b7958010a6f87ca348d04446a15d36821e5d9de3868920c8c682cfc867cca2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6fcf086cf5d73b053ea4fe8a674bb652d134bec701f829a9b422e83146a8b34f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
