{"doc_id": "doc21828", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Beta decay (β-decay) is a type of radioactive decay in which a beta ray (fast energetic electron or positron) and a neutrino are emitted from an atomic nucleus. For example, beta decay of a neutron transforms it into a proton by the emission of an electron, or conversely a proton is converted into a neutron by the emission of a positron (positron emission), thus changing the nuclide type. Neither the beta particle nor its associated neutrino exist within the nucleus prior to beta decay, but are created in the decay process. By this process, unstable atoms obtain a more stable ratio of protons to neutrons. The probability of a nuclide decaying due to beta and other forms of decay is determined by its nuclear binding energy. The binding energies of all existing nuclides form what is called the nuclear band or valley of stability.[1] For either electron or positron emission to be energetically possible, the energy release (see below) or Q value must be positive.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2069027021, "similarity": 0.9898270600203459, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "10ae37a8a9d3449867c2fc12791a2201e287c501ebc82aacd2a26d1d223de399", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "beta decay", "matched_aliases": ["beta decay"], "query_id": "test615", "question_hash": "1dcfd1bf01edc16a2262a080615c807a23511a451e580fbf45678d22c1316386", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "22af443fd0033715c0859d1cac866f062cfd01c5467080d6b1dafcdeedea825e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 453507220, "similarity": 0.0825536598789213, "source_content_hash": "ab0e2c2c801e08d19acd4311c22e08076278fbdbb52e075c514f3275eca02304", "source_hash": "7465fe82ac26bfe0b1e57b4a157c92c3bcb234c87fd1364dbe91e885bd630ff9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "53442f81063bc40bf0df10e3d62c5030298e2d22862e5de6f79b51709dbeb417", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
