{"doc_id": "doc27151", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Following Bacon's advice, the scientific search for the formal cause of things is now replaced by the search for \"laws of nature\" or \"laws of physics\" in all scientific thinking. To use Aristotle's well-known terminology these are descriptions of efficient cause, and not formal cause or final cause. It means modern science limits its hypothesizing about non-physical things to the assumption that there are regularities to the ways of all things which do not change.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1776265306, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Following Bacon's advice, the scientific search for the formal cause of things is now replaced by the search for \"laws of nature\" or \"laws of physics\" in all scientific thinking. To use Aristotle's well-known terminology these are descriptions of efficient cause, and not formal cause or final cause. It means modern science limits its hypothesizing about non-physical things to the assumption that there are regularities to the ways of all things which do not change.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 162959705, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "23deced1ea0582f4c02b06ee4e347576d95cf0eabb503921fc3679f1b6b4748a", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Bacon", "matched_aliases": ["Bacon"], "query_id": "test756", "question_hash": "a579c4bc7372e52e26e47afc967d6e9006d98484258a43d218e7939071c47dbb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8f59ced91c101cf90de6ce9535d1ff44af522eed9d6af41502ee5f94004cfbcd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1452875516, "similarity": 0.04633204633204633, "source_content_hash": "a230a79e244830d19ac36241875229ecdcac0eb3bbf3befffdfeb75f0feae363", "source_hash": "9a94b8af05f158b7c4c065bbf4ab715039f99128c223822a981cfa801922cce4", "target_answer