{"doc_id": "doc27202", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Canada's Constitution Act, 1982 was signed into law by Elizabeth II as Queen of Canada on April 17, 1982 on Parliament Hill in Ottawa. Queen Elizabeth's constitutional powers over Canada were not affected by the Act, and she remains Queen and Head of State of Canada. Canada has complete sovereignty as an independent country, however, and the Queen's role as monarch of Canada is separate from her role as the British monarch or the monarch of any of the other Commonwealth realms.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1122214999, "similarity": 0.9836734693877551, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e2bca69aa68505c2520cdc2c341f5034963a3a8533988b1bd73c1a2aa88e3e9e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "April 17, 1982", "matched_aliases": ["April 17, 1982"], "query_id": "test758", "question_hash": "015e8a5e8213bc58eda03d4dd91c5655566f9e840cf608801bbce5aeeea12a68", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "33a97bcddf640d408969a233183c5e4788bf588eab4f619daedb564d2914431e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1278200074, "similarity": 0.1300639658848614, "source_content_hash": "2b925910b2b5272f999a5d0d10126230884d30ae68f0bed1f24177f6c8ba3a8f", "source_hash": "5dc924c13d3d222d5a38c73e4c255fddc99106a7c11d61e768018afbdd60308e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "96353fb2780442cd581a3a173f1cee248b6e108f1619a48c5877b025530e60a8", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc27260", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In A Christmas Carol, Marley is the first character mentioned in the first line of the story. Jacob Marley is said to have died seven years earlier on Christmas Eve (as the setting is Christmas Eve 1843, this would have made the date of his passing December 24, 1836).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1817774383, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "725af0e70ab0e32e70da16e7e527be6ad7208bdbc136dea981216b1a64177619", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "December 24, 1836", "matched_aliases": ["December 24, 1836"], "query_id": "test760", "question_hash": "e330116b9cfba513d910c9d856a85326e6e96f101078661f687c62ca5fe45fb0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c78cdd0cd58fb9b7bde4b000a8e3f70ebdc71affbb12e0483ed00007fa994a61", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1979952064, "similarity": 0.21611001964636542, "source_content_hash": "dd179c2d2ebfaa4fbc015def5a8844d4b51fc95e0268153354dd78ba9579e0ba", "source_hash": "bc6e93c575d2cd17137fecf8e6bd5f230fa12c169c613176eedcaa55de08734c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9b3fcbf0233fa9a71e48b2cd35b194bf83df897b82d64b88e01fe77996e05171", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc27338", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "State of the Union address\nWhat began as a communication between president and Congress has become a communication between the president and the people of the United States. Since the advent of radio, and then television, the speech has been broadcast live on most networks, preempting scheduled programming. To reach the largest audience, the speech, once given during the day, is now typically given in the evening, after 9pm ET (UTC-5).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1965534152, "similarity": 0.9588719153936546, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2822f5ee09827c57c758e2323b3b5be657d6d16732f52118b662861d6d397c99", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "after 9pm ET", "matched_aliases": ["after 9pm ET"], "query_id": "test763", "question_hash": "de5bd9186975c1360c83edbfcce62815286de411fdf59a71f793aee856a57771", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9899fd33fc6cf52e274bea3d2b8d00b2f6d0b37742f146dfd023414fd55da2e6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 358282870, "similarity": 0.06919642857142858, "source_content_hash": "f86e3f2103b76e2dd6e22970b063a520db5f4d113f3a217d55e589b16ac835c4", "source_hash": "689811524931e7f2e845f98706145b74fdc26284d27ec080b2e37e41842c538c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ed0cca9fd32ff98466f7e13ee243fbc206d83b49c6f81aa4ddacb037f1087e2d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc27589", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "b34b105671892b8f8cbc45c8fdac3e6723f2a5872a00a19eebba6994a24e5ef1", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "Hanna Alström", "matched_aliases": ["Hanna Alström"], "query_id": "test772", "question_hash": "f08b8231327ad53912c4529798ca16e57f0c3e50e0308f0184863cd670a82532", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d3bb2e2f2fe5e26c1d520e9fe90a7fe13b33c663686ebc5f69afcf5ecd08f2a4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 740648707, "similarity": 0.16455696202531644, "source_content_hash": "1ee2763edf0790f44af4e6961e66295b7ab163c4744ae07ecae984a674fafc70", "source_hash": "e22cada822b184f89f48bdb61197e58683e457510e3144acb14d8f5e3350cead", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "05886d23f6dddaa525669ef8899e325e0b618244482221e7694a4e62e5c73562", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc27634", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The geopolitical divisions in Europe that created a concept of East and West originated in the Roman Empire. The Eastern Mediterranean was home to the highly urbanized cultures that had Greek as their common language, whereas the West was much more rural in its character and more readily adopted Latin as its common language. After the fall of the Western Roman Empire, Western and Central Europe were substantially cut off from the East where Byzantine Greek culture and Eastern Christianity became founding influences in the Arab/Muslim world and among the Eastern and Southern Slavic peoples. Roman Catholic Western and Central Europe, as such, maintained a distinct identity particularly as it began to redevelop during the Renaissance. Even following the Protestant Reformation, Protestant Europe continued to see itself as more tied to Roman Catholic Europe than other parts of the perceived civilized world.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1557496757, "similarity": 0.9536216779572694, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b94aa92bd20506ef3028bdb57faf4ecb626690e5291a904b6fa8601a81fcb16e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the Roman Empire", "matched_aliases": ["the Roman Empire"], "query_id": "test774", "question_hash": "a9eead3a2eb47fd624e3623429ce4b30302630965f0bc7020bbccc4dd6f7f2c5", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e65d96a6d10bf872f6e6db9674175ad6687dcad38292f25a3d83f44d7426a56b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 978500586, "similarity": 0.2814814814814815, "source_content_hash": "ec6604eff5217f2a05939470660d5f79ff3b97b1972d7ae00368f4c1027bd350", "source_hash": "bb24435ec05a922dc81ac5f68994769ed11d1cfdb87c7341d3c44b0f73e68a68", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c042d3e24e317b2f12dd6778875ceba76b8f818464a37d50afb6b34eae339a97", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
