{"doc_id": "doc31939", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Abolition of Corporal Punishment Act, 1997 (Act No. 33 of 1997) is an act of the Parliament of South Africa that abolished judicial corporal punishment. This legislation followed the Constitutional Court's 1995 decision in the case of S v Williams and Others, which ruled that caning of juveniles was unconstitutional. Although the ruling in S v Williams was limited to the corporal punishment of males under the age of 21, Justice Langa mentioned in dicta that there was a consensus that corporal punishment of adults was also unconstitutional.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 847712500, "similarity": 0.9637883008356546, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f567b6cbf9f6a91e9d9d41a5dbe26503af6153e7d33f050047f76017756fe5ce", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1997", "matched_aliases": ["1997"], "query_id": "test896", "question_hash": "dd2d452126ea0965c021a6b8bd266a18622cbf253d6d16a810e0a47f35cf0fd3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "74721f39a4eba969c48828a3312acfa41b05818af6e27c1f6396e0f36bf7b78c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 238861531, "similarity": 0.8682634730538922, "source_content_hash": "81f91e2631fc27325ca4640c1f581f5e80b8504e9bcc1f4b43f1568b79617483", "source_hash": "9305d6751e03fe67080c249252fe6e14d4f90696c289709439841538593d13d6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "aa8ef0f7b62f226ce96e5851e9651b216bb4ad936274ab1adc2b82790ca044bc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc31960", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Jamestown settlement in the Colony of Virginia was the first permanent English settlement in the Americas. William Kelso writes that Jamestown \"is where the British Empire began\".[2] It was established by the Virginia Company of London as \"James Fort\" on May 4, 1607 (O.S.; May 14, 1607 N.S.),[3] and was considered permanent after brief abandonment in 1610. It followed several failed attempts, including the Lost Colony of Roanoke. Jamestown served as the capital of the colony of Virginia for 83 years, from 1616 until 1699.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1223913280, "similarity": 0.9971830985915493, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c4c960faa7d11884803a8321603af652747b42422043b4e2286ed95408d6ed21", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Virginia", "matched_aliases": ["Virginia"], "query_id": "test898", "question_hash": "904ba16641debc0b72ed55303b5cbe622395a00ecc39fc761d58820d1583f57e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "74a55a2244742a371270230ce5fdef99c85239d8313065bbaab5fd4aaa4e2a32", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1929605042, "similarity": 0.084070796460177, "source_content_hash": "7f306c440ce4084519b59461b79fdf08a08311949fa848f76bbaccf40243d625", "source_hash": "b4a71de9d300970561e725df24bd94b1933c61a34d1947811b3e4733ddb6a415", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b1dba146fdc8f831daaadb0382c50bb69d79d4ba6c8c1780b9b5bd44366672f4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc32115", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Bill of Rights, also known as the English Bill of Rights, is an Act of the Parliament of England that deals with constitutional matters and sets out certain basic civil rights. It received the Royal Assent on 16 December 1689 and is a restatement in statutory form of the Declaration of Right presented by the Convention Parliament to William III and Mary II in February 1689, inviting them to become joint sovereigns of England. The Bill of Rights lays down limits on the powers of the monarch and sets out the rights of Parliament, including the requirement for regular parliaments, free elections, and freedom of speech in Parliament. It sets out certain rights of individuals including the prohibition of cruel and unusual punishment and reestablished Protestants to have arms for their defence within the rule of law. Furthermore, the Bill of Rights described and condemned several misdeeds of James II of England.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 806925202, "similarity": 0.9983775013520823, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5fcc14d2ea46c0e24221ba4fbd9568b42d1e0ebe74780eaf21bc2eff57b74a09", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1689", "matched_aliases": ["1689", "16 December 1689"], "query_id": "test902", "question_hash": "25958aaf15842a88e547f9d5afaeca68c0545637013ed66c9caa8b4798315618", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "63cb5910a02b30dfd573f77a8546d0f7d881cb902a5c1aeca8777934ae3d62dd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2046864148, "similarity": 0.397547266223812, "source_content_hash": "ffb25986c4c5b6e837c4863cce5d1bdc6862ff85e962c94bf6e8c3c05cae5dcf", "source_hash": "9f37bc1655cd255f3522cadc5ab7e19571ceae7a0fad075252ec4ff86369749b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "072afa8b7b4d08b47dfc83d26aba55cf09ba0a53c1caa976cd70750819c62e6b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc32213", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Prince Edward Island (PEI or P.E.I.; French: Île-du-Prince-Édouard) is a province of Canada consisting of the island of the same name, and several much smaller islands. Prince Edward Island is one of the three Maritime Provinces and is the smallest province in both land area and population. It is part of the traditional lands of the Mi'kmaq, and became a British colony in the 1700s and was federated into Canada as a province in 1873. Its capital is Charlottetown. According to the 2016 census, the province of Prince Edward Island has 142,907 residents.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1678095865, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "fa7723f00f8481ebbb7de018f64546e1b324f0092491a443e9492372e27008be", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "142,907 residents", "matched_aliases": ["142,907 residents", "142,907"], "query_id": "test905", "question_hash": "195f205c1ed1e8dae3c5e3a009dd9e7183a10b9cd95dfa9715886581cbd6c2aa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "358f682f7c3aca5727e563b759026758b94ec6c35db2ebdfd439e7b97b8f3de0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1779172700, "similarity": 0.7374872318692544, "source_content_hash": "54049f350205d25800377eface1c647013daf3ecc703bcdcbb432ab5e1fc7706", "source_hash": "35aecdb1d82e7bd4a0184768e643caf787d5c0a04f29d7e53175d90b022bfdf6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "edcbc68a261f042dd3525903b073a656e3d173b66c0f9f72ef8b615cab4a12e5", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc32505", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Peter Andrew Beardsley MBE (born 18 January 1961) is an English former footballer who played as a forward or midfielder between 1979 and 1999. In 1987, he set a record transfer fee in the English game and represented his country 59 times between 1986 and 1996, once as captain, taking part in two FIFA World Cups (1986 and 1990) and UEFA Euro 1988. At club level, he played for Newcastle United, Liverpool and Everton, having also had spells with Carlisle United, Manchester United, Vancouver Whitecaps, Bolton Wanderers, Manchester City, Fulham, Hartlepool United and the Melbourne Knights. He was briefly appointed as the caretaker manager of Newcastle United in 2010.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1663556623, "similarity": 0.9977661950856291, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Peter Andrew Beardsley MBE (born 18 January 1961[1]) is an English former footballer who played as a forward or midfielder between 1979 and 1999. In 1987, he set a record transfer fee in the English game and represented his country 59 times between 1986 and 1996, once as captain, taking part in two FIFA World Cups (1986 and 1990) and UEFA Euro 1988. At club level, he played for Newcastle United, Liverpool and Everton, having also had spells with Carlisle United, Manchester United, Vancouver Whitecaps, Bolton Wanderers, Manchester City, Fulham, Hartlepool United and the Melbourne Knights. He was briefly appointed as the caretaker manager of Newcastle United in 2010.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1759067169, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "ca4e91d8abc0aa33168e28146b4ac02a54b4e091035e3447699f2c48f48058f8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Peter Andrew Beardsley", "matched_aliases": ["Peter Andrew Beardsley", "Peter Andrew Beardsley MBE"], "query_id": "test909", "question_hash": "91ee1f03078394a