{"doc_id": "doc33705", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The cella of the Parthenon housed the chryselephantine statue of Athena Parthenos sculpted by Phidias and dedicated in 439 or 438 BC. The appearance of this is known from other images. The decorative stonework was originally highly coloured.[61] The temple was dedicated to Athena at that time, though construction continued until almost the beginning of the Peloponnesian War in 432. By the year 438, the sculptural decoration of the Doric metopes on the frieze above the exterior colonnade, and of the Ionic frieze around the upper portion of the walls of the cella, had been completed. In the opisthodomus (the back room of the cella) were stored the monetary contributions of the Delian League, of which Athens was the leading member.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 860799414, "similarity": 0.997968855788761, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "de9d94d6358938f4f32ee77ef1716b7d278bb2246adb6b042f5bf2ae9d5047ee", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "cella", "matched_aliases": ["cella"], "query_id": "test950", "question_hash": "45d8fa434020804090bffdce539588711203d1cde7a2d5a77c3afc5ee6049072", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "0084164d87b8cfd729d54ecd46db1272d82976e50a46482c61566a291cc974d3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1651866495, "similarity": 0.2913719943422914, "source_content_hash": "dfc2baec63609c7472effdaaa294321d42e58386e5b482e2d40866624715b515", "source_hash": "497fcca7a22be11c668006373a448fc8758b3447903ca3f3fead6a1a82137c7e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ee51396ce80e3fbc6fd27a3be0afd88a53b098bb976142232f21e43056ac4aa5", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc33717", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The only piece of sculpture from the Parthenon known to be from the hand of Phidias was the statue of Athena housed in the naos. This massive chryselephantine sculpture is now lost and known only from copies, vase painting, gems, literary descriptions and coins.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1381311395, "similarity": 0.9849624060150376, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c88876501e0de10d4274b4aabf603a582d4aa94c508cbcca52784e64e3f85026", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "cella", "matched_aliases": ["naos"], "query_id": "test950", "question_hash": "45d8fa434020804090bffdce539588711203d1cde7a2d5a77c3afc5ee6049072", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "44b78015840db6343a43e7a5632d694bcb2bbfa3b43928ffe21e88866e0a983a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 578547289, "similarity": 0.05366726296958855, "source_content_hash": "a89b09f24cfbac0a6895892d7055a12d91026188d60fd0448a17aa2d420898f2", "source_hash": "eee37769456862dce502f62ae95502dd49e5044d87c57b027bdf9894b45db2e2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "42f9b3f1b77dbd6c9af8f268d047fc5fcbde33e49cd3b148d2c5dc6e54e5f080", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc33819", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Mike Post (born Leland Michael Postil, September 29, 1944) is an American composer, best known for his TV theme songs for such series as Law & Order, Law & Order: SVU, The A-Team, NYPD Blue, Renegade, The Rockford Files, L.A. Law, Quantum Leap, Magnum, P.I., and Hill Street Blues.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 621385546, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b827bde5aada3dd4eec7038cf10c14e75f60987908bffb28f471600b0abf4413", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Mike Post", "matched_aliases": ["Mike Post"], "query_id": "test955", "question_hash": "98d7329d493f7a7ce2f1635b23123cc271d2c320a6aab2d5932ae09f171d631b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3273e78d6fba97e7ed6fbbd49952fc5cc2f50ad629c434ff563882f6813ad56d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1041496406, "similarity": 0.6736842105263158, "source_content_hash": "35a1eff22cc5e0e053194d24a43627fbec89b9a39ad63c62e4c3c2e002c49c61", "source_hash": "3f0dfe5cf34c2b7a988a4616d74495c64d1359b7a49eeece16dcbff39df5acda", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2967865cd281e4834ef3b1e94833ef3d2f995c655e1d40f48c48dab87413ecca", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc33892", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Moscow Kremlin (Russian: Моско́вский Кремль, tr. Moskovskiy Kreml, IPA: [mɐˈskofskʲɪj krʲemlʲ]), usually referred to as the Kremlin, is a fortified complex at the heart of Moscow, overlooking the Moskva River to the south, Saint Basil's Cathedral and Red Square to the east, and the Alexander Garden to the west. It is the best known of the kremlins (Russian citadels) and includes five palaces, four cathedrals, and the enclosing Kremlin Wall with Kremlin towers. Also within this complex is the Grand Kremlin Palace that was formerly the tsar's Moscow residence. The complex serves as the official residence of the President of the Russian Federation.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1772357962, "similarity": 0.9984779299847792, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "bdfea71469773dc62e610554bb734896045a0e19271c1ebc0ef27525c9c6c8de", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the tsar's Moscow residence", "matched_aliases": ["the tsar's Moscow residence"], "query_id": "test958", "question_hash": "d791093f9e6b0537d01eb38856f92208b367db80108c9831406e5db1dd9ad12e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "440a7b4774ad5da39d02d689f69a8bed533c37df93ba117e815932034dc671fe", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1539157281, "similarity": 0.06666666666666667, "source_content_hash": "190bc827b844dc1ae0067ad0ff7914900759b44d020564ab70abba77f920ea92", "source_hash": "f1eb738841c0de83dff9f2049d258064044ae247ab842f234879a186d80e8ba6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "f725994901383005af87919d340e8944ac3f980b24185c1ebab7706d5a3c698a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc33926", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The opening ceremony of the 2018 Winter Olympics was held at the Pyeongchang Olympic Stadium in Pyeongchang, South Korea on 9 February 2018. It began at 20:00 KST and finished at approximately 22:20 KST. The Games were officially opened by President of the Republic of Korea Moon Jae-in.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1752867962, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "86afa4de99196b9162073e02cdaff110fd0a4d8940d7718a861ad69ae828a96b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "9 February 2018", "matched_aliases": ["February 9, 2018"], "query_id": "test960", "question_hash": "f0e49ed45e9418247462655be1c2b90bd90218e2b1f8e9e36f7b56bc7ae2019f", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "6396c0081df2c1a11104f8b022a696e8b86ce055fed40a0b9221a0861be84615", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1171003552, "similarity": 0.1412639405204461, "source_content_hash": "6710b636de11b60a71f749d2de3581120beddb456372d37d4a73fb7d4671b5e6", "source_hash": "67d35d539e04d7d7b4b1e561560bc01fd2f219ba9d77893b039745c6a79d485f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e8d0b93b270b53be2d0533e5c122ce1bc23408fc6eb8665508f1bf9a68a180f1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc33943", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The \"Theme from The Dukes of Hazzard (Good Ol' Boys)\" is a song written and recorded by American country music singer Waylon Jennings. It was released in August 1980 as the second single from the album Music Man. Recognizable to fans as the theme to the CBS comedy adventure television series The Dukes of Hazzard, the song became a #1 hit on the Billboard magazine Hot Country Singles chart in 1980.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2074423356, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a3089d2f6d74c0a5a8f2360de6560cc0a9f0e32a9b3eba7db8224a6a12d34a58", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Waylon Jennings", "matched_aliases": ["Waylon Jennings"], "query_id": "test961", "question_hash": "83c3ded075973643a4a6a5e07a698ff24cdc6954612734f3c4582a1b58760e4d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4e775dba89e6677c6fe187e2dab0d9abb27a4f79364e0bba345a5a27232c702b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1761403639, "similarity": 0.4960182025028441, "source_content_hash": "46c29f4efede76f06bf05ebb4e6f8d2c2f769642b6e6f9d4b61bbddd6adc6676", "source_hash": "1e99e8848529df7c47e8d43fb54a610d985cc51c43c472d6ce026b2f61445d38", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4acf08950f7d7a3458b004365f8ec1574f903601eec8e53eaac06f90a6430d1a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
