{"doc_id": "doc35769", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the 2013 training camp pre-season games, jersey No. 1 has been worn by rookie wide receiver Alex Gillett, and No. 5 by rookie wide receiver Omarius Hines. Quarterback Don Majkowski wore No. 5 his rookie season (1987) before switching to No. 7.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1148833693, "similarity": 0.9939393939393939, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "3c368be22b21041ff2f72357d29677bb11ea468ac06df4995ccb0b5c755612c2", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Don Majkowski", "matched_aliases": ["Don Majkowski", "Quarterback Don Majkowski"], "query_id": "test1013", "question_hash": "1ad6340a45c50336b91314b9e971b9c1d1eb8a892dc507819f5d38c5cb42f50d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "91bceae62066f0f3209574a4a9fc02849ed39940408e596c61c99bd7551dd4af", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 627994627, "similarity": 0.8986083499005965, "source_content_hash": "97e99a69f3f09736d32a44ff0a978a9b6960257ea4430382da0cfdbb56a9cdee", "source_hash": "ee35d6820d928c865ff27852a6488b0f6b11846ed0cffa51d35ed52e5d254fcf", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "32595a970b52571af2381f0393344741736bba1707b8835a79b477636bd1d740", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc35772", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Maginot Line (French: Ligne Maginot, IPA: [liɲ maʒino]), named after the French Minister of War André Maginot, was a line of concrete fortifications, obstacles, and weapon installations built by France in the 1930s to deter invasion by Germany and force them to move around the fortifications. Constructed on the French side of its borders with Italy, Switzerland, Germany, and Luxembourg, the line did not extend to the English Channel due to French strategy that envisioned a move into Belgium to counter a German assault.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1783081142, "similarity": 0.9981060606060606, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1dff84293e9e6072a17c60a39891879408d790e95cfb4449c236208b48f70767", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Maginot Line", "matched_aliases": ["Maginot Line"], "query_id": "test1014", "question_hash": "659636ad85aade39a33320d150ca449fecacf4d8d98f3ac3cf720a08858e89b4", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "52011a2e710f11680fb89092ce568f30438d57d146697290f0c4c8cdcb69879d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 258123300, "similarity": 0.2665388302972196, "source_content_hash": "c291db48397a548fd0164cac245dfa5208035e2f6c137ac6f4401aa63ab73da8", "source_hash": "0e6413e281db2645299e298442ed651c91d417606d0136bd565484a541d0659b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1c79d04f12bebb976e5c5876c0c73ddab4f17a6513d8556c0b08e69806f0597d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc35855", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Ain't Living Long Like This is the debut studio album by American country music singer-songwriter Rodney Crowell, released in 1978 by Warner Bros. Records. It failed to enter the Top Country Albums chart. The songs, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles but they all failed to chart within the top 40. Despite this, Ain't Living Long Like This is considered one Crowell's best and most influential albums. Brett Hartenbach of Allmusic says it \"not only showcases his songwriting prowess, but also his ability to deliver a song, whether it's one of his own or the work of another writer\".[2] Most of the songs on this album were later covered by other artists including The Oak Ridge Boys and Alan Jackson. When the album was re-released in 2002 the font on the cover was enlarged to make it more legible.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 120699591, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b0268b9972a10ed04c973d1305aeeee6ad628b1de6cb32e6b12f1fbea08fb6be", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Rodney Crowell", "matched_aliases": ["Rodney Crowell"], "query_id": "test1016", "question_hash": "ec2f076e3256000aacd8bdf3cbfa4237eb967525199db6a34dcc59b4a00313cd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a2a0c7a1afc9f667692e4e66c95728b349294d41231d0af15e416c5787a2e029", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1332219876, "similarity": 0.2876132930513595, "source_content_hash": "8cd0521c2ad379b122e443f9cb2a344d6cbac145f8e7c117b17ad68c4ecc790e", "source_hash": "82a52bfa81c8efd9754b12f6e781d680413f345e5638b2ad105bf434ce773807", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7f05da90be1517eb701cfe07d62cbadb5a454ad19cae6e49a17fbe4f9e31dfd9", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc35863", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The visible part of the human nose is the protruding part of the face that bears the nostrils. The shape of the nose is determined by the ethmoid bone and the nasal septum, which consists mostly of cartilage and which separates the nostrils. On average the nose of a male is larger than that of a female.[1]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1219164949, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6a4695e1320cae90ca438e0ae07d56cc951389cdad74214d46e42efd50697e5d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the nasal septum", "matched_aliases": ["the nasal septum", "septum"], "query_id": "test1017", "question_hash": "d14d1053f5d75438bd5d232eff06aa3daae5a926a9775befe1cc9b818a341768", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "dfba95e401a41a31a39c43fe1ed5e8304b4557e26f01d2f9b64c0fa9a1678ca3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 767495138, "similarity": 0.3942766295707472, "source_content_hash": "d8c0581d4f7caf0d4d64d38a23373c38b3519712f068320c11944d19de1b1f5b", "source_hash": "557b7c5e894ff1602e76461af48b7a2ff165d8c106fa22b8e81acfca1249be53", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1efe1c54bf3741d43ff28a0a9a1dfb7802b534d5615162c0fd7babb1307dcc78", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
