{"doc_id": "doc37026", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Treasure of the Sierra Madre (originally titled Der Schatz der Sierra Madre) is a 1927 adventure novel by bilingual German author B. Traven, whose identity remains unknown. In the book, two destitute American men in the 1920s join an older American man in Mexico to prospect for gold. John Huston adapted the book as a 1948 film of the same name.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1244076936, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "4a427261a6cb982124b584d94723d73b34ac2ae9a31de799d31a753ecbc4dcd2", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "B. Traven", "matched_aliases": ["B. Traven", "bilingual German author B. Traven"], "query_id": "test1063", "question_hash": "5d35183aacadda83e1268d1c85e5e9a9f79bffd68a188151cad52ca093ca7910", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "451dc9db6f531c05ae7c64e2227a2094f8a5ff8dd74e5c85a4d73256894ded32", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 578042878, "similarity": 0.7426981919332406, "source_content_hash": "cea50a4ef809733dc276700e471ad92a41229dcbb9832a897e93c7fe569105c5", "source_hash": "192b47a19f2870adfe150dd90526b41735e38ba429a0c5311a608a3d3a795ea0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "40fd1774ca773153576ade2946be741dca4aad962e3e3262735e2b6dc01403b0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc37038", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The iconic Star Destroyer first appears in the opening scene of Star Wars, as Darth Vader's flagship, the Devastator, chases the Tantive IV above Tatooine. This appearance shows the Imperial ship's massive size in comparison to the Tantive IV.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 370943200, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "aae14fa8d4e38c0ecbc3af077879934e1f7a2e7e4c25ff284b10d4168be3ec1d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Devastator", "matched_aliases": ["Devastator"], "query_id": "test1064", "question_hash": "1557c121e2a4ce3acabb0c732539d5a4c995479299c8abe2ebd83c171bc72a22", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e7c2a5c6b1b3d04ab431f1d06222826b4648ceb7fc5acbb212b0e98b195d702a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 833872783, "similarity": 0.3137254901960784, "source_content_hash": "10836209842a9a965de787c3950adc2c63c35359ea92cc08ceeca9093761b8df", "source_hash": "9f558be325103f01fbf2bd834fde2d504c79ccf77da141a2f01a7d96245baa48", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "decd4b44753d59cdb6bc7c7c0d5bb7b7254190426b391eb67ad247182869394f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc37055", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Nala (voiced by Moira Kelly in The Lion King, The Lion King II: Simba's Pride, and The Lion King 1½, and Gabrielle Union in The Lion Guard) is the daughter of Sarafina, the best friend and later wife of Simba and Kiara and Kion's mother. Although she is a prominent character in The Lion King, she makes minor appearances in Simba's Pride, The Lion King 1½, and The Lion Guard.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1606683986, "similarity": 0.9946949602122016, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "61f10d2981c1a8383d645c742ce8209550b2f64a5e84bf3d23cc3e2deb788f70", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Nala", "matched_aliases": ["Nala"], "query_id": "test1065", "question_hash": "75b064bfbe035520728e85178b056c47f8e9eff8886d3472bf449130c6c823a3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "62ae1a15164d1ff4fb9dd770f11d3e1f1074577dcec509782ada3ee98d311b6a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 90012247, "similarity": 0.13680781758957655, "source_content_hash": "9b5f2b0d9864dd1723357bb56378e8026db7be9ba4b522f700146b9a0e8cc083", "source_hash": "f0082b59cb0fd68cb7b132a5418521748fda255c902c2b6f7bcd56b877e9bd9c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c113e9078d24286166662b993fc8aa7ced2350edc866317c3dcea99239734432", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc37187", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On March 7, 2014, Star Wars: The Clone Wars released its sixth season, which included 13 episodes of bonus content.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 55743215, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "On March 7, 2014, the Star Wars: The Clone Wars feature film was released on Netflix, marking the availability of the sixth season alongside other seasons and the feature film.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1550546781, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "42e5d88d5ba9152ea12c0cc613d0f5a8ced2bb75002a334ccce1f350f7e548f6", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "6", "matched_aliases": ["6"], "query_id": "test1068", "question_hash": "198845dcb13f881329e0f51a592262ae7d3b4272944d0a5cd0a9e88bdfaba836", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5f1eef5069910b00dc89015a4e0ded770b5e8589d1651c11d21b9498ffee6768", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1969243287, "similarity": 0.9472830494728305, "source_content_hash": "1352ef7e4e5f9553624f710921a40baba3baea7d378749a63eccbb66450db814", "source_hash": "04940fdf7d8ca47f56a36b5eb8ea488ff7d6e2d9161a9eb21ebe056c95f8a2ce", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e4197950f6b8e97854b4467e90d38615460a85b5d4618f04f84235ad13d45c9e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc37211", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Chilliwack is a Canadian rock band centered on the singer and guitarist Bill Henderson, which started off with a more Progressive rock sound that incorporated elements of folk, jazz, and blues, before moving towards a more straight-ahead hard rock/pop rock sound by the mid-70s. They were active from 1970 to 1988, while Henderson reformed the band in 1997. Their six best-selling songs were \"My Girl (Gone, Gone, Gone)\",[3] \"I Believe\", \"Whatcha Gonna Do\", \"Fly At Night\", \"Crazy Talk\", and \"Lonesome Mary\". The band's lineup has changed many times while they have continued to tour across Canada.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 699939920, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Chilliwack is a Canadian rock band centered on the singer and guitarist Bill Henderson, which started off with a more Progressive rock sound that incorporated elements of folk, jazz, and blues, before moving towards a more straight-ahead hard rock/pop rock sound by the mid-70s. They were active from 1970 to 1988, while Henderson reformed the band in 1997. Their six best-selling songs were \"My Girl (Gone, Gone, Gone)\",[3] \"I Believe\", \"Whatcha Gonna Do\", \"Fly At Night\", \"Crazy Talk\", and \"Lonesome Mary\". The band's lineup has changed many times while they have continued to tour across Canada.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1447318818, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "187e61533bc1cc1d239e0cccb510b8eb007826dd121453b0d6139402fdf47754", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Chilliwack", "matched_aliases": ["Chilliwack"], "query_id": "test1069", "question_hash": "1c4bfa0c168b843a6b3dc121730e068d92473cedadb15cf45df5539d1d9da0db", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "358d589cea541084eb59e4222c0f792ae6f0cdd4a073961ec179deae