{"doc_id": "doc40151", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Under federal law, airsoft guns are not classified as firearms and are legal for all ages. People under the age of 18 are not permitted to buy airsoft guns over the counter in stores. However, a person of any age may use one (with the permission of their parents of course for anyone under 18). This is also the case for the laws in each state. However, in some major cities, the definition of a firearm within their respected ordinances includes propulsion by spring or compressed air, thus making airsoft subject to applicable laws. For example, airsoft guns within the state of California can only be bought by a person above the age of 18. However, no laws indicate an age requirement to sell airsoft guns. Generally speaking, toy, look-alike, and imitation firearms must have an orange tip during shipping and transportation.[53]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1229752997, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7d7c9a5018fd4f6aa5c7f9b6d6ac93b66d4a333d4e443eda6d35745da63d0435", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "18", "matched_aliases": ["18"], "query_id": "test1133", "question_hash": "02ac1bc7e74ba2aee7ac02f329b31e3bdb2a76bda6c39f89c5753334e22bbe92", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "51f291d8678c39c4d219f270bb84ff53efc9511a0665409a00c996f24964878f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1667670157, "similarity": 0.037944664031620556, "source_content_hash": "87282e3da0989095e5cea296d234f1c6a7a62a94bb3e006b9dd98501d790d67c", "source_hash": "e52d8509763410a85974fd0cf987b12c9a416a00ab0ce0de8b2790277945518d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ebfe430514c0a56ddf0d16b8322e0bfd2975ff77e86ccef5dca2d4f77a9c91b2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40207", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "It has been claimed that jelly beans were mentioned first during 1861, when Boston confectioner William Schrafft urged people to send his jelly beans to soldiers during the American Civil War. It was not until July 5, 1905, that jelly beans were mentioned in the Chicago Daily News. The advertisement publicized bulk jelly beans sold by volume for nine cents per pound, according to the book The Century in Food: America's Fads and Favorites. Most historians contend that jelly beans were first associated with celebrations of Easter in the United States sometime during the 1930s due to their egg-like shape.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 80692821, "similarity": 0.9975429975429976, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "bce0e72ee78afb272ae24a9b42948c58da1ef5f711c72eba5a47343406f0ab01", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "during the 1930s", "matched_aliases": ["during the 1930s", "1930s"], "query_id": "test1135", "question_hash": "bb0207ec533e4496a890aad90c4729da2d9dece1c89c82c67609a56993711ba5", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4c9b3c88b7247ade690ea862f70d35a58504beb82ecdf6e26636f4087b50846b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1680245488, "similarity": 0.08764044943820225, "source_content_hash": "b5258d2fec04212a29de056484e711b91a9de75d1c7b21a19337980413f3cf2f", "source_hash": "94112d853647fec28062dc4e59b56394b2dd4916fb7f8f4e6790fc5db901e12f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "beda94cae86df191792b782637d7d8a9415d5d97695da8b72417af68de50710f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40236", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Although the tradition of decorating the home with evergreens was long established, the custom of decorating an entire small tree was unknown in Britain until some two centuries ago. At the time of the personal union with Hanover, George III's German-born wife, Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz, introduced a Christmas tree at a party she gave for children in 1800. The custom did not at first spread much beyond the royal family, but Queen Victoria as a child was familiar with it and a tree was placed in her room every Christmas. In her journal for Christmas Eve 1832, the delighted 13-year-old princess wrote:", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 207273297, "similarity": 0.9822580645161291, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "abe5c929da17379a5908349ab380659d3778292f38bb3c4b144127ccecb2dbd6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz", "matched_aliases": ["Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz"], "query_id": "test1136", "question_hash": "cdb9521cb70053fe6429bc1b14ff54ac9629847c953966f8b16bd9a8a0862f5a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b1b7e0b9e8a79214f3de8f1782abcf50f547327e6b99d7ba86d96cd323d03643", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1205511766, "similarity": 0.1393188854489164, "source_content_hash": "f888ad2078958e047d71b2dc0af1dd0197438571a59bb948ca4592165e67e57e", "source_hash": "f6989230395f3503944ad561aa0622b8aa9e7741ed403af12464c6e6b303316e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3c2e7f6491bc53b677a54527c4bd31e042a6cc59f21e325a58c38c2757f5cf99", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40343", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "8b9517c5c717327d91ef2560d0d8e62a014ecab6951081b19a18bf0af6064539", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "K'iche'", "matched_aliases": ["K'iche'"], "query_id": "test1137", "question_hash": "07d8becf4cf9babe81f03cfdf9115d2cbc26b5e6f0a0550c54b978715a4a9eb3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d67ce503938b8f3895c4c5b46bf10f7771168ee553d636b26616537eccd8e059", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1938755211, "similarity": 0.30689655172413793, "source_content_hash": "5ec46ca66709ed1a6169353d1d6ec6fbb9f14805323ca6a5be1f8c293b01742a", "source_hash": "55f56da66a3e2b0b805751da6353403391a31089c588275fb2b4692cf3f9eda8", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a268695da56d4fd9552696e1b3bb3bbc2fedd10c75350181e8940ebd90988d5e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40373", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Like most mineral nutrients, the majority of the iron absorbed from digested food or supplements is absorbed in the duodenum by enterocytes of the duodenal lining. These cells have special molecules that allow them to move iron into the body. To be absorbed, dietary iron can be absorbed as part of a protein such as heme protein or iron must be in its ferrous Fe2+ form. A ferric reductase enzyme on the enterocytes' brush border, duodenal cytochrome B (Dcytb), reduces ferric Fe3+ to Fe2+. A protein called divalent metal transporter 1 (DMT1), which can transport several divalent metals across the plasma membrane, then transports iron across the enterocyte's cell membrane into the cell.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 284107025, "similarity": 0.9949458483754513, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9266faf04e9c6ad0893eb58b7b3cccea531692cb04437c2ef6fb696da882ff92", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "in the duodenum", "matched_aliases": ["in the duodenum", "the duodenum"], "query_id": "test1138", "question_hash": "68aaa5f357ca90fc5f51c8a1227da9faa8bd3d7cedb54fd4bc1e13b4fc3e8dd2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "48e6c2c5bf79f68de38f9d036ef8fd33c6194c26f38f8d12e4e8e497ed9088f4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1973862646, "similarity": 0.2539936102236422, "source_content_hash": "41e15164add4dc9d21fa02d0b1e079f7e39b995ea29b8d4bb6d86d71438d2cdb", "source_hash": "58544af2e5b5647b3b6745deb5626871d65765298f7488044b25d0433fd751bc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "577f613ce763e1c913b5fb9b6a6c495c9638c4572dcbe3e6ece67b154838fd0c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40554", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "At the time of its initial public offering (IPO) on the stock market in June 1992, Starbucks had 140 outlets, with a revenue of US$73.5 million, up from US$1.3 million in 1987. The company's market value was US$271 million by this time. The 12% portion of the company that was sold raised around US$25 million for the company, which facilitated a doubling of the number of stores over the next two years.[27] By September 1992, Starbucks' share price had risen by 70% to over 100 times the earnings per share of the previous year.[21]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 358011655, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b838d77ef22c366e503f209a969ec6c123ed82d4da942c8bd56abf880160b7b8", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "June 1992", "matched_aliases": ["June 1992", "1992"], "query_id": "test1144", "question_hash": "3a5a8b197c1e766a56e20bbe9a4171f14b5987349a100c5545b418553bc8be79", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "7ed00ef972cf8fd6ccac1ea2fc36b02b89f57e153c58c2506044978c91e1b68a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 901604557, "similarity": 0.1624087591240876, "source_content_hash": "c5eccee2108f4d5d66c357fb221eca174273b9545431552a2ac96c062acbd28d", "source_hash": "c67044a9808fa4438007025bcda393061ac9d129959a51a239d9bb2ac4597c4a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4577275602074e2d19049d3fcbeafa2361e71e2f93fb94c5b72059cdcc925fe3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc40684", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the summer of 2011, regulations were changed to allow for wearing of sew-on embroidered skill badges like the ones worn on the older BDUs. The 5-badge limit remained in effect, and there could be no mixing of sew-on and pin-on badges. At the same time, the US Army tape, personal nametapes, and rank insignia could be sewn-on at the wearers preference. Skill tabs, such as the President's Hundred Tab, Special Forces, Ranger, and Sapper are worn on the left sleeve pocket flap, and are subject to a 3-tab-only rule. A tab that is an integral part of a unit patch, such as the \"Mountain\" or \"Airborne\" tab, is not counted against the rule. The U.S. Army Chaplain insignia is the only authorized army branch insignia to be worn on the ACU. It is centered 1/8 inch above the right name tape. The insignia may be the metal pin-on variety or the black embroidered insignia on digitized fabric with Velcro fasteners.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 69528406, "similarity": 0.9918433931484503, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "40e0ecc94a791c2769457939b7b1a665cbb4f14795f84ad4c005ed12b2d40c7b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the right", "matched_aliases": ["the right"], "query_id": "test1145", "question_hash": "ce11598b7a48531b6f3a38b277d6a137699acd192347e3bca79bf6b6601c24aa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e6f8fba5d837360565de1a930a2450def87bd5dd694116f555ce4e5704c88ede", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 831496656, "similarity": 0.30913978494623656, "source_content_hash": "b543ed9f459d246539cf1a48718f296be6acb791f4f95ba4a8e153f8c6715176", "source_hash": "899ecf9e26ea8f8b4588b3481d2f615025884bb73fe730a48afb53c418ee5255", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "aa35cd8b9555c57234bd057cb59af66ddb5fd11787264d40637a0e8f14bf9817", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
