{"doc_id": "doc43169", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Miller Lite was essentially the first mainstream light beer. After its first inception as \"Gablinger's Diet Beer,\" developed in 1967 by Joseph L. Owades, PhD, a biochemist working for New York's Rheingold Brewery,[3] the recipe was given by Owades to Chicago's Peter Hand Brewing.[4] That year, Peter Hand Brewing was purchased by a group of investors, renamed Meister Brau Brewing, and Lite was soon introduced as Meister Brau Lite, a companion to their flagship Meister Brau. Under the new management, Meister Brau Brewing encountered significant financial problems, and in 1972, sold several of its existing labels to Miller. The recipe was relaunched simply as \"Lite\" on packaging and in advertising (with \"Lite Beer from Miller\" being its \"official\" name until the late '90s) in the test markets of Springfield, Illinois, Knoxville, Tennessee, and San Diego, California, in 1973, and heavily marketed using masculine pro sports players and other, so-called, macho figures of the day in an effort to sell to the key beer-drinking male demographic. Miller Lite was introduced nationally in 1975.[5] Miller's heavy-advertising approach worked where the two previous light beers had failed, and Miller's early production totals of 12.8 million barrels quickly increased to 24.2 million barrels by 1977 as Miller rose to 2nd place in the American brewing marketplace. Other brewers responded, in particular Anheuser-Busch with its heavily advertised Bud Light in 1982, which eventually overtook Lite in sales by 1994. Anheuser-Busch played on the branding style of \"Lite\" by highlighting the fact that their beer was called \"Bud Light,\" as \"everything else is just a light.\" In 1992, light beers became the biggest domestic beer in America, and in 1998, Miller relabeled its \"Lite\" brand as \"Miller Lite.\"[citation needed]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 791695745, "similarity": 0.995356459983611, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "560feda06104feaad6ab04ea8fa9ab84a365d52f6dcdda41d28a84dccd50870b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Miller Lite", "matched_aliases": ["Miller Lite"], "query_id": "test1210", "question_hash": "1795eb83041919e7995bf9934fa00ebc48831ada399539a3239f75e448ca0936", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8f387fbea2239e2df20cb7ce8b9def8b8da342935af462b6c62293bcf2156772", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1201071664, "similarity": 0.24210526315789474, "source_content_hash": "f0759dad765e2adce49e6ee3e2eadf155c5dd7bc0884852e4304ad9edf790f23", "source_hash": "051cabb660c9b7c987181f77e4eddab97c9272d380ade87d7c5e33eaab643276", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a151ce8fac1297448f1fe6921c7909a58c813258f2bfee77c77358742554fda4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
