{"doc_id": "doc44097", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series' title music, \"Old Ned\", won its composer Ron Grainer his second successive Ivor Novello award. The series had no standard set of opening titles but the opening sequences would often feature the Steptoe's horse, Hercules. \"Steptoe and Son\" is the Steptoes' trading name, but as established in the first episode, the \"Son\" is not Harold as initially believed, but Albert. The name dates from when he and his mother—Mrs. Steptoe—worked the rounds. The first series has the pair as very rough looking and often dirty and wearing ragged clothes, but they quickly \"tidied up\" for later series.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1615606087, "similarity": 0.9975020815986678, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7f526b21be374d27bf5c1a485920b96c7e7cd861a24aa66014b3784e751af36f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Hercules", "matched_aliases": ["Hercules"], "query_id": "test1248", "question_hash": "fa6357e9be09c6cd944baf29f691c28daec4e6c1730b61a80e75f2acb77bdce2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "02e7dfebebf66812f7aa2afdb734845dd2afbea3b610676f951e74ad804221be", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1326899104, "similarity": 0.01237842617152962, "source_content_hash": "2f12173ee6f7bb9e24138bb0f8b1c832d9a3bffc6bdf637ef4187bedafd8c5f6", "source_hash": "19652bef3e4c3c977f5a33d8e81ba45d756fd3d0dd6af9b332f9a259f0a69593", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "8ef1c47c1720754f6d9120d9e434121a4acb6db74e949f3c549250fd0742bab5", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc44175", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The first recipient was Uttam Kumar from Bengali cinema, who was honoured at the 15th National Film Awards in 1968 for his performances in Anthony Firingee and Chiriyakhana. As of 2017, Amitabh Bachchan is the most honoured actor, with four awards. Two actors—Kamal Haasan and Mammootty—have been honoured three times, while six actors—Sanjeev Kumar, Mithun Chakraborty, Om Puri, Naseeruddin Shah, Mohanlal, and Ajay Devgn—have won the award two times. Two actors have achieved the honour for performing in two languages—Mithun Chakraborty (Hindi and Bengali) and Mammootty (Malayalam and English). The most recent recipient is Riddhi Sen, who was honoured at the 65th National Film Awards for his performance in the Bengali film Nagarkirtan.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 350834232, "similarity": 0.9959731543624161, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a23ec37f9fef7dd179e5dea376730c8e18f0cd1c6a58eec8001b5f0a4d275873", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Amitabh Bachchan", "matched_aliases": ["Amitabh Bachchan"], "query_id": "test1251", "question_hash": "4475dd70a9d62aeabc316596b377ebde696969edbe944ca6e20cc31c39af2cc1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d682be5d05ff975c5b8ef463cf120f60f3f2535f0289466b0030a414231899d7", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1049949592, "similarity": 0.10583657587548638, "source_content_hash": "5cca763fb210f38728fc6284d317a3f926f3612103294fd2caf4e7fb59f022db", "source_hash": "70929fcda541ded520d4a35147e03320e548037759c7ac2d33050c57093aa902", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b3930f2af20af51a75b92912c44f5dc9621482c91195eb3a0c857d90d1b983ed", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "pro