{"doc_id": "doc46605", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Thrust SSC holds the world land speed record, set on 15 October 1997, when it achieved a speed of 1,228 km/h (763 mph) and became the first land vehicle to officially break the sound barrier.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1016007353, "similarity": 0.9895287958115183, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "37cd852b4d6fa6cd991eec9d6732228f5ed4f7e7ca340724ba22df455a0815df", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1,228 km/h", "matched_aliases": ["1,228 km/h"], "query_id": "test1317", "question_hash": "d6e838ac65bac86c81713126f5e580ddfdb3897b169ebe3fa991ecbd7015f22d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "450134efcca8bc6d5427d945cddd78850312be4485d57394fc16a924e0097243", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1850630701, "similarity": 0.6534216335540839, "source_content_hash": "64fe8d600b8bff4511ece4fce00bb08e4bb88d9328b4477d79f907e60c4afca8", "source_hash": "f909f81a831c6016a330f1b8163a2839acdba7fe9b38940b3c25c5dc01b666a0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d7552b82dc0a22c4095dfeee29d0282f874cad348b8c8de1bb7ca46baa2c3049", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc46709", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On January 22, 1903, the Hay–Herrán Treaty was signed by United States Secretary of State John M. Hay and Colombian Chargé Dr. Tomás Herrán. For $10 million and an annual payment it would have granted the United States a renewable lease in perpetuity from Colombia on the land proposed for the canal.[25] The treaty was ratified by the U.S. Senate on March 14, 1903, but the Senate of Colombia did not ratify it. Bunau-Varilla told President Theodore Roosevelt and Hay of a possible revolt by Panamanian rebels who aimed to separate from Colombia, and hoped that the United States would support the rebels with U.S. troops and money. Roosevelt changed tactics, based in part on the Mallarino–Bidlack Treaty of 1846, and actively supported the separation of Panama from Colombia and, shortly after recognizing Panama, signed a treaty with the new Panamanian government under similar terms to the Hay–Herrán Treaty.[26]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 308018589, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7f839b6084289cb392adb9dfb26d63dfdc23d67784515189d4ce67d015169752", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Theodore Roosevelt", "matched_aliases": ["Theodore Roosevelt", "President Theodore Roosevelt"], "query_id": "test1319", "question_hash": "83ed949967d468f90beddd027bf1a988840582f793fead6bf358c62a998fa92e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "37137fbcdc29b1e48ae58ce1b423f8aee3828e68489b6bd3efb3660d710e7523", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 478214525, "similarity": 0.2683544303797468, "source_content_hash": "8b04dde860747811d7d8e79a51b1f5f7127fbd596818b8d45a41e460b51cbad1", "source_hash": "5f34bf216c82c545daddb301447c212a0b68af867a1c57e8b35eba0f783b419d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7173d759399bca830599e5bfb81538a6e1ac8c2141334b9019ce6f7df9793ee0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc46715", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On May 6, 1904, President Theodore Roosevelt appointed John Findley Wallace, formerly chief engineer and finally general manager of the Illinois Central Railroad, as chief engineer of the Panama Canal Project. Overwhelmed by the disease-plagued country and forced to use often dilapidated French infrastructure and equipment, as well as being frustrated by the overly bureaucratic ICC, Wallace resigned abruptly in June 1905. He was succeeded by John Frank Stevens, a self-educated engineer who had built the Great Northern Railroad. Stevens was not a member of the ICC; he increasingly viewed its bureaucracy as a serious hindrance, bypassing the commission and sending requests and demands directly to the Roosevelt Administration in Washington.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1225709238, "similarity": 0.9920318725099602, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "On May 6, 1904, President Theodore Roosevelt appointed John Findley Wallace, formerly chief engineer and finally general manager of the Illinois Central Railroad, as chief engineer of the Panama Canal Project. Overwhelmed by the disease-plagued country and forced to use often dilapidated French infrastructure and equipment, as well as being frustrated by the overly bureaucratic ICC, Wallace resigned abruptly in June 1905. He was succeeded by John Frank Stevens, a self-educated engineer who had built the Great Northern Railroad. Stevens was not a member of the ICC; he increasingly viewed its bureaucracy as a serious hindrance, bypassing the commission and sending requests and demands directly to the Roosevelt Administration in Washington.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1679763092, "similarity": 0.9920318725099602, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "d73d9a778963a423f3296e59f7497dfbf78e00791cbcf5ec03a4cbf0a748d314", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Theodore Roosevelt", "matched_aliases": ["Theodore Roosevelt", "President Theodore Roosevelt"], "query_id": "test1319", "question_hash": "83ed949967d468f90beddd027bf1a988840582f793fead6bf358c62a998fa92e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9f6121736dd7cae6dbcae0feca92050bd68c25d9e432d8e3aceef9958e254328", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1790446929, "similarity": 0.21149751596877217, "source_content_hash": "0851078787f8e41fb6bdf8cf92c982b559aa3ff7b0bc5ff88676ead9b2187453", "source_hash": "e0822ff8c9ca2b91867c00b7d3def51a1e56ca57f18ec27e1fda34de1a451a5d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a97aa40dd3a5455c3557f308831d2c0f24d71b25deae35b3431d310976f7580a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
