{"doc_id": "doc46892", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In his penultimate film performance, Ledger played the Joker in Christopher Nolan's 2008 film The Dark Knight, released nearly six months after his death. While working on the film in London, Ledger told Sarah Lyall in their New York Times interview that he viewed The Dark Knight's Joker as a \"psychopathic, mass murdering, schizophrenic clown with zero empathy\".[31] For his work on The Dark Knight, Ledger won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor with his family accepting it on his behalf, as well as numerous other posthumous awards, including the Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor, which Christopher Nolan accepted for him.[32][33] At the time of his death on 22 January 2008, Ledger had completed about half of the work for his final film performance as Tony in Terry Gilliam's The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus.[34][35] Gilliam chose to adapt the film after his death by having fellow actors Johnny Depp, Jude Law, and Colin Farrell play \"fantasy transformations\" of his character so that Ledger's final performance could be seen in theatres.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 424311098, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ae4c0cd34832947fd32f34abe5b6ac5270a5a73c5f0d155bdd348d51ed14e1ba", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Ledger", "matched_aliases": ["Ledger"], "query_id": "test1325", "question_hash": "6f572b8463e9ffb85fdcd4c20fd01798287a0f760d1b867c73ea587885443e8b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e54ba19ba5fe477f903674cbba2afc92b273d3d2439c862e837d2ef72457b2fc", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 990868959, "similarity": 0.15148609779482264, "source_content_hash": "ce18903334127f0969fd5c26f68dad0032febda10ef964068271611bb4a5f571", "source_hash": "923546659d84c98f50beb16aaa36660cfd8b7e2e67775208a734a32e33ce1f14", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5621c3e90d2477524bb0cdd09f44fea5ac2b966077e51b7c76441b899330afcb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc47145", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Gravity, or gravitation, is a natural phenomenon by which all things with mass are brought toward (or gravitate toward) one another, including objects ranging from atoms and photons, to planets and stars. Since energy and mass are equivalent, all forms of energy (including light) cause gravitation and are under the influence of it. On Earth, gravity gives weight to physical objects, and the Moon's gravity causes the ocean tides. The gravitational attraction of the original gaseous matter present in the Universe caused it to begin coalescing, forming stars – and for the stars to group together into galaxies – so gravity is responsible for many of the large scale structures in the Universe. Gravity has an infinite range, although its effects become increasingly weaker on farther objects.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 623310195, "similarity": 0.9974874371859297, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "208f40267c84755a6e7fa51890f39c5385354b2dfd22d8844cb68fb25ba21dc2", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Gravity", "matched_aliases": ["Gravity"], "query_id": "test1331", "question_hash": "4763d12d519df56311ace3f708ccb746d83dacc7ae8c68b6d35c47ceaf3449bc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4ea39d46a96885136f6d7cac8e3ba8bef93b1125fcf9e24c70d3755bef94f608", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1879850183, "similarity": 0.1166429587482219, "source_content_hash": "db118e8935a7fc8b955d9a5b5bfc109cd7de446417f80ddd59b6358f62ab934a", "source_hash": "0e2afff9954f74632f2e3019a365b06b4fe07e9ae9a793c9cc1a76665781105f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "fe4448b31e296a7d5b25e317b3b9e785112a733d1255e9a074095fd66a3e0ab3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc47323", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Judith Cynthia Aline Keppel (born 18 August 1942) was the first one-million-pound winner on the television game show Who Wants to Be a Millionaire? in the United Kingdom. She is also the only woman in the United Kingdom to have won it and also the first person to win a million pounds or more on a British television game show. She has appeared on the BBC Two quiz show Eggheads since 2003.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 308206685, "similarity": 0.9961685823754789, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "3469a8611ea20ba02bc27e54d0d8791b286de8e65b268149ca074094b270f728", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Judith Cynthia Aline Keppel", "matched_aliases": ["Judith Cynthia Aline Keppel"], "query_id": "test1335", "question_hash": "ac638fa0f54f2c09952c98add4cd3aaeeb5240cdf7efa21a26d88e800674e996", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "09b69feab641ba29d05813fe2c85780ca9dfbc5ccd0965d5ce9b43b7ad4a1e8e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2022758358, "similarity": 0.42874845105328374, "source_content_hash": "b89ccefbdf77211c179851f03d5a44ad3e218b5420106b4e4e2fe64c9f28dff7", "source_hash": "28c2a89f3e134810244d5ab0c97222c0743b0b374d6c113d3c13a0a94f4c82c8", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2d72586b9760ac153f3decd1a521bed71b2aecbea6f068154e3515f3f9cb63d8", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
