{"doc_id": "doc50338", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Maia Harumi Shibutani was born on July 20, 1994, in New York City. She is the daughter of Chris Shibutani and Naomi Uyemura, both of Japanese descent, who met as Harvard musicians. She has an older brother, Alex Shibutani, who competes with her as her partner in the discipline of Ice Dance. She started figure skating at the age of 4 in 1998 in Old Greenwich, Connecticut, where she was a student at Greenwich Academy in Greenwich, Connecticut.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2017531612, "similarity": 0.9834254143646409, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d1800bc00e74dc3900f9e6c46f66c30b6e596cf6e0d8766d6bb1275ced7201d9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Japanese", "matched_aliases": ["Japanese"], "query_id": "test1410", "question_hash": "3794584d38967ab3904b36c0073aa63c7492933efa1f2fe4ccd1b3f0d1f83f96", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5e52bc85842f356c33ed9ae47981058e5d2d15ca3be1f751812928c1b4e4dc85", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 974875146, "similarity": 0.1, "source_content_hash": "c0656951b2f2dc3148e3e4ad33f0b41fa1a1e27aa90c846148dc0f152620b70f", "source_hash": "d48a27e3caa18bd9ed446af97682a24bac32564d4e9f72209a2d1017085ca780", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a01b536f2e98bd169e2c5670bf53075f5f25f2fdf8d7d902aa4a9aa83a6d2b28", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc50441", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Rivingtons followed up their 1962 Billboard Hot 100 hit \"Papa-Oom-Mow-Mow\" with the similar \"The Bird's the Word\" in 1963. The Trashmen had not heard this version but saw a band called The Sorensen Brothers playing it. They decided to play the song that night at their own gig. During this first performance, drummer and vocalist Steve Wahrer stopped playing and ad-libbed the \"Surfin' Bird\" middle section. Despite not knowing \"The Bird's the Word\" was a Rivingtons song, the similarity to \"Papa-Oom-Mow-Mow\" was obvious and The Trashmen added the chorus to the end of their new track.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 753688420, "similarity": 0.9949409780775716, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c2261816d0215eb871075097c5c6cffeee9f245d13a0117740c4b11d7c535f26", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1963", "matched_aliases": ["1963"], "query_id": "test1414", "question_hash": "445a07ee52e3369b257f33c9c3f6409381d9fa70d00f1535038e4deab87326a9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3922838b28038e07d3af212c93ad4680dd8d6b4067dbc9a5a88b12cf9ff8fcd8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 593187796, "similarity": 0.0380952380952381, "source_content_hash": "45373d5a451b0a2cfd144c159f89f5f6995cd3f3aa7643a2af0f500e996ec5c2", "source_hash": "b0814896d63400199bdc2f7484a6690b28a45059b824552f176e41ee27fb4779", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "11229930f11a8f7427e11635c88e9686c6509682713f3e9d7fe0262f1b54235c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8f