{"doc_id": "doc51071", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Tosca (Italian pronunciation: [ˈtoska; ˈtɔska]) is an opera in three acts by Giacomo Puccini to an Italian libretto by Luigi Illica and Giuseppe Giacosa. It premiered at the Teatro Costanzi in Rome on 14 January 1900. The work, based on Victorien Sardou's 1887 French-language dramatic play, La Tosca, is a melodramatic piece set in Rome in June 1800, with the Kingdom of Naples's control of Rome threatened by Napoleon's invasion of Italy. It contains depictions of torture, murder and suicide, as well as some of Puccini's best-known lyrical arias.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2081456149, "similarity": 0.9981818181818182, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "27a4eddb17f11136d723effbe52341c075bb71fabef98371880c2c218aefdd51", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Tosca", "matched_aliases": ["Tosca"], "query_id": "test1438", "question_hash": "05e9afe0f09151b2872cf0535524834b1c24683143525ec6e508095052e817e6", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e6681fce4a76cb18ea6c7991f8600f0bfceb424e120076dd3d1e97fc99a32482", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1501009472, "similarity": 0.3591331269349845, "source_content_hash": "ea0b520bd1cf3aea7b3719e8cd04dc2794c4e021b307ffdacf4a7463c96db68c", "source_hash": "13145ad2bef7e78d6e5f491777f3803898c148483f8c3f2228d641574a370f84", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "49524b81478bc49f924a22a7086174512010e178d975b3328d7c287ea9bac667", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc51161", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "With Sauron's assistance, the Elven-smiths forged the Rings of Power, which conferred great power upon their bearers. He then secretly forged the One Ring in the volcanic Mount Doom in Mordor. This \"One Ring to rule them all\" had the power to dominate the other Rings and enslave their wearers to Sauron's will. The Rings of Power were extremely potent, however; to create an instrument that could dominate even them, Sauron was forced to transfer a great part of his native power into it. Yet \"while he wore it, his power on earth was actually enhanced\".", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 395958236, "similarity": 0.9964093357271095, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7c179b93682e5c1eb5ec4ac88381ca0728cc4e0fc4681daaa0e0eb46bbc364aa", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Sauron", "matched_aliases": ["Sauron"], "query_id": "test1439", "question_hash": "7b5af066e7ac4187dd177f87ff62923260dbbfc8e18dd4c433fdfa98f3c51f3b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a6e635203faa9e03f78a3cdaf4e9da7b0349279b40eed6ffe36671541728aae8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 927182532, "similarity": 0.05178571428571429, "source_content_hash": "67d01037e84ad6b69e57ce1c91f470f435bb68a68c286ac40fd17cf2a35362ec", "source_hash": "ff73669a8eab70180d9f34745f113c5258a955917417fc71007ee68e39978fe9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "53ffd254d325978fb9d63cbe6d895f1a39be1a516cfd1316518e0c0e98d253cd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "ve