{"doc_id": "doc52698", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "5fe7cd9ac400af97c8cc6c99c766d0646498cde6d1613d4e7489351a7d607c64", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "May 18, 2018", "matched_aliases": ["May 18, 2018"], "query_id": "test1481", "question_hash": "d8fa7cec2eee7e166493e03d0822152769d599edfb8311f1c89fb7d9c81a685b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "44911720fbb6340f44f6788cd29a19c265ef6e1c6f72a3b06c891422f6c4f10a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 73116808, "similarity": 0.7875647668393783, "source_content_hash": "10910eebd450b404a45bcbaa720fb18dfafe234742c16525afa6a3bffd8e479b", "source_hash": "4a523eacbea6424394c00fb2e45abe4dcaf536ed8052ca90c8fc19693d83c496", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "945d0d36e9834e60bfac0fcd508f419367c1ffd7e3fe03d791264992d2a992d6", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc52772", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "With the Intertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) swinging northward over West Africa from the Southern Hemisphere in April, heavy showers coming from pre-monsoonal convective clouds mainly in the form of squall lines also known as the north easterlies formed mainly as a result of the interactions of the two dominant airmasses in Nigeria known as the Maritime tropical (south westerlies) and the Continental tropical (north easterlies). The Monsoons from the south atlantic ocean arrives in central Nigeria in July bringing with it high humidity, heavy cloud cover and heavy rainfall which can be daily occurrence lasting till September when the monsoons gradually begin retreating southward to the southern part of Nigeria. Rainfall totals in central Nigeria varies from 1,100 mm (43.3 in) in the lowlands of the river Niger Benue trough to over 2,000 mm (78.7 in) along the south western escarpment of the Jos Plateau.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1115429074, "similarity": 0.9727709556860651, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "As the Intertropical Convergence Zone shifts northward into West Africa in April, heavy rain events driven by squall lines and north easterlies emerge from the interaction between the Maritime and Continental tropical airmasses in Nigeria. While these systems originate in central Nigeria, the Monsoons from the south atlantic ocean arrive by July, bringing high humidity and heavy cloud cover that result in daily rainfall lasting until September. During this period, the monsoons gradually retreat southward to the southern part of Nigeria, marking the end of the wet season. Rainfall totals in central Nigeria vary significantly, ranging from 1,100 mm in the lowlands of the river Niger Benue trough to over 2,000 mm along the south western escarpment of the Jos Plateau.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1960784918, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5b15e892e201134b153dc4298c51e92b1c5b1163fe7e2ae1bb9a4b96059b997f", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "till September", "matched_aliases": ["till September"], "query_id": "test1484", "question_hash": "38aa07798e8a6ffd4cd7e9132d9b09e4c2196e0ad97468fcf4eb73d8acce409d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "dac165b6c3c34c8beedf598a62d87d6c7ac1edb8f7d445c089626bef909339ac", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1731917009, "similarity": 0.19132369299221358, "source_content_hash": "1a230fe4d27a63788b6ba2d5f16af03a9d88e6deadc1ad3cfeaf53c866f99660", "source_hash": "3771047755610a3f43e35ea721120c27e6ed0905234bf6faa90612b13accbf64", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ff9a6390c22d0468c732b4d8fe5b188d5f34e596047d281330ac6a69e8bae20d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc52806", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Cylinder's text has traditionally been seen by biblical scholars as corroborative evidence of Cyrus' policy of the repatriation of the Jewish people following their Babylonian captivity[4] (an act that the Book of Ezra attributes to Cyrus[5]), as the text refers to the restoration of cult sanctuaries and repatriation of deported peoples.[6] This interpretation has been disputed, as the text identifies only Mesopotamian sanctuaries, and makes no mention of Jews, Jerusalem, or Judea.[7] The Cylinder has also been referred to by Mohammad Reza Pahlavi, the last Shah of Iran, as the first declaration of universal human rights, a view rejected by some historians as anachronistic and a misunderstanding of the Cylinder's generic nature as a typical statement made by a new monarch at the beginning of his reign.[8][9][10][11][12][13] Neil MacGregor, Director of the British Museum, has stated that the cylinder was \"the first attempt we know about running a society, a state with different nationalities and faithsâ€\"a new kind of statecraft.\"[14] It was adopted as a national symbol of Iran by the Imperial State which put it on display in Tehran in 1971 to commemorate 2,500 year celebration of the Persian Empire.[15] On October 14, the Mohammad Reza Shah's sister, Princess Ashraf Pahlavi, presented the United Nations Secretary General U Thant with a replica of the Cylinder. The princess asserted that \"the heritage of Cyrus was the heritage of human understanding, tolerance, courage, compassion and, above all, human liberty\".[16]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1878176571, "similarity": 0.9990281827016521, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Cylinder has long been debated by scholars as a potential first declaration of universal human rights, a view championed by Mohammad Reza Pahlavi, the last Shah of Iran. While some biblical scholars and historians argue that the text's focus on Mesopotamian sanctuaries and the absence of specific Jewish references precludes it from being a declaration of rights, others contend that the monarch's presentation of the artifact to the United Nations Secretary General U Thant, along with the Princess Ashraf Pahlavi's assertion, established its identity as the first statement of human liberty. Neil MacGregor, Director of the British Museum, described the Cylinder as the first attempt at running a society with different nationalities and faiths, characterizing it as a new kind of statecraft.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1938750136, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "aeedf058c6f8b4569a6fadc03c07afc03e9982e6a3632e274e8f23cb6e6682ab", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Cyrus", "matched_aliases": ["Cyrus"], "query_id": "test1485", "question_hash": "5162963677b689b3dd590223c62f6799821ebde648ab283647692962328e8b62", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fa5a2aa0224d2b0718822fb7e2405f0d47c74ca15fa9ecc092a517c3483ac191", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 485464458, "similarity": 0.3500821018062397, "source_content_hash": "a3c1276af0364883a5618e5b17448e13ffcf46be5150829a69531494e8c91759", "source_hash": "a2aba0921f98db9c307aabf52788fb697e397ab6cdceec87fcc7147db31a6fb9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b137f44657bbc11d6178eefd5625a0495280e06788a6f433c95617a8150e0a56", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53234", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Dragon Ball Z (ドラゴンボールゼット, Doragon Bōru Zetto, commonly abbreviated as DBZ) is the long-running anime sequel to the Dragon Ball TV series, adapted from the final twenty-six volumes of the Dragon Ball manga written by Akira Toriyama. The manga portion of the series debuted in Weekly Shōnen Jump in October 4, 1988 and lasted until 1995; the anime adaptation premiered in Japan on Fuji Television on April 26, 1989, taking over its predecessor's time slot, and ran until its end on January 31, 1996, lasting 291 episodes in Japan, and 276 episodes in the United States originally, although all 291 episodes were later broadcast when content from the first 67 episodes was restored.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 979101441, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Dragon Ball Z (ドラゴンボールゼット, Doragon Bōru Zetto, commonly abbreviated as DBZ) is the long-running anime sequel to the Dragon Ball TV series, adapted from the final twenty-six volumes of the Dragon Ball manga written by Akira Toriyama. The manga portion of the series debuted in Weekly Shōnen Jump in October 4, 1988 and lasted until 1995; the anime adaptation premiered in Japan on Fuji Television on April 26, 1989, taking over its predecessor's time slot, and ran until its end on January 31, 1996, lasting 291 episodes in Japan, and 276 episodes in the United States originally, although all 291 episodes were later broadcast when content from the first 67 episodes was restored.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1227868171, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "6bd6735d9641707e901eb2e4991603ef678b87db57b9d155d65e91ebf4368933", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "291 episodes", "matched_aliases": ["291 episodes", "291"], "query_id": "test1494", "question_hash": "a3816779a4eb7b3f9f8e1f9a41340e2fb7c20d93be0af9791b0dded51aeb2254", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "412e42c01c5d8d0aa09a150bda6892a1bce8db5a230e211e39357c97d47daba6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 446748085, "similarity": 0.32083696599825634, "source_content_hash": "adb9af0f2d1fb6d2a886ab4be417662e4a110456583e0499467a7251f1b98f76", "source_hash": "a913b386f8a48f15c39e694f19c9d852da774a249eaf5e1aa1548c7fc85be27f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5ef30f62a67cbd97c5fcbf866ddfc51324dc1cd49deb65f472bf7b7bb7a413ea", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53473", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In vertebrates, the gallbladder is a small hollow organ where bile is stored and concentrated before it is released into the small intestine. In humans, the pear-shaped gallbladder lies beneath the liver, although the structure and position of the gallbladder can vary significantly among animal species. It receives and stores bile, produced by the liver, via the common hepatic duct, and releases it via the common bile duct into the duodenum, where the bile helps in the digestion of fats.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 388323755, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ab58de2fd30a6f78ada59b7a2984371eb665ae8c5174d09d30ea43b0ecf1bf94", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "beneath the liver", "matched_aliases": ["beneath the liver"], "query_id": "test1502", "question_hash": "5d3246f5a7406adb232f682874facef369d97ad9f430a827d672d3a306d6262a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "67dcf84c07707d0cb39e440247cf3fed3ee8c0493da56cb42f21301a7f175dc1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 14029772, "similarity": 0.02295552367288379, "source_content_hash": "c2b832f1a67feacd0692f30357e854d265994e431671af1e721c10ef8293f6f0", "source_hash": "e7e59b097e40f5149c4f7d8ddd2dd93b2c6170e20d7122a900a6ed85fa332526", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "18179ab214c64a7a04fecd34edec1fa4f1469f52f752ef320ca31d0bd0682a20", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53636", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The provisions relating to the right to property were changed a number of times. The Forty-Fourth Amendment of 1978 deleted the right to property from the list of fundamental rights[36] A new provision, Article 300-A, was added to the constitution, which provided that \"no person shall be deprived of his property save by authority of law\". Thus if a legislature makes a law depriving a person of his property, there would be no obligation on the part of the State to pay anything as compensation. The aggrieved person shall have no right to move the court under Article 32. Thus, the right to property is no longer a fundamental right, though it is still a constitutional right. If the government appears to have acted unfairly, the action can be challenged in a court of law by aggrieved citizens.[25]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 177854812, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "83caf59f8660fde5f970b74af29f55f3ddc7b0a726b07c9b952f594bec56988d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "constitutional right", "matched_aliases": ["constitutional right"], "query_id": "test1505", "question_hash": "51c55dbd679d85aa640babd2ef57ec46f701f5d94a57086254003779d33d061b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c67b0abc2834f167ab9eb90f9c3d780d6791d62cf4985946ad4f227f51fe5de6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1526418463, "similarity": 0.162839248434238, "source_content_hash": "5e6d8cf2f95b7908674007d27ea7cc3f02be75801da312dd9f4a41eadd4ca420", "source_hash": "2d5cbc435ba507ac6dfdc0f9a0461c52d4e0d0f529b9eeec681b5292ff0e5019", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1d9e6d73576a871c227a1a05b736c7b61881c3fce095ca3f7344755ed1032124", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53646", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Donald Trump is the 45th and current president, inaugurated on January 20, 2017.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 943085315, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "76fc28cc66190d5f53a4cb98f35f866f5663a9fab6fc5c57936fe34153ef1de1", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Donald Trump", "matched_aliases": ["Donald Trump"], "query_id": "test1506", "question_hash": "f1a2d9b8654cb8bda4235e16281c286ac6e9446c738058c9ace58c0c99a52228", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9433d21b7fa3e1a4158475a8fc698d3aff29eff63aac80fa7804ebf5509cecf9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 807272020, "similarity": 0.6593406593406593, "source_content_hash": "c159c1e129de084edba5fa3fa3e4cb1d64cbd751be5ade511b2083970dbec909", "source_hash": "2d0d8854bd5b4c6aca74a391e8f9d8ddb86e4dff5a612d20d88f9850f74d6a8f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c1c612ced9e80aa75f791ee0635fbdf512a15348dfe507452489e0785a2ba143", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53915", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The story in the book takes place in Tulsa, Oklahoma, in 1965, but this is never explicitly stated in the book.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1078993604, "similarity": 0.9866666666666667, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The story in the book takes place in Tulsa, Oklahoma, in 1965, but this is never explicitly stated in the book.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1330120738, "similarity": 0.9866666666666667, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "fc5b7d4a9e666629119628aad31e8b5efc2491766c223503c93df1a3593d0b67", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Tulsa, Oklahoma", "matched_aliases": ["Tulsa, Oklahoma"], "query_id": "test1510", "question_hash": "4958bc7bdabcc732f368311e45587475ab7640df80f556c7547c28c311b117e4", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "288c1cdc731f48a55b99f4222768daf5f448cb2c4a9c37852635f4ae7abb6dbf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 837439944, "similarity": 0.15915119363395225, "source_content_hash": "a640de0af711d0689b001482afe01de63db3b44015e19a046f5d6178049a7d5a", "source_hash": "408a82e58108d519773b84b865ad8c28e64988b1887734f4c350fcc1576b4b4b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d483f557840e62aa10770905b807aecf00f151b0bbac72f8e23608dc121baa98", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53925", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "ac3bd46c107ba6f18c01d21c37b1675def0f7976ef4c067e0f680ef9327715db", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "Dr. Lexie Grey", "matched_aliases": ["Dr. Lexie Grey", "Lexie"], "query_id": "test1511", "question_hash": "310c96880f060b1b0f3bfb77460fca1acac54a649638ff9c5c2d2f0ab93ea36b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fa77ca9c2fcdbdb9035617d6619b07ef5ca329a434a978f8c25acecd6969a9bc", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2126627744, "similarity": 0.3264887063655031, "source_content_hash": "d22e5582338a47a4a89f2701c04aec8a2adb378e63955bcfd4a4201b755cf441", "source_hash": "e6997e734591ef270d25cdac206ce4ee5618df6909ff0036d6099fbc7fd6f25c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9a950bc7f3256eb84fe123733b2979eddf092ffa92a153512ebe639671c12e68", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53927", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "63ab066067dba104a1ebaac3a14933cf208bef7ff42ee549face169223f1249d", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "Dr. Lexie Grey", "matched_aliases": ["Dr. Lexie Grey", "Lexie"], "query_id": "test1511", "question_hash": "310c96880f060b1b0f3bfb77460fca1acac54a649638ff9c5c2d2f0ab93ea36b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "37273360586b6ad88a680f84f1dcdc4a566fb84c4cef13452a9b9f4867559128", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 972498552, "similarity": 0.24158125915080528, "source_content_hash": "7ae0c88aa70f4378484c0c78cdfec326afbdd6a48ce714bd0f309419abe9a503", "source_hash": "9b7f97d03b9290b712bca9a198926a2bf615ecf32a096d36bfb7161ccb2b68b5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b514157223efd6128a722b7a88e9f4db53d49bc0466277f3569365cd9fa5e473", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc53990", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Spike is a stern but occasionally dumb American bulldog who is particularly disapproving of cats, but a softie when it comes to mice (though in his debut appearance, Dog Trouble, Spike goes after both Tom and Jerry), and later, his son Tyke. In the shorts Jerry would often try to get Tom in trouble with Spike making him a shoo-in for a beating from the bulldog. Spike has a few weaknesses that Tom tries to capitalize upon: his possessiveness about his bone and his ticklishness. He made his first appearance in the 1942 Tom and Jerry cartoon Dog Trouble, and his first speaking role was in 1944's The Bodyguard, where he was voiced by Billy Bletcher up until 1949, from which point he was voiced by Daws Butler. Unlike his father Spike, Tyke does not speak. He only communicates by yapping, whimpering, growling, facial expressions and wagging his tail. In Tom and Jerry Kids, Tyke does have a speaking role in the program and is the first time that viewers were able to hear Tyke speak. Spike is very protective towards his son and gets very angry at Tom if Tyke is bothered or harmed. Although Tyke has spoken in Tom and Jerry Kids, he has laughed in one Tom and Jerry short. After Daws Butler, Maurice LaMarche, Frank Welker, John DiMaggio, Michael Donovan, Phil LaMarr and currently Rick Zieff would all perform Spike's voice. Tyke's vocal effects are provided by Frank Welker and speaking roles by Patric Zimmerman.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 333260016, "similarity": 0.9840940525587828, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "289644451e697a61bdf8e0f737df2e30155eacdc5ee1d0786a9c072dc38b628b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Spike", "matched_aliases": ["Spike"], "query_id": "test1513", "question_hash": "c7df2480366f33cb2d2c108f5c0c55d7a6bc3c3b8a097f9ee69087659b0f5b0a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "121ea419c6983f26268ca560f37c628f5f7b430c0b9fc6ce986416494280bbc2", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 197808521, "similarity": 0.1252236135957066, "source_content_hash": "dfe4033233cae7de063177e89561d7ecb191c5f28705a546babdce53884f2eb4", "source_hash": "baf48666383ee083c2fd2b2937991670cbab347920d6834f49030e14c3846208", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bb0d53d3d1eae22d9da84b465fcaa992bb5ca96341fe8d6f639d43b20900d03f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
