{"doc_id": "doc55488", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the 12th century, luxury increased and bedsteads were made of wood much decorated with inlaid, carved, and painted ornamentation. They also used folding beds, which served as couches by day and had cushions covered with silk laid upon leather. At night a linen sheet was spread and pillows placed, while silk-covered skins served as coverlets. The Carolingian manuscripts show metal bedsteads much higher at the head than at the feet, and this shape continued in use until the 13th century in France, many cushions being added to raise the body to a sloping position. In 12th-century manuscripts, the bedsteads appear much richer, with inlays, carving, and painting, and with embroidered coverlets and mattresses in harmony. Curtains were hung above the bed and a small hanging lamp is often shown.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 204562537, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9c669bb87c0a5f850062c6540b6fbbd507746768475bbe12304062615d7090de", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the 12th century", "matched_aliases": ["the 12th century"], "query_id": "test1552", "question_hash": "57676df6fc6bfdc064c58fb717cacafa4a4f3eeec0a27ca29d42526d1a13f5cd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "95696c83dd4d9f9d92c6f0c15deff3ca2f20d0e372cd245b4b9a283a48e66d1b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 435812146, "similarity": 0.18490245971162, "source_content_hash": "6bab3f79a5e9b2add3b5a917777defa23873f3072ae0850d94ca24ef40485f3c", "source_hash": "5bc3f4b703be01676658e46108bd9d8f5830a36a173c55b26806409b98d6eb49", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a1d3999224007165a2823346a0b2a5b58bbcc663a1e5bde6b6d70979a2e565bb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc55509", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"The Glory of Love\" is a song written by Billy Hill, recorded by Benny Goodman in 1936, whose version was a number one pop hit. In 1951, R&B vocal group, The Five Keys, had their biggest R&B hit with their version of the song, hitting number one on the R&B chart for four non-consecutive weeks.[1] Although The Five Keys recording sold a reported million copies pressed recordings are very rare.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1909449957, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "0d06dfc31b14ddaed51fd6276f6c39be811ebff53804d91fcf8b90508ce6a020", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Billy Hill", "matched_aliases": ["Billy Hill"], "query_id": "test1553", "question_hash": "bec8b218e42081e844d91cd5bbda503c4977b11cae911f97a9246257fddaf3e7", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "bc5cb857e361efd24c54ad88503f96edfd2bb799195397b9389e204a9767faed", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1559600849, "similarity": 0.2517289073305671, "source_content_hash": "13f2b032f4f81328f01c229a9ef57627357f644f000318ff7ccf28a0d8263e28", "source_hash": "894039f13682216e156ce590b3c194b2103b964af4174daf3fd070349dd165f1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "17a4b5c77b38ae3cae10f3fa47b9a01a3028f59b7e07030e006e5f4e77fd7dec", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc55593", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On the Origin of Species (or more completely, On the Origin of Species by Means of Natural Selection, or the Preservation of Favoured Races in the Struggle for Life), published on 24 November 1859, is a work of scientific literature by Charles Darwin which is considered to be the foundation of evolutionary biology. Darwin's book introduced the scientific theory that populations evolve over the course of generations through a process of natural selection. It presented a body of evidence that the diversity of life arose by common descent through a branching pattern of evolution. Darwin included evidence that he had gathered on the Beagle expedition in the 1830s and his subsequent findings from research, correspondence, and experimentation.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 104647161, "similarity": 0.9940119760479041, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1f3a6b833d00a7c28a527ef46bb7ecabccd4ac663e1a9ebf5c215e8ab80fac13", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Charles Darwin", "matched_aliases": ["Charles Darwin"], "query_id": "test1555", "question_hash": "57ad3ca4e2a0bd33a984412046caefae90ba1a1531281487aa957ce28b9a24e0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "567e42963366d73aef22677065953a9ee713751ecedbfe4916413879b2e50aca", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1510855690, "similarity": 0.04114490161001789, "source_content_hash": "76c4798b6431dff93f76bb092f1473acb1bee3af7e3f96fd7c0be12e1af9dfcb", "source_hash": "3de7b696a256b55a739dafb0171f1ea099345a115338b63b0b9376a20eda5b64", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "51da781905afa5ca2791a3c2f11fefa0b86e7c985d39995d308a19d6bb48105b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc55700", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Rip It Up\" was a 1983 single by Scottish post-punk band Orange Juice. It was the second single to be released from their 1982 album of the same name. The song became the band's only UK top 40 success, reaching no. 8 in the chart. \"Rip It Up\" signalled a departure from the sound of the band's earlier singles, with Chic-influenced guitars and using a synthesiser to create a more disco-oriented sound.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 592201100, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "56efcfdc338e5a5d20f62e5a7cd3c820c74a7c0ebacce22d9a56764a9e63ea0b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Scottish post-punk band Orange Juice", "matched_aliases": ["Scottish post-punk band Orange Juice", "Orange Juice"], "query_id": "test1556", "question_hash": "1f08f5439629ba5cdf511bc5a318f658978057646390914a992f038dbfe74b36", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c515696624a9b006efaf6290230f72a7bb3fbfc40ba88039da3ad45d3b20794f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 57297722, "similarity": 0.23333333333333334, "source_content_hash": "05a02a7e67d194c1c5174420397920deef31627d1e6e58f1071c3b0d56c54923", "source_hash": "9faae49fcbddf1f6abcc6b241f464552011fc1681560aa76c5a582d231d02bc7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7400751b4ffa0208963e17eb87b0330cab7e297882e55a7a683e034d6c20320e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc55708", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In late-2011, she announced plans for a clothing and jewelry line called House of Maryse, and later began working as a realtor. In November 2016, she began starring in the reality television series Total Divas on E! as part of the main cast. She and her husband The Miz will also star in their own reality show titled Miz & Mrs. that will premiere in 2018.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 481446620, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "419b49d49805902088380952b7c222efa83965cf7e59d9a3185035f9be5a2717", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "2018", "matched_aliases": ["2018"], "query_id": "test1557", "question_hash": "ed1fff167e29a1676160990adc2653c00de6c2f8bd8fb67b2fc72dcad2349963", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "cfcf1d85e1b05bdfe71b360e6ace145c0468119c8cb9c03bdae9b0ad9bae795f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 484936799, "similarity": 0.5505124450951684, "source_content_hash": "901a330d59899826bbb1c7fa74d5ae4909153a153ca1d46988a47b9c92f8c58b", "source_hash": "3c5eb1272230cc83584b51977db81c81e99b2f2a4bd9501b0193daa5f6f4768a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0c19a553c463f969fa02675bce7a565eb6c3fb9b1184283deb33ede01480df34", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
