{"doc_id": "doc58895", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On December 1, 1969, the Selective Service System of the United States conducted two lotteries to determine the order of call to military service in the Vietnam War for men born from 1944 to 1950. These lotteries occurred during a period of conscription from just before World War II to 1973. It was the first time a lottery system had been used to select men for military service since 1942.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 205528639, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "42bc44bcdef9beff4b0ef96b0fee6fcb36187cb9831dc7ad717d9d8bb1ef36bb", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1973", "matched_aliases": ["1973"], "query_id": "test1664", "question_hash": "4e2923e5e60736e95223478b853a995bfe13f6fc43761f3153f3bf0f39802ab1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9c860261f77b5a7c2ba245ca308e8391a72fa4e07b8b440505d8c4da287a7328", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1644035266, "similarity": 0.2965986394557823, "source_content_hash": "7359d57bd4721883d4437518efd8e5a2d7708600d059f2d2efd09908333b4384", "source_hash": "17ea7448291474888f63b62c1ba3c95e36079793131b667338fe6e1a75dffff5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4cdac5b5f7727191984753215153cfce47aad8da2cbeb517b58b632410014d4a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc58901", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Draft lotteries were conducted again in 1970 (for those born in 1951) and from 1971 to 1975 (for 1952 to 1956 births). The draft numbers issued in 1972 were never used the next year to call for induction into service, because the last call was December 7 and authority to induct expired on June 30, 1973.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1088820984, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "665981856babbb36f9d1f50aa8733fe8a2603a5955d26ed3538e410c8f6fc58d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1973", "matched_aliases": ["1973"], "query_id": "test1664", "question_hash": "4e2923e5e60736e95223478b853a995bfe13f6fc43761f3153f3bf0f39802ab1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4a0781d37cca73766a1d57892a03d597f1e732ed2e7aac25fe13ff15f7911197", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1033998650, "similarity": 0.24027072758037224, "source_content_hash": "d8566b3360a0c2ba8ba31953c6cda3bf0de35f7b1c69a8a0945d6f9b5fc221ed", "source_hash": "d6491e35df732d9cc9e36e817bba345df048b94af2aeba2b793e105c792885eb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "91342c515667687cdf761c81f7f89f6d5be2e76f9a47e446552de3b08e009085", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc58920", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Super Bowl LI Halftime show took place on February 5, 2017, at NRG Stadium in Houston, Texas as part of Super Bowl LI. The show was headlined by Lady Gaga, who performed a medley of her songs, including newer material from her most recent studio album Joanne.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 748117752, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "edcd64c82f6d1993d49299ad72e009b9488af4caba11f170023a17c8605a0729", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Lady Gaga", "matched_aliases": ["Lady Gaga"], "query_id": "test1665", "question_hash": "d66d49439e9af7bb30e8b3ddc2685919b52d3cb107d2dc32ba2e694ab6a9149a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f19a021582047291a2b7c489924e0428497823a0977047ad816a95e7a1ff4150", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1631047803, "similarity": 0.37988826815642457, "source_content_hash": "7f0efb54183ad25f12fb0be05d076229f39c40fb5c6ac560d90e1459e565090d", "source_hash": "bf8509c371513a1fd136dab9919907a81fa4ba042213c2908996d73d1b16c003", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5133db8d9afe2f14bc1ceeb16546c2f999516cb7aa615c787fedbe54df27e9ae", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc59024", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The essay describes the experience of the English narrator, possibly Orwell himself, called upon to shoot an aggressive elephant while working as a police officer in Burma. Because the locals expect him to do the job, he does so against his better judgment, his anguish increased by the elephant's slow and painful death. The story is regarded as a metaphor for British imperialism, and for Orwell's view that \"when the white man turns tyrant it is his own freedom that he destroys.\"", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 501484231, "similarity": 0.9969040247678018, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "952e03457aae40308bb8e1c23d651ded2690d8ecf792a1f571ea3b4db031166f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Orwell", "matched_aliases": ["Orwell"], "query_id": "test1668", "question_hash": "93eec02e768bbdda880f08e3ebdd7a210b0a9aacf7d2c93eac62dcd298dc4c4f", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "93eb7e1597902014a5b66bd2bb0176173fa6fd33e28f27c0b45c640954dbc5f9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1481767341, "similarity": 0.22111553784860558, "source_content_hash": "3a4864f20f1bee2b4f509f68be6029a7421d327420372e0262628544d9dd6117", "source_hash": "01ebd21231540df310308cc4b578b1913bc4f83859953331fa35436a65ebd6d6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "208bea94f41df7c8f90c33496791333b7f26845c37bfb8875e8ce07a95496e87", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc59085", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The United States two-dollar bill ($2) is a current denomination of U.S. currency. The third U.S. President (1801–09), Thomas Jefferson, is featured on the obverse of the note. The reverse features an engraving of the painting The Declaration of Independence by John Trumbull. Throughout the $2 bill's pre-1929 life as a large-sized note, it was issued as a United States Note, National Bank Note, silver certificate, Treasury or \"Coin\" Note and Federal Reserve Bank Note. When U.S. currency was changed to its current size, the $2 bill was issued only as a United States Note. Production went on until 1966, when the series was discontinued. Ten years passed before the $2 bill was reissued as a Federal Reserve Note with a new reverse design. Two-dollar bills are seldom seen in circulation as a result of banking policies with businesses which has resulted in low production numbers due to lack of demand. This comparative scarcity in circulation, coupled with a lack of public knowledge that the bill is still in production and circulation, has also inspired urban legends and occasionally has created problems for people trying to use the bill to make purchases.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1428886594, "similarity": 0.9982876712328768, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The United States two-dollar bill ($2) is currently recognized as a standard denomination of U.S. currency. Thomas Jefferson, serving as the third U.S. President from 1801 to 1809, appears on the front of the note, while John Trumbull's painting of the Declaration of Independence adorns the back. Throughout its history as a large-sized note prior to 1929, the bill was issued under various names including United States Note, National Bank Note, silver certificate, Treasury Note, and Federal Reserve Bank Note. When the currency shifted to its modern size, production of the $2 bill was limited to the United States Note format until the series ended in 1966. Ten years later, the bill was reissued as a Federal Reserve Note featuring a new reverse design. Due to banking policies that have led to low production numbers and a resulting scarcity in circulation, the bill is rarely found in everyday use, which has also sparked urban legends regarding its continued existence.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1530729694, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "e3cb1148e41b1f5ed4066255666384e4fec01c0091d462fad8a0cf7ff635acec", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "current denomination of U.S. currency", "matched_aliases": ["current denomination of U.S. currency"], "query_id": "test1671", "question_hash": "82c37855d61e942d8749b2a8139c7d960bf01e27914172962db8fa30c02d1795", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "95f8f0cce0b365602063cece1e3b6056214df65fdd4a1f0d8ec9307d0dd207b5", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 371954127, "similarity": 0.9221556886227545, "source_content_hash": "3c16d8dc6af7af6d8f822e6549d036b29f98f0ad9e97e75a563488284c4c30eb", "source_hash": "04c656af7c06317f11548d86c0f78cb1759cd2fa03d1e21b0ed1668042ebc97c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0d32487b7f1db4aeea53b33e377960d34f2a67bea928869ca15e524ebe2de40c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
