{"doc_id": "doc60587", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": false, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The video features a wedding scene where the bride and groom are initially dressed formally, only to be revealed later to have fallen asleep with eyes painted on their eyelids. Their families interrupt the ceremony; the bride's family is shown to be upper-class entertainers, while the groom's family consists of lower-class carnival folk. A ringmaster, played by vocalist Brendon Urie, acts as a narrator and disrupts the events. Following an argument between the two families, the bride runs out and is followed by one of her guests. Urie drags the groom outside by his tie, where his fiancée is seen kissing the guest who followed her out of the church. The groom appears shocked as he straightens up, and Urie and the groom bow to the camera. The ringmaster is ultimately revealed to be the groom's alter ego.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 217899193, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e5ba1d86c8e537d14dab31db129442fe807cf2328a6c15da46d21f1fd91a088a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "I Write Sins Not Tragedies", "matched_aliases": ["I Write Sins Not Tragedies"], "query_id": "test1708", "question_hash": "29ae2c95808d51c1cecb862026e17d34e564396b72a3f986b4111811a7f14a41", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fd70d1fefbeaa57321baeac33120e135c1dbbd7b0c5a94eaa7d136a6b76c0702", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 119778762, "similarity": 0.125, "source_content_hash": "27dc10281f25c7ccaa27c58cecfb73060eba73edd8a67c46a52a9ad114162c23", "source_hash": "217a8cb050a372fd45cb5ad8d4ecd78e11bfc5076da6eeee69e7690a983ce2a2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0f5986918f8945473b6d22177ad534f46fd61063965e08a8fa5b5e2cc0e3f74d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc60640", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "German verbs may be classified as either weak, with a dental consonant inflection, or strong, showing a vowel gradation (ablaut). Both of these are regular systems. Most verbs of both types are regular, though various subgroups and anomalies do arise. The only completely irregular verb in the language is sein (to be). Although, textbooks for learners often class all strong verbs as irregular, there are more than 200 strong and irregular verbs, but there is a gradual tendency for strong verbs to become weak.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 958839895, "similarity": 0.9817483189241114, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d8711aa4fa2bd14e6c25f62b11054e1d27bf51793602c128fed2ccb50a4ae0ac", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "more than 200", "matched_aliases": ["more than 200", "more than 200 strong"], "query_id": "test1711", "question_hash": "28e0204abb10f7540906512af0fd602cc4679080b0593eff93089a72462a397d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "25f0729a71cc83dc8573b80e74428f2164c7393d03e14ac93f9aa48747ac6d9b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2141246555, "similarity": 0.15707762557077626, "source_content_hash": "e3e38da306bd5984b706e77cc1bea68ff38a80de425d7f4b70f5954e61898f32", "source_hash": "d43e967316640e98c86ae06e2320b3835fdd3570bde3a6f60adaf9bd6f4bc3b2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "02d08d84920f81144a254cfafb43c433b92515efc383c502b1dcf5ab49b1c2cc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc60909", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Rocky Road (Once Upon a Time) features Elsa, who has literally frozen Storybrooke and hopes to find her sister, Anna. She accompanies Emma Swan to try to break down the wall of ice she created, but her powers aren't strong enough to melt the barrier. The two, along with Hook, pay Gold a visit to find out if he has known Anna based on the necklace Elsa found in his pawn shop. Belle uses the fake dagger to \"command\" Gold to tell the truth but it fails, as he knows nothing about Elsa or Anna, and wishes them the best of luck finding her. At the same time, Robin Hood, Marian, and Roland visit \"Any Given Sundae,\" where the Snow Queen serves them ice cream, but unknown to them she casts a spell on the ice cream cone that she gave Marian. Afterwards, the family joins the other residents at the Mayor's office, as Mary Margaret, who is still trying to balance both maternal and mayoral duties, is holding the first annual \"Mayor's Fireside Chat,\" where she assures the citizens that they are no longer afraid of Regina's influence, but it appears that they want Mary Margaret to do something about the town's snowy fiasco. Mary Margaret then tells the residents about Elsa's presence in Storybrooke and is trying to reassure everyone that she is not dangerous, only to have Marian beginning to start feeling as if something was glossing over her and she passes out. Elsa's presence has also resulted in her becoming a prime suspect, and with her heart slowly freezing, a cure must be found before Marian's heart completely freezes and kills her. The Storybrooke residents blame Elsa, who is being framed by the Snow Queen for the icy cold mayhem. With the entire town ready to go after their newest addition, Emma (who starts to question her abilities as \"The Savior\") and Hook decide to hide Elsa at the sheriff's office while she and David search for the real suspect.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 575611519, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Rocky Road (Once Upon a Time) features Elsa, who is revealed to have a sister named Anna. When Elsa's aunt, the Snow Queen, serves ice cream at Any Given Sundae, she casts a spell on the ice cream cone that she gave Marian, an action that remains hidden from the characters present.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1625933718, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5414ab8c45b3dbe7400ae18c487ecd9fa755f7d633a0b99078c65ff3aa7f16d9", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Elizabeth Mitchell", "matched_aliases": ["Elizabeth Mitchell"], "query_id": "test1716", "question_hash": "1fb285e612b359191e8fa0515fbc0ea8c6e74c6d14f742f7c38567c571dacb5e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f512b838ee2076ff75d12dea926ed1457790b9b0a14dbff8908d26b456e5bfd2", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 984975516, "similarity": 0.09064609450337512, "source_content_hash": "577c50bcb3f043d78e26fdf2c42b23b60708e40642998b89c90b10b37e2c476d", "source_hash": "7401ca8df32c375807dc31ce3071377381e102b54030a05496eaf9c18daad96e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "43815e9409fdffaffbd60146f9f41e1920cd8dd41309d7765287deaf869112fa", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
