{"doc_id": "doc62264", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Paul's letter is addressed \"to the churches of Galatia\" (Galatians 1:2), but the location of these churches is a matter of debate. A minority of scholars have argued that the \"Galatia\" is an ethnic reference to a Celtic people living in northern Asia Minor, but most agree that it is a geographical reference to the Roman province in central Asia Minor, which had been settled by immigrant Celts in the 270s BC and retained Gaulish features of culture and language in Paul's day. Acts of the Apostles records Paul traveling to the \"region of Galatia and Phrygia\", which lies immediately west of Galatia.[9]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1119848375, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c9f2c4aeb28d4b9db9a3a8680b6ea50599be9e90b79d51b0217043d4aef187da", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the churches of Galatia", "matched_aliases": ["the churches of Galatia"], "query_id": "test1763", "question_hash": "8af42457c864bd444c9e81871fc5a29785e11d489ce206ab97b22d9d3fd87a27", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "2adc19199fe37819bacfb4040467ec245e0abaf0a14a68f2f0ac18407ce15f9a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 778922253, "similarity": 0.14925373134328357, "source_content_hash": "b4dd8c45584b11cb2def61ee256b06a17e527556ba1d06a8d6dfdba6665721cc", "source_hash": "66c2a9cde8d08d16bf73d8badc397585092af206f69060381644790a08265e58", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "810dbcea2ecb1a4b70a5fbe4f58fbe73c42e64de0faa254983e154e8e06ab735", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash"