{"doc_id": "doc63472", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In January 2004, the NASA twin Mars Exploration Rovers named Spirit (MER-A) and Opportunity (MER-B) landed on the surface of Mars. Both have met or exceeded all their targets. Among the most significant scientific returns has been conclusive evidence that liquid water existed at some time in the past at both landing sites. Martian dust devils and windstorms have occasionally cleaned both rovers' solar panels, and thus increased their lifespan.[31] Spirit Rover (MER-A) was active until 2010, when it stopped sending data because it had fallen into a sand dune.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1811650127, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c260d3d8a3fa21732fee157fe1e43f00543d92e30791d53b61984458793a59b9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "January 2004", "matched_aliases": ["January 2004"], "query_id": "test1803", "question_hash": "1768acaa841ce5c28ecb66cd74cb64615557eead2c464825e74fa5ad54b63123", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f5e2e38e19d7ac7e76a43183428b12b7f4c3da8dcab3173060796b7f9f51677c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 103187605, "similarity": 0.19238476953907815, "source_content_hash": "5ce3d3eb90dd92f33d8539ad1182d1fe3dbebf3145fc1eea1782a525a0b7ceb1", "source_hash": "8ad054009273fe6aff77935808037053ca60ee703dadf822e203e23f15860093", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3505e0977ae542c6bfdaaf7916b8e635addab6e30b710fc4494ff618bd4768a4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc63543", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Haji Sahib of Turangzai, the most famous Pukhtun religious leader of the time, was requested by Nawab Sir Sahibzada Abdul Qayyum to lay the foundation stone of Islamia College. Although Haji Sahib agreed to the request, he had been declared a proclaimed offender by the British for his anti-British activities and his entry was banned into British controlled territory. He was residing in tribal territory, which was outside British control, so Nawab Sahib prevailed upon Sir George Roos-Keppel and the British to permit Haji Sahib to enter British controlled territory for one day so he could lay the foundation stone of Islamia College. The British agreed to this request with the understanding that Haji Sahib would return to tribal territory once he had laid the foundation stone. Haji Sahib was permitted to enter British controlled territory for the ceremony and spent the night in the 'Pokh' Mosque of Tehkal. At the foundation stone laying ceremony, Sir Roos Keppel and other British officials were present, so Haji Sahib hid his face in his sheet (Chadar) from them and was led by Sheikh Muhammad Ibrahim to the place where he was to lay the foundation stone. After laying the stone Haji Sahib went to Tehkal and then returned to the tribal territory.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 828933301, "similarity": 0.9924573243350536, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f3be0c6f17348fe759b2e7e17802fdf41f6aced2b797988d159edc724de8ffb8", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Haji Sahib", "matched_aliases": ["Haji Sahib"], "query_id": "test1805", "question_hash": "e8505cef35fef1364b837584beb52b6c5e6bea769d2b0ffd9b6c3e907de51a41", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "bc6780158449cd66698774081bbb3a2df06335d5fdf89ff1329f8c8a646f174c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 48672058, "similarity": 0.057172557172557176, "source_content_hash": "9203a8a49283a0e542c392efeefa16906e6451ef00a8da148eb0389b4d9498c5", "source_hash": "8ad23c2c03f2edb49f706f379afeb399b7602897046a2920d52b1d49caecfb98", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2a7c7761be348838174cb50fd31b5de1eda70a2f60f2b8e8c29898c28d7a2056", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc63585", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The 2017 NCAA Women's Division I Basketball Tournament was played from Friday, March 17 to Sunday, April 2, 2017, with the Final Four played at the American Airlines Center in Dallas, Texas on March 31 and April 2. This was the first time that the women's Final Four was played in Dallas and the first time since 2002 that the Final Four games were played on Friday and Sunday, rather than Sunday and Tuesday. South Carolina defeated Mississippi State to win the championship.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 379556570, "similarity": 0.9968586387434555, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e635d71322083fc010fd8e6ae69c05c518e75274215e9c6db95cbab533f3c14a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "South Carolina Gamecocks", "matched_aliases": ["South Carolina"], "query_id": "test1808", "question_hash": "29e9b7a25b2c65aeba05ba7d12e8309b4db3aa2ed08b6cde2b80e42ca4330a89", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1013303f83678fcdb86b0b8c45f483d5a6f050b890499bff55a7e1fef672d333", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1620753283, "similarity": 0.15233415233415235, "source_content_hash": "6495d2359e090ac8a270a411eb7e20b3d6932d3afa85134a9bb5e85ac809fe0b", "source_hash": "0beb28f15836c7e8fa7e46284832663e846bd3affc18cc56abae09c31e1f0251", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5eb9e649edbfe949f20b56cbac0b41b675425391a24aaaf31a3eeb5dcb257ab0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}