{"doc_id": "doc64330", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The first Christmas cards were commissioned by Sir Henry Cole and illustrated by John Callcott Horsley in London on 1st May 1843. The central picture showed three generations of a family raising a toast to the card's recipient: on either side were scenes of charity, with food and clothing being given to the poor. Allegedly the image of the family drinking wine together proved controversial, but the idea was shrewd: Cole had helped introduce the Penny Post three years earlier. Two batches totaling 2,050 cards were printed and sold that year for a shilling each.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2066772469, "similarity": 0.986922406277245, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6bcd91d67596b33ece1cc2c2bfff4debff9a2b61a36a7229e5f1a82f61aa2870", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Sir Henry Cole", "matched_aliases": ["Sir Henry Cole"], "query_id": "test1831", "question_hash": "240634f9fd5fb0bccfbf8f7c500c87b14a36abfef2fdd34910f9f54e68536e1e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "880835f64a85991b05f4eebaecca91c5d4139fccf007621fce330612fe51f61e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1240088781, "similarity": 0.20508474576271185, "source_content_hash": "6fb61444dcf0800d0e6b678c91ed046130e0287a76fa51bc0ad0d78bcb6996cc", "source_hash": "966da008921a1bc9e39681ff45857aebcdde6ec7c5d699ed8a0d990d3acbd146", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9f8480b03f38f99ce32a472677fd3c65785725a507cdf2eb01e1f7efdfee955d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc64580", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "4a2c24317ae9315ad62ece5332a02b184770f8af11e7ff62c763544154d8222f", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "Amycus Carrow", "matched_aliases": ["Amycus Carrow"], "query_id": "test1837", "question_hash": "b0e7998c039b64c04c7f65a4777a7b6c81c28a0dbda9704f28e17699799ea751", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9b0dc15fa44a7decca8a095153655ff00e63e575a6c0353a08b87c6c4b3ab97e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 253242396, "similarity": 0.7180851063829787, "source_content_hash": "f3d678fb1c5a465dba19c57b53b60e24dc48cfe7056098f12d8866eab2972e0b", "source_hash": "7adf1297f1dfbb8c603c54cb94befc26830dbbc0d99eb5cfab14922b070e6bd9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c16ffae0b1dc3ed7322a7610442713645ee6f0d0aa8061da60dd1a335a671f10", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc64765", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The location of the Super Bowl is chosen by the NFL well in advance, usually three to five years before the game. Cities place bids to host a Super Bowl and are evaluated in terms of stadium renovation and their ability to host.[43][48] In 2014, a document listing the specific requirements of Super Bowl hosts was leaked, giving a clear list of what was required for a Super Bowl host.[49] Much of the cost of the Super Bowl is to be assumed by the host community, although some costs are enumerated within the requirements to be assumed by the NFL. Some of the host requirements include:", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1547589278, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1f9891dfc72270244b74aeda1a917454de70cdbf7dc3ff710aa454ead22470df", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "The NFL owners", "matched_aliases": ["the NFL"], "query_id": "test1839", "question_hash": "4d2ad8099df93b180f04ee9900646b4e8f17cbac0250393f7a800f9ec198ce5d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5e6e983c4caee84f793d58c2355f15deac221118191adbfab5d0e5b54583688d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 715264112, "similarity": 0.6884862653419053, "source_content_hash": "f1d9111693e46b49412ec4753475be6d31b781a02b26edf9c483ca123e51c607", "source_hash": "8ecd10b6bcca93df934a4a008114c8d82d9790197571b3758b57f2abd3aa2b86", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1218d0750e56fd27e5c6f4a7d76e90e16c759d11831aadc264b39ac2bb951f19", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc64766", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The NFL owners meet to make a selection on the site, usually three to five years prior to the event. In 2007, NFL commissioner Roger Goodell suggested that a Super Bowl might be played in London, perhaps at Wembley Stadium.[51] The game has never been played in a region that lacks an NFL franchise; seven Super Bowls have been played in Los Angeles, but none were held there in the 21-year period when the league had no team in the area.[citation needed] New Orleans, the site of the 2013 Super Bowl, invested more than $1 billion in infrastructure improvements in the years leading up to the game.[52]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1852423788, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "eb0999e4196e002d35aa080d1c2197839a8984e80f14abdd2caf9555a44d770a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "The NFL owners", "matched_aliases": ["The NFL owners", "the NFL"], "query_id": "test1839", "question_hash": "4d2ad8099df93b180f04ee9900646b4e8f17cbac0250393f7a800f9ec198ce5d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3d5f2758b34f5e6cd06e9a6a68fc354773a92f52415ee8fe294beba0c2b1e275", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1395290374, "similarity": 0.12849162011173185, "source_content_hash": "33ebc34d3fa4385d103cb5b380e3ab0bb45c4d9e0aea6aa4296f8efd650499f7", "source_hash": "433bb90cbbe59373b3ec03a22141578ec58ef1c3d9855cbd6584fdf673814110", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5239326eac61b312e0d97c83cdc160c5d77019814e2370353d2ee7be1f4b2a73", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc64877", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "G. Callen is a fictional character in the show NCIS: Los Angeles portrayed by Chris O'Donnell. He is an NCIS Special Agent in Charge, and the senior agent assigned to the Office of Special Projects. O'Donnell made his first appearance during NCIS' sixth season episode \"Legend (Part 1)\".", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1752233357, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "G. Callen (born: Grisha Alekandrovich Nikolaev) is a fictional character in the show NCIS: Los Angeles portrayed by Chris O'Donnell. He is an NCIS Special Agent in Charge, and the senior agent assigned to the Office of Special Projects. O'Donnell made his first appearance during NCIS' sixth season episode \"Legend (Part 1)\".", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1626155220, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "aeb8a3ab91496a2ee386fde7477dc74753eabaa8ccdf4efcfa0b7716935c6e9e", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Grisha", "matched_aliases": ["Grisha"], "query_id": "test1843", "question_hash": "c4a0b3d8732be7d3a7aeeb7204e2b2f79e46e78d6db259fdb67316a4d5c9dd14", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "cd325d6f06b02314698202afc58a16ee53621a560b73d8d1caf272c64825b836", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1857010953, "similarity": 0.39867109634551495, "source_content_hash": "6bd33174027d5883649849f7f2d437498922473f93114e1ed29f1312a60d9ce3", "source_hash": "cef0c45a15ea774f1ae7d740ead54045cce84f2658bf6c85130e8e62933f28eb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3e31b288680ed924f65cf8272ea3272e8d58c8e5d49ea9a61cae5c4bf791c7a8", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verif