{"doc_id": "doc65071", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "During the Great Depression, popcorn was fairly inexpensive at 5–10 cents a bag and became popular. Thus, while other businesses failed, the popcorn business thrived and became a source of income for many struggling farmers, including the Redenbacher family, namesake of the famous popcorn brand. During World War II, sugar rations diminished candy production, and Americans compensated by eating three times as much popcorn as they had before.[8] The snack was popular at theaters, much to the initial displeasure of many of the theater owners, who thought it distracted from the films. Their minds eventually changed, however, and in 1938 a Midwestern theater owner named Glen W. Dickson installed popcorn machines in the lobbies of his theaters. The venture was a financial success, and the trend soon spread.[5]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 975774826, "similarity": 0.9975490196078431, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d9426a58d2bdfda306467c81e2bafba02baf61a6020a02dea12f4bde17f8efd7", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Glen W. Dickson", "matched_aliases": ["Glen W. Dickson"], "query_id": "test1849", "question_hash": "ce49f184d01a444447eea0f150afa9b4ffcfe66b63fa4a824108802c2c07e079", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b806873711c909c3d2b54164259706b0cb5e1ee878e22f9a7fbb1c0834a9df83", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1120905059, "similarity": 0.28135048231511256, "source_content_hash": "a6d7747f1ebae9c8d880438259d59c53fb859a51a55d58dd84bcae3c3858fe3c", "source_hash": "a258a003fbbf6d5966aedbd4f516d11ecdf9a4e0a4ac820366dc94bcd186d2b9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3d30c1b058f67906773fff8932f5f1ad67ba9dd557aabf6822009b58ca1b9314", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc65122", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "External threats closely shaped the course of the Revolution. The Revolutionary Wars beginning in 1792 ultimately featured French victories that facilitated the conquest of the Italian Peninsula, the Low Countries and most territories west of the Rhine â€\" achievements that had eluded previous French governments for centuries. Internally, popular agitation radicalised the Revolution significantly, culminating in the rise of Maximilien Robespierre and the Jacobins. The dictatorship imposed by the Committee of Public Safety during the Reign of Terror, from 1793 until 1794, established price controls on food and other items, abolished slavery in French colonies abroad, dechristianised society through the creation of a new calendar and the expulsion of religious figures, and secured the borders of the new republic from its enemies. Large numbers of civilians were executed by revolutionary tribunals during the Terror, with estimates ranging from 16,000 to 40,000. After the Thermidorian Reaction, an executive council known as the Directory assumed control of the French state in 1795. The rule of the Directory was characterised by suspended elections, debt repudiations, financial instability, persecutions against the Catholic clergy, and significant military conquests abroad. Dogged by charges of corruption, the Directory collapsed in a coup led by Napoleon Bonaparte in 1799. Napoleon, who became the hero of the Revolution through his popular military campaigns, went on to establish the Consulate and later the First Empire, setting the stage for a wider array of global conflicts in the Napoleonic Wars.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1408260565, "similarity": 0.9975384615384615, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b156cc8a7fa7cf63cda0297509469483e8f477122594ace9cdad8870fe7c94d4", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Napoleon", "matched_aliases": ["Napoleon", "Napoleon Bonaparte"], "query_id": "test1852", "question_hash": "1d2d1635821a7517fbeb527a9025ebe2e94ff3bc0444ee6ec6262a3bd841e69e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "59e11f840422edea89428de7fc57e280380de090fc3c39155cf934f6dde93424", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 76556353, "similarity": 0.17738791423001948, "source_content_hash": "53f7fb58a5529237caa3dc64135942664f87b2b5742f8ac9d89c4f112e66343d", "source_hash": "d35d4bb29c5777b47243ccd770205b7625edb81b0fed6d0569eb59d640315233", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "f048b72659657fd173221cd44d893dbf6f4481fd2c694207735a9e24a74fd518", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
