{"doc_id": "doc65389", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"A White Sport Coat (and a Pink Carnation)\" is a 1957 country and western song with words and music both written by Marty Robbins. It was recorded on January 25, 1957, and released on the Columbia Records label, over a month later, on March 4.[1] The arranger and recording session conductor was Ray Conniff, an in-house conductor/arranger at Columbia. Robbins had demanded to have Conniff oversee the recording after his earlier hit, \"Singing the Blues\", had been quickly eclipsed on the charts by Guy Mitchell's cover version scored and conducted by Conniff in October, 1956.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 256992037, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b42e510e169a27c733276ee1e5a556c14a4fe6a3693cb36589c07c6988f8a02c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Marty Robbins", "matched_aliases": ["Marty Robbins"], "query_id": "test1856", "question_hash": "22f623dfb9e10b3c02d843189936f8129818e411a0046700dc3b70370f0772ff", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "bf47483f43e1db350db44ee34dbd8f78984327129db8205562708c17346ff478", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2076649126, "similarity": 0.4939870490286771, "source_content_hash": "d7100c4d891b9c2cbd2964001e06d257df2094428c84e9d9e4d52322dc8fd664", "source_hash": "3040633a7cae7c3c49abde3819ae3f9d4a661a2cee588eb3bccb2ec1ad56c703", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0117d4cc70286a40e416146c3d88d77a656b16807af19f7944bf871f89baab35", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc65395", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The song was released in 1977, following several other hits from The Stranger including \"Just the Way You Are\", \"Movin' Out (Anthony's Song)\" and \"Only the Good Die Young\". Musically, Joel has said that he was influenced by Gordon Lightfoot and his mellow acoustic guitar ballads. It is a love song that Joel wrote for his then wife, Elizabeth Weber. Elizabeth had taken over management of Joel's career, and was able to put his financial affairs in order after Joel had signed some bad deals and contracts. She was a tough and savvy negotiator who could \"wound with her eyes\" or \"steal like a thief\", but would \"never give in\". Because of her tough-as-nails negotiating style, many business adversaries thought she was \"unfeminine,\" but to Joel, she was always a woman.[3] The two eventually divorced in 1982.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1493704931, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "52a6603644d7bbd683816da47a9b43776cfe6b25f6c5d2beedb6590ee996a392", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Billy Joel", "matched_aliases": ["Joel"], "query_id": "test1857", "question_hash": "bd179800196992ccb9617744872093617a6547179b0a678ef58f5f31cd33ae93", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f9d85584d3468dccc7bedc88d93c4e4dd53460785980452f53eaf68e6e91fdf1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1382801167, "similarity": 0.5506849315068493, "source_content_hash": "8e995020ee7f86528a5e836fb57423e73fe9c7c020252eb165f989f36b6a3363", "source_hash": "f0b63edede655396b7567d0a2986d171e3b91fcb025f562b05cec6b3f615f1c3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "8471eb957cc0370d0f05ffe608200355ecd9b043dfa4968df42ae6a2bfbde9f0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc65432", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "8d4067ac3d32ce13539a70b7cdb9fae7331e16fa1dc681dbd80ec7f7bf666985", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "at IBM", "matched_aliases": ["at IBM"], "query_id": "test1859", "question_hash": "fa713e4418201aa944f28924585ff005caa4b676893a63f99f131ead94c807d3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "94f985e316c167f57df404c4fa8d248eca9bd87d99ec9bda3ca9a053e3a8285e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1466885514, "similarity": 0.7406199021207178, "source_content_hash": "97ff42f31f85e4ee476b0ff118b66280db9691adc001c5d91ab05240a1a52cee", "source_hash": "37a6b6eb9b8bd4bf804566ddd50085192da84abd9b96c2ea344d64ba72b649ad", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3ca6eca30a338e330c0bb55a386afc6555e442ff89671924aff73c7e87ea9c3f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc65502", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Matthew Lyn Lillard (born January 24, 1970) is an American actor, voice actor, director, and producer. He is best known for portraying Chip in Serial Mom (1994), Stu in Scream (1996), Stevo in SLC Punk! (1998), Jerry Conlaine in Without a Paddle (2004) and Shaggy Rogers in both Scooby-Doo (2002) and Scooby-Doo 2: Monsters Unleashed (2004). In animation, he has been the current voice of Shaggy since veteran actor Casey Kasem retired from the role.[1]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 333634081, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Matthew Lyn Lillard, born January 24, 1970, is an American actor, voice actor, director, and producer. He is best known for portraying Chip in Serial Mom (1994), Stu in Scream (1996), Stevo in SLC Punk! (1998), Jerry Conlaine in Without a Paddle (2004), and Shaggy Rogers in both Scooby-Doo (2002) and Scooby-Doo 2: Monsters Unleashed (2004). In animation, he has been the current voice of Shaggy since veteran actor Casey Kasem retired from the role.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 226391586, "similarity": 0.9889380530973452, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "480d381fdd1beec33d8cbd42ae16e3e22d99a4cb775985f041d1f9cb9b34aeb4", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Matthew Lyn Lillard", "matched_aliases": ["Matthew Lyn Lillard"], "query_id": "test1861", "question_hash": "eda80937c0daacee33c68871ff36f091e85c2cd5b689fe8582d6af6e8ff1c171", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8f1708a6beebd7cdbd1fef0a1a05c0686866b82b1be8ee55a6c50357833a8d83", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1589583063, "similarity": 0.13008130081300814, "source_content_hash": "8b6d2589fa70246f69643b022fe6f0f43bb6ff3dcd61c39d30a226222558b21f", "source_hash": "7c65bf0dfc9c01fd1495ffa321ee2b5fc273783c201402058338e1fe5cd0cbf8", "target_ans