{"doc_id": "doc66608", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Little Red Riding Hood\" is a European fairy tale about a young girl and a Big Bad Wolf. Its origins can be traced back to the 10th century by several European folk tales, including one from Italy called The False Grandmother, which was later written among others by Italo Calvino in the Italian Folktales collection. The best known versions were written by Charles Perrault and the Brothers Grimm. The story has been changed considerably in various retellings and subjected to numerous modern adaptations and readings. Other names for the story are: \"Little Red Ridinghood\", \"Little Red Cap\" or simply \"Red Riding Hood\". It is number 333 in the Aarne-Thompson classification system for folktales.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1705378617, "similarity": 0.9577464788732394, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "19eff1bdc0f1a56b3d4f1c6da94b214c129b181a40edff620f20a6f30a5dd6fb", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Charles Perrault", "matched_aliases": ["Charles Perrault"], "query_id": "test1896", "question_hash": "7214e859b27e382117f1525f908a53493cd57d783c16a31764f31388cff78fde", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1a763d4f2ee39a59d89753ed75ca96f4cd887b3938a87b342f477782e28e6744", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 595524154, "similarity": 0.21296296296296297, "source_content_hash": "2451664800a97e9e611fca5cda1b787da7aa6a30ce70cf930b0c53fbdabab89a", "source_hash": "6f4d575dfea6df754ce5e5ef79ce982c9038eefe525b5eccfd759310b21b0bea", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "831f805e7c34b00366c94ea99bcf5f601dbb962adbffa3e176eaec1eac3246ef", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc66621", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The earliest known printed version of the story was known as *Le Petit Chaperon Rouge* and may have had its origins in 17th-century French folklore. It was included in the collection *Tales and Stories of the Past with Morals*, titled *Tales of Mother Goose* (Histoires et contes du temps passé, avec des moralités. Contes de ma mère l'Oye), in 1697, by Charles Perrault. As the title implies, this version is both more sinister and more overtly moralized than the later ones. The redness of the hood, which has been given symbolic significance in many interpretations of the tale, was a detail introduced by Perrault.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 99795323, "similarity": 0.9656301145662848, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ebcf3e0a429cd6ebc56fb6de09936c00c190f95848191bf49d759e8ac00000ed", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Charles Perrault", "matched_aliases": ["Charles Perrault"], "query_id": "test1896", "question_hash": "7214e859b27e382117f1525f908a53493cd57d783c16a31764f31388cff78fde", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "604743af9caeff1465d85a2d2cb00b1560dd1c8f936791183ded16aad29da9a0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1242611252, "similarity": 0.19193548387096773, "source_content_hash": "6232182be0130c9f8c513e5ca011a78bfbdd9023a4fef0a3d7f6885537c0e211", "source_hash": "eacf6b6860371e91ed658a3a0bee97672ac323350aca9464423aa0361342bb2f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5e6f7c753459f87029bae072f49523daa17278a28d0b8f5a21745476d60aae7a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator