{"doc_id": "doc67058", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Premiering in early 2007, the music video for \"Lips of an Angel\" was directed by Shaun Silva and largely follows the narrative of the song's lyrics, focusing on a late night phone call between the raconteur (Austin Winkler) and his former lover (Emmanuelle Chriqui).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 421654431, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Premiering in early 2007, the music video for \"Lips of an Angel\" was directed by Shaun Silva and largely follows the narrative of the song's lyrics, focusing on a late night phone call between the raconteur (Austin Winkler) and his former lover (Emmanuelle Chriqui).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1708511142, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "b80270d56a3816b8b2332ae45cc99d16b8d0b295d7bb2d3e27caa1448b8302b3", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Emmanuelle Chriqui", "matched_aliases": ["Emmanuelle Chriqui"], "query_id": "test1912", "question_hash": "a7b7a63aa0aeaa5168db7ef3042560be18af2f130e96a3deb273914efd10aea1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "59c94acac025a6b36dcf950fa36b0b0a8de336f73958e59b9f53952ee3062d13", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 869925780, "similarity": 0.9090909090909091, "source_content_hash": "750461ef716810cc00e81baef5b57ac7c0ec949f883c71e6fd89f1ced2726b0a", "source_hash": "0e38b01c0b0c25c815eb614c47887ac728602041be870e4c83dd0db34af4ed2c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "15ea8f07748d54162d4cc8a5d25c21916f9ce2b55d8f05d4918a93938efe1622", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67059", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Swine influenza is an infection caused by any one of several types of swine influenza viruses. Swine influenza virus (SIV) or swine-origin influenza virus (S-OIV) is any strain of the influenza family of viruses that is endemic in pigs. As of 2009, the known SIV strains include influenza C and the subtypes of influenza A known as H1N1, H1N2, H2N1, H3N1, H3N2, and H2N3.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 93813900, "similarity": 0.9959731543624161, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2e4fc66db60dcceba01c6ac0e35b82040ba6b2fff3b3444402ec4ef142022e62", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Pig", "matched_aliases": ["pigs"], "query_id": "test1913", "question_hash": "6cd2d3aa8f204fda4d7443f8db16c50beada74f36536c8ae0befcdcf56507153", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "580c3c7bf6d7fb3795869a38629a4d8c9cd14572648a0db80a78864d47c92f98", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 642222373, "similarity": 0.5310015898251192, "source_content_hash": "0037dc8a26ace2fa2651ac4e8b15b596505b3608464bf0b1d16afe5875baf72f", "source_hash": "29abc9a64d8fa4ba4cf70d68669684016f20b9dd2e3df239bb9f10047901256f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7acd377d9411c794df4c56e4a107f93243ffbb92bc6d57d30686b1cd98e4f07c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67119", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The phylogenetic origin of the flu virus that caused the 2009 pandemics can be traced before 1918. Around 1918, the ancestral virus, of avian origin, crossed the species boundaries and infected humans as human H1N1. The same phenomenon took place soon after in America, where the human virus was infecting pigs; it led to the emergence of the H1N1 swine strain, which later became the classic swine flu.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1129663098, "similarity": 0.9734299516908212, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7a586cc33add821400842ef730db567b4bae992f5b8c0c259734d35a03551631", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Pig", "matched_aliases": ["pigs"], "query_id": "test1913", "question_hash": "6cd2d3aa8f204fda4d7443f8db16c50beada74f36536c8ae0befcdcf56507153", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "497cc59ef61c61bac47e2e6fe8314faecbe57f0b5d4cd2e0ddbc1550d4eccac1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1014637899, "similarity": 0.1396011396011396, "source_content_hash": "5f68201f794b727365a01650fcf2acf6ea7bb483dadc3689d5909e33fd4e5379", "source_hash": "90ccc4fff7b76dcd1789ff91ce40decf7dfc9d4f6f116ce60cdacae88f08f972", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "386ad40fa3e65e7dfd6f10c6e76d938862dc206507e48582ff2f276e3d6b58e9", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67139", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "560dd2a0110dc14840423bc1022207d27ac1c3d61158ca164bdf3b65d9856b0c", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "optical smoke detector", "matched_aliases": ["optical smoke detector"], "query_id": "test1914", "question_hash": "aaff85101193622743189ffd37ed7dd7fe624b1fdd4457e2ce953dbd1449c920", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e13771fc853c69b0de43f9f0a54f6eaf5176e5dd557af7be310aaaf6d914cfbb", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1137221172, "similarity": 0.10698244181298489, "source_content_hash": "e517b54a58657c1ac2284d64ef2be69ec0c412b4546c688e12c31f8469798201", "source_hash": "57caf022449870f9ff7fcda404a9cbb34f2878e0bd4f6f2158178a260265f2d3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "09ea5cd42d5ea67ad60ecec0e24c536f9761496737afd8188eb31f732aa97fab", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67192", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The period typically called Romantic varies greatly between different countries and different artistic media or areas of thought. Margaret Drabble described it in literature as taking place \"roughly between 1770 and 1848\",[23] and few dates much earlier than 1770 will be found. In English literature, M. H. Abrams placed it between 1789, or 1798, this latter a very typical view, and about 1830, perhaps a little later than some other critics.[24] Others have proposed 1780–1830.[25] In other fields and other countries the period denominated as Romantic can be considerably different; musical Romanticism, for example, is generally regarded as only having ceased as a major artistic force as late as 1910, but in an extreme extension the Four Last Songs of Richard Strauss are described stylistically as \"Late Romantic\" and were composed in 1946–48.[26] However, in most fields the Romantic Period is said to be over by about 1850, or earlier.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 336463945, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Romantic period is a broad era in art and literature that spans a wide range of national boundaries and artistic disciplines. While literary historians like Margaret Drabble suggest it began around 1770 and concluded by 1848, other scholars such as M. H. Abrams have pinpointed the start to 1789 or 1798. A more comprehensive range often cited in the field is 1780 to 1830. Although specific dates vary significantly across different countries and media, general consensus suggests this movement was largely active from the late 18th century until the early 19th century, with the end date frequently falling around 1830 or slightly later.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1362788488, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "a923553672eff6b36f5bcadfa8d202cb5c3519027cd6a107572fffa0b17291c2", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "1780–1830", "matched_aliases": ["1780–1830"], "query_id": "test1915", "question_hash": "6881fa7019ec0be26bda48f8238fa5cb6e654bd15e2fa46bfa0f7059985f9351", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b2c97657a9bf1669d9420fab52f5929990415965b3beb4eed93e18f55966e44e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 509515934, "similarity": 0.9324124321657622, "source_content_hash": "f3929a143811101ad9ad4cdf0f64d455732997d7ca04d3a921e9af95265d127b", "source_hash": "03022911607d915ea0459a78cff2197e61557f48fe4671f86d94d71600cab4f1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4893ecff8a7bf6d4a208ad8f5bf9b0cfcfd2475ec1176bb96ae7b157cd7cc8bb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67309", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "A Thousand Years is a song by American singer-songwriter Christina Perri and David Hodges. It is taken from the album The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn — Part 1: Original Motion Picture Soundtrack. The song serves as the second single from the album. The song was released as a digital download on October 18, 2011 worldwide. Perri re-recorded the song with vocals from Steve Kazee for The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn — Part 2: Original Motion Picture Soundtrack titled A Thousand Years, Pt. 2.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1186811867, "similarity": 0.9949647532729103, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2a31e8f9f24f8aa574c9d3a9f6815cfa46399defe2e6ec56d84e84b94c6abdd1", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Christina Perri", "matched_aliases": ["Christina Perri"], "query_id": "test1917", "question_hash": "fa44dc7341787b2186be97323342c1ae1c4ee234b5a36eaf1553203419bc833e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "7552184fd81c9d06c5a693ba31e3a8e4768c404782e073786feed8d41b8cf00f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 138009276, "similarity": 0.5353645266594124, "source_content_hash": "ebeed649f195575c98fa50dfbb858e42d42902fd99182237e424e1bb97d87a83", "source_hash": "6468eb5e2dc32d21cd68e1435402920dc5148ffaca7a0ba869f49616e5ffbde7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "f775ef89d7c1079c92121f5de05df3fa348e96f4d7958ab37a1c1516f1266cca", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67317", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Vincenzo Peruggia (October 8, 1881 – October 8, 1925) was an Italian thief, most famous for stealing the Mona Lisa on 21 August 1911. Born in Dumenza, Varese, Italy, he died in Saint-Maur-des-Fossés, France.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2082565527, "similarity": 0.9928057553956835, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "17f31d3e51b8036792629bf594725c8fa38f7d5348cf8e490526ee2d4a656e70", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Vincenzo Peruggia", "matched_aliases": ["Vincenzo Peruggia"], "query_id": "test1918", "question_hash": "e6b2375568de14b77d36f5a490589c54d49e0db9ced782fc0448f5db92025a40", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "722ad22741f52ce67706c7532c0b81d1b6d98e68df197ee6ef925ba050435d82", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 645986502, "similarity": 0.43253968253968256, "source_content_hash": "d6dc7d4911e343ed5ad313f5b1f3e8d536b6f0c7b05b7b3b518fe18a4a05fca3", "source_hash": "7e623f63424726a6dcaae0502b700b1fcaf76e37f3df5ec8575193fbb395b6e1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "64e683906dc93968628718797745acda4afa890f91dbf6da9948c58132a64c37", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
