{"doc_id": "doc71583", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Despite warnings by Jeremiah and others of the pro-Babylonian party, Zedekiah revolted against Babylon and entered into an alliance with Pharaoh Hophra. Nebuchadnezzar returned, defeated the Egyptians, and again besieged Jerusalem, resulting in the city's destruction in 587 BCE. Nebuchadnezzar destroyed the city wall and the Temple, together with the houses of the most important citizens. Zedekiah and his sons were captured, the sons were executed in front of Zedekiah, who was then blinded and taken to Babylon with many others (Jer 52:10â€\"11). Judah became a Babylonian province, called Yehud, putting an end to the independent Kingdom of Judah. (Because of the missing years in the Jewish calendar, rabbinic sources place the date of the destruction of the First Temple at 3338 HC (423 BCE)[12] or 3358 HC (403 BCE)).[13]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1337088010, "similarity": 0.9987937273823885, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "381de6a70b731564e3fc2637e2888b928c10b086fafaeca706446c96338d742b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Nebuchadnezzar", "matched_aliases": ["Nebuchadnezzar"], "query_id": "test2054", "question_hash": "d0a40dff3f9a712aaeb169b56d5135cb401575606d82e3684fafb4924dd7a3ca", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "889ee55b3917ac0cbf54b2468ea4de36a3f37f7eb80ea5dca4988e3d49631bac", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1586652522, "similarity": 0.10432852386237514, "source_content_hash": "4b1515809c99d2c2cc5940fbcc259ecb2af31dd2a60dc4bc3e3f1fab6e640879", "source_hash": "b1b7180be97746d33a0f9eb219d6635909e849792800b83de6a10485f2e70083", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0585798a9f98cba633b5d3fb534fe87d19415411c8fb8043c1ef9d526264f7fd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc71604", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Investment banker Harold Lee is persuaded by his colleagues to do their work while they leave for the weekend. Kumar Patel attends a medical school interview, but intentionally botches it to prevent getting accepted. Harold is attracted to his neighbor, Maria, but is unable to admit his feelings. After smoking marijuana with Kumar, and seeing an advertisement for White Castle, the pair decide to get hamburgers. After traveling to the nearest White Castle in New Brunswick, they find it replaced by \"Burger Shack\" but learn of another White Castle in Cherry Hill.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1878267334, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9b70beed6a88f81d8ac0d29cbf4ba156232cf0e208fbd67303d147b11b091763", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "in Cherry Hill", "matched_aliases": ["in Cherry Hill"], "query_id": "test2055", "question_hash": "f10f7cef7b19cb069bd57e93921d335bdff408cbbf3b64616789b121518371cc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e5f2f476ecd932448a49f6a7f5e308479f5f8d6be49eec301eb2580f59a73810", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 198232119, "similarity": 0.1326829268292683, "source_content_hash": "0b7210a8eac13fc7d08452fa9143cfa6d8a292c8da031f1f9147d386b4a7fed9", "source_hash": "ce17f2cdc5662fad7e03407d86e8d4bf7c679e893c402db0ab8af1e513e10017", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "022c7859aa59a823f79d594d847d8bcbc38614fbc83ef2218ec3e183ea188502", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc71625", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Child Benefit Bill was introduced in 1975 by Barbara Castle, introducing for the first time a universal payment, paid for each child, doubling the number of children within its scope. Like the family allowance, which it replaced, the new benefit was not means tested; an attempt by the Callaghan government to introduce this was thwarted in 1976 when cabinet papers were leaked to the Child Poverty Action Group.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1898209510, "similarity": 0.9952153110047847, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6428723ce69806443081588c7946633d3f70a11b70ce2872b8d44fdba52bbffe", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "1975", "matched_aliases": ["1975"], "query_id": "test2056", "question_hash": "a179b77ee23f9e62c9c8ba08c6b1de5482f6a7f2bb6d46f4f3362d925e298cdd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3327a40c06a589b1d8aedcc5d6283969cc0b33eb9cae21b5978a0e782ed551a2", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 40716228, "similarity": 0.40489432703003336, "source_content_hash": "71f483fb1503e4c9919f04e1c4d6dd566f5f0b1361243392769d280c3f83875a", "source_hash": "891b4b2f0e906f5b7e714bdfbd1fce117ccd88f32352b9cd3cfad48557b257c0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5c776b78e69a6e6dff1c1a9c86b218c6ca12358ba7bc291c4acc98bd5568038c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
