{"doc_id": "doc73690", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The 2011 NBA Finals was the championship series of the National Basketball Association (NBA)'s 2010–11 season, and the conclusion of the season's playoffs. The Western Conference champion Dallas Mavericks defeated the Eastern Conference champion Miami Heat 4 games to 2 to win their first NBA championship. Dallas became the last NBA team from Texas to win its first title, after the Houston Rockets won back-to-back titles in 1994 and 1995, and the San Antonio Spurs won four NBA championships in 1999, 2003, 2005 and 2007, and a fifth one subsequently in 2014; all three Texas NBA teams have now won at least one NBA championship. It was also the first time in four years that the Los Angeles Lakers did not make the Finals, having been swept in the Western Conference semifinals by the eventual champion Dallas Mavericks.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1431311309, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b58e6147c2da4c638a375aa019771f30c9817ff90f1d308cfd38ee6e6723ba6a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Miami Heat", "matched_aliases": ["Miami Heat"], "query_id": "test2119", "question_hash": "5c529a92975d32244582e24cc447ef980eae0b1ffe2366a72c3b1c6fe89ae14a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9aefa8431397fd6aab83951dd5f5259c827fdf801eadfb6014435e1983532425", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 293236852, "similarity": 0.09219858156028368, "source_content_hash": "6986e5e810213a11f6aab4589574d2b71680e0b42d1afd76b355ee763fbb21c5", "source_hash": "592a859181cef73e4cdad5eb3b8bec59f6210532e211b88105037bc726a5ae54", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4f93a103831a0d854826cbd4a2be0716237a87e16dc6e636f74e942a392c1f36", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc73719", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Sneaky Pete is an American crime drama series created by David Shore and Bryan Cranston. The series follows Marius JosipoviÄ‡ (Giovanni Ribisi), a released convict who adopts the identity of his cell mate, Pete Murphy, in order to avoid his past life. The series also stars Marin Ireland, Shane McRae, Libe Barer, Michael Drayer, Peter Gerety, and Margo Martindale. The pilot debuted on August 7, 2015, and was followed by a full series order that September.[1] Shore left the project in early 2016 and was replaced by Graham Yost, who served as executive producer and showrunner for the remaining nine episodes.[2] The first season premiered in its entirety on January 13, 2017, exclusively on Amazon Video.[3] On January 19, 2017, Amazon announced that Sneaky Pete had been renewed for a second season,[4] which was released on March 9, 2018.[5]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1888071798, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ee427fbb2016c8dd8805e03a4dbf855f9e6b46465d414fedcefa391cbf58e403", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Giovanni Ribisi", "matched_aliases": ["Giovanni Ribisi"], "query_id": "test2120", "question_hash": "d1b294803d1a31d6ef1b696d05cf1da92035c8a68164650a5b45400c7f8c5f69", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "2fb2558d03a7804962377f0fbcd899895bf977201c5f603c03ebce3cc44a29d5", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1054673797, "similarity": 0.40171990171990174, "source_content_hash": "65a4a836491f49a6e2a97684ea97165bc5f3edff8902f8e051e6353ea0447a91", "source_hash": "af36e7c4183c71560b92c223a96044ad7dc1e3ab7c5c87c6494a81f5e61a1e14", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6b1a30e8a8b4b9121800538b1e56fb5f702ecd39111f4f54daec653875dbec53", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_