{"doc_id": "doc73914", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Alabama is nicknamed the Yellowhammer State, after the state bird. Alabama is also known as the \"Heart of Dixie\" and the Cotton State. The state tree is the longleaf pine, and the state flower is the camellia. Alabama's capital is Montgomery. The largest city by population is Birmingham, which has long been the most industrialized city; the largest city by land area is Huntsville. The oldest city is Mobile, founded by French colonists in 1702 as the capital of French Louisiana.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 342106658, "similarity": 0.9927909371781668, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9b636bf97772970b56095497868b0fd698fcbab533f771709a3f6e2a265b2b70", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Montgomery", "matched_aliases": ["Montgomery"], "query_id": "test2129", "question_hash": "7f64340d9df9563a196c37459f8ac235327b1857a4686c9e8277a1daa22c3dc7", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "9d165ec649c4db9ac49793cf5868fbfe306b7fb3612dc36c70e4d338f8775423", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1586462333, "similarity": 0.35920177383592017, "source_content_hash": "ecc1471b4c4eac363b2c9b3cb2ba24a696f19fc135410481de3faa72e0e80d0f", "source_hash": "407d3f63dab6a992c3c9a391bc6748fa079404d59d1eedcf126db58cb656f5d2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3a90f661a4e9f1d12e88c26c536f53ff37fa3c225eb7e9da96331d5487d3a203", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc74071", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The origin and history of coffee dates back to the 10th century, and possibly earlier with a number of reports and legends surrounding its first use. The native (undomesticated) origin of coffee is thought to have been Ethiopia. The earliest substantiated evidence of either coffee drinking or knowledge of the coffee tree is from the 15th century, in the Sufi monasteries of Yemen. By the 16th century, it had reached the rest of the Middle East, South India (Coorg), Persia, Turkey, Horn of Africa, and northern Africa. Coffee then spread to the Balkans, Italy and to the rest of Europe, to South East Asia and then to America.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 224604813, "similarity": 0.995253164556962, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "022485c85379a81ce67ea5b94f9a963946e63123a93c7384769e1a44f70f409d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "15th century", "matched_aliases": ["15th century"], "query_id": "test2130", "question_hash": "ec47ca021f92c36fd70d852db9c8713d8a54dffc82d0f37d2410d25a5bd76da9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a8b6c235625c7e98d4786e828710d1bfe9a3f221398093f8a748332dac565e0f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 561409400, "similarity": 0.04554079696394687, "source_content_hash": "630f7531e0f9cf3051605422833463e2e93673f3c5d45d0b5e625a28fe2087c5", "source_hash": "4cde7f059af05e91c7ec78342e1c9ec793756c3a92e02279b8e99d1775832c28", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "29ab5445886e3cd7448897e91c5980948c9f8cd497fd43df5d09d6982e7d8898", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validat