{"doc_id": "doc76875", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Republic of Tecala, where most of Proof of Life is set, is a fictional South American country. Tecala has long been the scene of an internal conflict between its government forces and the Liberation Army of Tecala (ELT). The ELT was originally a Marxist guerrilla group supported by the Soviet Union, but after the Soviet Union's dissolution in 1991, the ELT's primary source of funding fell through, and they began kidnapping people for ransom to fund their operations. A map seen in the film is that of Ecuador. The country's capital Quito was chosen along with the eastern jungle and the nearby city of Baños de Agua Santa in the Ecuadorian Andes.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 816273203, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f497e06181aa287610b47f4cb1966e97d56fc0c122ae531d6acd81a92e4baeb3", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "The Republic of Tecala", "matched_aliases": ["The Republic of Tecala"], "query_id": "test2207", "question_hash": "2852efa75b046ededec0364d26b627d17cd36e443865e1a3b14cf3b09795c901", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "175fe6a2e7b12a60f9d6fa64eedf1d9b6a7161bc32839cc3323b7c06c4ad965b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 996355779, "similarity": 0.17843289371605897, "source_content_hash": "0c5650a4f82026f76f3e5569109f51239090f719b4fcfea733c24c02737991ed", "source_hash": "7b5570d424933430988dde333f0c69648a32725f58da141a8e7d59df927cbeaf", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "078e732c51436b8c8e9c4a3d597c214e4aa697ed1da44d50dc7ca5a908326966", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc76971", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "G. Sankara Kurup, (3 June 1901, Nayathode, Kingdom of Cochin (now in Ernakulam district, Kerala, India) â€“ 2 February 1978, Vappalassery, Angamaly, Ernakulam district, Kerala), better known as Mahakavi G (The Great Poet G), was the first winner of the Jnanpith Award, India's highest literary award.[1][2] He won the prize in 1965 for his collection of poems in Malayalam Odakkuzhal (The Bamboo Flute, 1950). With part of the prize money he established the literary award Odakkuzhal in 1968. He was also the recipient of the Soviet Land Nehru Award, in 1967, and the Padma Bhushan in 1968.[3] His poetry collection Viswadarshanam won the Kerala Sahitya Akademi Award in 1961 and Kendra Sahitya Akademi Award in 1963.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1337101585, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "G. Sankara Kurup, (3 June 1901, Nayathode, Kingdom of Cochin (now in Ernakulam district, Kerala, India) â€“ 2 February 1978, Vappalassery, Angamaly, Ernakulam district, Kerala), better known as Mahakavi G (The Great Poet G), was the first winner of the Jnanpith Award, India's highest literary award.[1][2] He won the prize in 1965 for his collection of poems in Malayalam Odakkuzhal (The Bamboo Flute, 1950). With part of the prize money he established the literary award Odakkuzhal in 1968. He was also the recipient of the Soviet Land Nehru Award, in 1967, and the Padma Bhushan in 1968.[3] His poetry collection Viswadarshanam won the Kerala Sahitya Akademi Award in 1961 and Kendra Sahitya Akademi Award in 1963.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 207442369, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "87b63ac11c63181a69f652b60795d5170e755279967b5aed9feacd84feca9307", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Malayalam", "matched_aliases": ["Malayalam"], "query_id": "test2213", "question_hash": "9001e815204beff8bcfaea581d250da333a9cd6567874f8c856b814ede6e9513", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8b1e7adf93180b929fb6c20ce7aa39405ee6ad93b904617d74dcc105d8d36b36", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 156159907, "similarity": 0.12525667351129363, "source_content_hash": "e9bfcbd5a4565429ea4d5f19e3b021db233818bea19ac426040da6090529d46f", "source_hash": "b46ddd0e0006aa40796b3de49b684b5208f2568a7df58bb71baf4395bb44ed51", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6b3f20a4cb7b1aed36a34bceeb0a3d8ec906bde1009dd805288c13828793e3d3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc77026", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Cadbury, formerly Cadbury's, is a British multinational confectionery company wholly owned by Mondelez International (originally Kraft Foods) since 2010. It is the second-largest confectionery brand in the world after Wrigley's.[2] Cadbury is internationally headquartered in Uxbridge, West London, and operates in more than 50 countries worldwide. It is famous for its Dairy Milk chocolate, the Creme Egg and Roses selection box, and many other confectionery products. One of the best-known British brands, in 2013 The Daily Telegraph named Cadbury among Britain's most successful exports.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1290997917, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "432c640a7cda50a85cbf8ea08ab9d02be8d8a7efe7dda732d3bf4cdc6574fca9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "more than 50 countries worldwide", "matched_aliases": ["more than 50 countries worldwide", "more than 50"], "query_id": "test2216", "question_hash": "ed10fa5157c484587a341e7ce26a6f00bc84b46b9ed93bff6987579b78baf44f", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e5fd183e7d4bf8ceeebc2ef32d3d90cea90bb67e8ea72dd903c17ff2cc999e05", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 301010598, "similarity": 0.40913415794481445, "source_content_hash": "8c0bdc4ae63b0559e34f6e89f9134b69a2a80d3933b2c75d6bd65b9a52260602", "source_hash": "c916c72ac4ded6a86a2af2636c4bd608505e6356a516740c8354d156f0cc35c0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "360140dfcd3d3241cbc05559cdbcae8d3dff1d9e083a178a520294df98f7dac4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "