{"doc_id": "doc78010", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The division of Korea between North and South Korea occurred after World War II, ending the Empire of Japan's 35-year rule over Korea in 1945. The United States and the Soviet Union occupied two parts of the country, with the boundary between their zones of control along the 38th parallel.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1629725784, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The division of Korea between North and South Korea occurred after World War II, ending the Empire of Japan's 35-year rule over Korea in 1945. The United States and the Soviet Union occupied two parts of the country, with the boundary between their zones of control along the 38th parallel.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 293341661, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "cb306e71b5deaa0b2a47209e3ff3bc8d86c4bc6aebd86e0f58e1cb32ae06a115", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "1945", "matched_aliases": ["1945"], "query_id": "test2249", "question_hash": "f98bef5afc66f5b275f5b62ff713930d6873e7823fbbd98b978103b30b56b761", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3afb213522cecee5431533b19f4cf9ad80f160ffdef1d87218c2f3cc01440472", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 533779427, "similarity": 0.3037542662116041, "source_content_hash": "a081ce2dcaa43b34bb25902df0012146eb371c0d712e19f567b56c469cf00c36", "source_hash": "a30f5155f3a3af30d45f7c21fb453b392a1568de802e1f313393126ee8ce0785", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a57bd920e6104d49e9c82be347bb4f65c7fcaf66b4fd7afb76052d9ec37fa33e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc78015", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "95c478590321ca600b7d8bb75d7db89c498407a4781c104fa5f82f2f144cf19b", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "1945", "matched_aliases": ["1945", "17 August 1945"], "query_id": "test2249", "question_hash": "f98bef5afc66f5b275f5b62ff713930d6873e7823fbbd98b978103b30b56b761", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8577cc6eb2049755daf6f0d2c19840bf963fb3661bf806a1173f83a79a4437d9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1894090517, "similarity": 0.09355345911949685, "source_content_hash": "808efb1bdc9a00bc2e5d358338d9bec6b58c16183021197e27b3922de576f75c", "source_hash": "a4cb615694c8add71e3e220f9be0cc572fc82cd237b02670ecb3d8d453bad30f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "953c92cffdea856cf5763da9fc0ada16ed696df5365a99ef29e1d70775980fcc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc78173", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "According to the Origination Clause of the United States Constitution, all bills for raising revenue, generally tax bills, must originate in the House of Representatives, similar to the Westminster system requirement that all money bills originate in the lower house. Traditionally, though, appropriation bills also originate in the House of Representatives.[5][6] House appropriations bills begin with \"H.R.\", meaning \"House of Representatives\". In reference to revenue bills, the Constitution also states that the \"Senate may propose or concur with Amendments as on other Bills.\" As with revenue bills, the Senate and House each drafts and considers its own appropriation bill. The Senate then \"cuts-and-pastes,\" substituting the language of its version of a particular appropriation bill for the language of the House bill, then agrees to the bill as amended.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 118471754, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Origination Clause of the United States Constitution mandates that all bills designed to raise revenue must be introduced in the House of Representatives, a rule analogous to the Westminster system for money bills. While this clause specifically governs tax legislation, it also extends to appropriation bills, which traditionally originate in the same chamber. For instance, the House of Representatives introduces these funds-raising measures with the designation \"H.R.\" to signify their status. The Constitution further stipulates that the Senate may propose or concur with amendments to these appropriation bills, ensuring a collaborative process between the two legislative bodies.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 676755498, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "21fdbfe577ccb007b867687d910d66ae150e6c500a1206ca2eeb05f5218095e8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "raising revenue", "matched_aliases": ["raising revenue"], "query_id": "test2252", "question_hash": "7d51077060f2530e9a1789caf23358847abbee070eedcf824a2e383c209616fc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ceb9256487541c1c0f0c1109b42f08f253b1faa86528c2eb98a65c417a10a43c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1978938294, "similarity": 0.43621399176954734, "source_content_hash": "1821b026530ede818178e096c9e98b9849b5b4e8bc49fbb55a8353b07fabc50d", "source_hash": "60dec9c6a89394c9cba72cbf8e6283670dbb81afddd1a5ceb9b7c45f6ed325bc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b5d03fe6324503479ae1100ba3726dbf6b6278e612c92806c969e3e5f40cb414", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc78237", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "As of 2015–16, there were still a significant number of customers who preferred the 4-inch screen size of the iPhone 5S, which remained the second-most popular iPhone after the iPhone 6 and ahead of the iPhone 6S. Apple stated in their event that they sold 30 million 4-inch iPhones in 2015, even as that form factor was succeeded as the flagship iPhone by the redesigned larger display 4.7/5.5-inch iPhone 6 and 6 Plus back in September 2014. Furthermore, the 5 and 5S design was regarded as \"long been the golden child of Apple phone design and a benchmark for phones in general\" (with the 5S's gold finish adding a premium touch to the 5's already well-regarded look), while the succeeding 6 and 6S design was less critically acclaimed as it \"felt a little bit wrong, as though you were holding a slick $650 bar of soap\". The iPhone 5 was described as \"elegance rooted in the way the aluminum and glass work together. It felt streamlined, yet substantial, which is different from iPhone 6, which feels substantial in size alone. Plus, unlike the ubiquitous rounded corners of the 6, iPhone 5 didn't really look like anything else on the market at the time\". However, the iPhone 5/5S design was not suited to scaling up, in contrast to the iPhone 6/6S which could better accommodate the growing consumer trend towards larger screen sizes and indeed spawned the 6/6S Plus phablet models. When Apple discontinued the iPhone 5S, it was replaced by the iPhone SE which outwardly appears almost identical to the 5S even as the SE's internal hardware has been upgraded significantly.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 370429165, "similarity": 0.9955724225173941, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d004a4aaea15cb3098c3a1c69a355318ca30fc7d21896be85d389c39734faeef", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "4 in", "matched_aliases": ["4-inch screen size"], "q