{"doc_id": "doc78737", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The American Civil War was fought in the United States from 1861 to 1865. As a result of the long-standing controversy over slavery, war broke out in April 1861, when Confederate forces attacked Fort Sumter in South Carolina, shortly after U.S. President Abraham Lincoln was inaugurated. The nationalists of the Union proclaimed loyalty to the U.S. Constitution. They faced secessionists of the Confederate States, who advocated for states' rights to expand slavery.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1113317704, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9b01340a295de7c1a708adddae789bd90978c3dae0bc42bbb24f943cab0ddf7a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "nationalists of the Union", "matched_aliases": ["nationalists of the Union"], "query_id": "test2279", "question_hash": "d2bd28e7ba174e90f380a0587e101246d71e5659f49dc2117d6a71b3c1888db3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "daf8c5434e996b7dae17f63c5a72626cfa9d47a19631a51be22df26e2e0d503e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1224714384, "similarity": 0.12074001947419669, "source_content_hash": "f984ed15bc2fa921e698d9337629b7a32f346245a238c030560b707ea7c709b6", "source_hash": "2969e7662aa348e4832cdd98e0899aa822b2f4c53dff6afa4d4f29cac220f2d1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "984d2c9e11cc1e38102555f440ff15dd40d4c4d65cf24562557b8624eddaf9b7", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc78933", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "One of the best-known 18th Dynasty pharaohs is Amenhotep IV, who changed his name to Akhenaten in honor of the Aten, a representation of the Egyptian god, Ra. His exclusive worship of the Aten is often interpreted as history's first instance of monotheism. Akhenaten's wife, Nefertiti, contributed a great deal to his new take on the Egyptian religion. Nefertiti was bold enough to perform rituals to Aten. Akhenaten's religious fervor is cited as the reason why he and his wife were subsequently written out of Egyptian history. Under his reign, in the 14th century BC, Egyptian art flourished under a distinctive style. (See Amarna Period.)", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 962434114, "similarity": 0.9976689976689976, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "456c5a351ed1dc494ddc047b487c0799ab066c891f64561ef35333c9a1deb205", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Aten", "matched_aliases": ["Aten"], "query_id": "test2281", "question_hash": "166fda9a8c35c2ff82070bf16856ba031907ed05f34abe1c0dccc876ac6f15ca", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "314f98fe283ead201cb1451e59d2ad002d15d6e884c5431bc2955228d8f2ca77", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1386944842, "similarity": 0.053475935828877004, "source_content_hash": "dacfcf7ea42c5af9dbdb2b5f0f3e568b8f46e588c0f4093e6a7b7075564c4c15", "source_hash": "d6de0aa18a64af40fc6a47f768417cdae3e274c8a10f7cc9cbe65e67808ca209", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a01a9786faa112fe9f90e8ea2eb70b78454cff8a4beeb9dd01d6577fb8d14fa2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validat