{"doc_id": "doc80543", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the movie *The Perks of Being a Wallflower*, the story begins with a quiet, sensitive 15-year-old boy named Charlie writing letters about his life to an unknown recipient. Charlie chooses that person because he said that he heard the person was nice and thought that this person would not be judgmental. He discusses his first year at high school, grappling with two traumatic experiences from his past: the suicide of his only middle-school friend, Michael Dobson, a year before, and the death of his favorite aunt, Helen, during his early childhood.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1104848618, "similarity": 0.9547169811320755, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The narrative opens with a 15-year-old boy named Charlie composing letters to a mysterious recipient, a choice driven by the hope that the person would be kind and non-judgmental. This young man recounts his first year at high school, where he grappled with profound sadness stemming from two devastating losses: the suicide of his only middle-school friend, Michael Dobson, and the death of his beloved aunt, Helen, during his childhood.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1477983346, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "3822359e06d9f771db6b6610b4bb506983d77b196cbf84df9b49b1eef009e6d4", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "an unknown recipient", "matched_aliases": ["an unknown recipient"], "query_id": "test2333", "question_hash": "4ceda1dd64c9e2d871383b63cb15eab25d416e7a394476b6f7e42ab8e1f5b7e2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "33d88181d5b6b32924b9504b1fc2e6e643cae177d46c87994b14db82b8f8778a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1013851009, "similarity": 0.328804347826087, "source_content_hash": "a085f7b5efb93a9473b6fe94d85fc6e7f68dda3112dc33392f2d51fe18e5a98e", "source_