{"doc_id": "doc81549", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Escherichia coli (/ˌɛʃɪˈrɪkiə ˈkoʊlaɪ/;[1] also known as E. coli) is a Gram-negative, facultatively anaerobic, rod-shaped, coliform bacterium of the genus Escherichia that is commonly found in the lower intestine of warm-blooded organisms (endotherms).[2][3] Most E. coli strains are harmless, but some serotypes can cause serious food poisoning in their hosts, and are occasionally responsible for product recalls due to food contamination.[4][5] The harmless strains are part of the normal flora of the gut, and can benefit their hosts by producing vitamin K2,[6] and preventing colonization of the intestine with pathogenic bacteria, having a symbiotic relationship.[7][8] E. coli is expelled into the environment within fecal matter. The bacterium grows massively in fresh fecal matter under aerobic conditions for 3 days, but its numbers decline slowly afterwards.[9]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 384281237, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5826c1fc782aad9566056161b3181ef0ddd88278e2984200289a8a54c7f9e47d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Escherichia coli", "matched_aliases": ["Escherichia coli"], "query_id": "test2357", "question_hash": "2e5c677b0373d0d621e27835f9e0e685b1ef31136c857df5847db2a9051eab79", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c485ecd1ec30286812863455522712d78a59737bc5c1810101dc60d16df9e49f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 898019191, "similarity": 0.23481781376518218, "source_content_hash": "98fdfec0ff1ce94dac4a41e954cb693ac0b56ab450d9ff71cff50b51a6c82933", "source_hash": "dcf6ab595a10608f09bd4008b12841a8c6e91efabe1a7a8655646fe5dae01f9e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "106f9e6bd8c59d01ef5e75f64c150d27cb9e0ee4fef834e81a0980d0ea7dbbd6", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81651", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Doreen Mantle (born 1926) is a South African-born English actress who is probably best known for her role as Jean Warboys in One Foot in the Grave (1990–2000).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1057214369, "similarity": 0.9693251533742331, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6503f4bd88154ff20043684a3395fac297fdb4c03292967a557340567ed53974", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Doreen Mantle", "matched_aliases": ["Doreen Mantle"], "query_id": "test2359", "question_hash": "5b55daa585cdc8e2247a7806cc6ddbc6629f4031d9ce50010f7331f71b1ee6aa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c0bec39a37b78ac9e64c42d9fec8cc96d0dbbf7c045b6c358c5b1fa467ca8061", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2002860112, "similarity": 0.7292225201072386, "source_content_hash": "6db70b9ce5ce33c07e410882fe45930d2887a1b2b9d473947e0bb894c46c68a3", "source_hash": "1a63ff3f697ec100719cc62addabd2fc9e46bc4370be10f5c57317ff9cf4368d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c052a4a958d262598157934ac7b8fbddae08a1150b35d6e50de1771b419f8bf4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81680", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Humble and Kind\" is a song written by Lori McKenna and first released by American singer Tim McGraw on January 20, 2016, as the second single from his 14th studio album, Damn Country Music. McKenna later recorded her rendition of the song for her eighth studio album, The Bird and the Rifle, released in July 2016. Among several other wins and nominations, the song won the award for Best Country Song at the 59th Annual Grammy Awards, \"Video of the Year\" at the 2016 CMT Music Awards, \"Song of the Year\" at 2016 CMA Awards and \"Country Song of the Year\" at 2016 American Music Awards. It has been certified platinum and reached the number one position on the country music charts in both Canada and the United States.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1571778185, "similarity": 0.9979181124219292, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5d7af0573decc6dd2172ddcf4797719c1188922137ea52a36f96a044909ad5c9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Lori McKenna", "matched_aliases": ["Lori McKenna"], "query_id": "test2361", "question_hash": "3ace544b9b8ee6ee33c8aa94dcd017c83a271ab6f8dafaf38fda52fc7d177ec1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1685158107c0bcad42d6818dbfdd160b105df35a3287bd54afe10aa68b3f60af", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 466650172, "similarity": 0.6708562450903378, "source_content_hash": "7ede3ea415fdb6ef82b3a6f1b7fef3088749666675116a15d0d38724efb6ef12", "source_hash": "3c49dd9968790d346e2c3831d1cec95efc75145946e8a7f2e70122c98cea75d4", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bf71ae529e57b5c92fe4c8d639bf6db0b3ecdd8effc0afce3ea861908175a12a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81696", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series is generally praised for what is perceived as a sort of medieval realism. George R.R. Martin set out to make the story feel more like historical fiction than contemporary fantasy, with less emphasis on magic and sorcery and more on battles, political intrigue, and the characters, believing that magic should be used moderately in the epic fantasy genre. Martin has stated that \"the true horrors of human history derive not from orcs and Dark Lords, but from ourselves.\"", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 389372816, "similarity": 0.9786368260427264, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b77891050b53073b3b9a1af58e1327abfe0f0a72d6c98388d71b51bf01c8093a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "medieval", "matched_aliases": ["medieval"], "query_id": "test2362", "question_hash": "93f485d069d418ea79127fe8e3de258ebbfde89341b876466a210533bfa13079", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "76c246ac60c7ce74f9d4366423a975d2977de1eb9d371f55c47a07754ceb754a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1579486727, "similarity": 0.04719101123595506, "source_content_hash": "85133aea4c6e6cc9359de219f9bfb6a928be1bc8bc521042c164f81291ff6d15", "source_hash": "d1d29bb07cf17ceb5147d498e54cef9e06afca149e9d54905bd86ae1ab6c9079", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0a3a6b4b5154adca5e6c0d88aba62adccaf2f384c6121a98317b383427195901", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81795", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The play Arsenic and Old Lace is a farcical black comedy revolving around the Brewster family, descended from the Mayflower, but now composed of insane homicidal maniacs. The hero, Mortimer Brewster, is a drama critic who must deal with his crazy, homicidal family and local police in Brooklyn, New York, as he debates whether to go through with his recent promise to marry the woman he loves.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2061461531, "similarity": 0.9725490196078431, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7d51dba406b055ec8cf7fdb6dd00f0e44296c0fc6354675965e69f706069451d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Brooklyn, New York", "matched_aliases": ["Brooklyn, New York"], "query_id": "test2363", "question_hash": "0172dabf6f8a15931de0fb55d9db2465811d155d08efc65c78412621ce53ac0d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "61d0369b9bde8074aab7e8cfedce82c0c9eabbf6cc8f344c51c6e3a0a794e522", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 183381090, "similarity": 0.045584045584045586, "source_content_hash": "2a3b7d42fa90564a18d68cefe9008fbd581f46733c3257e99a512f6ef34f560c", "source_hash": "6b5d51ec72524ad73c4122c7ba53f4fb603bb6dc33c7a2ad440cde1f747525d3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "58d82ac9d23a5ad90ed5cd3f718753aaf75bc55af6e54aaa0502dba63783036b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81809", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "During the match in which he took his hat-trick, Griffin was repeatedly called for throwing by the umpires and never bowled again in a Test match. Australian Peter Siddle is the only bowler to take a hat-trick on his birthday, and Bangladeshi off spinner Sohag Gazi is the only player to score a century and take a hat-trick in the same Test match.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 528513151, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "77ecc5c3cc848fa585d97170a122a22fbcc023808e4fbc12c939fea6cc044d1d", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "leg spinner Jimmy Matthews", "matched_aliases": ["leg spinner Jimmy Matthews", "Jimmy Matthews"], "query_id": "test2364", "question_hash": "f4e180917723d644c2c778b55f54a2e74a7d7d24a5dcdb3e169c352301dbf913", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "17a2f708f6c10d52c77d2942020a664782a5a6a45490f870773b88c028c1fe06", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2040857638, "similarity": 0.1873479318734793, "source_content_hash": "9251c22c92626d1c81c103dae458034f92d45bc46c2c1f5b118fdad5c96e3648", "source_hash": "0fb181d739c29c981b18f2f986f6c93f60263842f24fda9f7a22230cd322b9e6", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1696e1a11da6f2514c7d791d3c102af4568584ad372c188f081a62cb7adae28b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81845", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Along Came a Spider is a 2001 American neo noir psychological thriller film directed by Lee Tamahori. It is a sequel to the 1997 film Kiss the Girls, with Morgan Freeman reprising his role as detective Alex Cross. The screenplay by Marc Moss was adapted from the 1993 novel of the same title by James Patterson, but many of the key plot elements of the book were controversially eliminated. The movie received negative to mixed critical reviews, although it became a box office success.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1702625325, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "69c6d7a7407a258025beaf72ed1551e781347680d68c89399ba6464a0f6cd70a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Morgan Freeman", "matched_aliases": ["Morgan Freeman"], "query_id": "test2366", "question_hash": "e4bee3fce1168a4abd616f1adc2d1ec60a17f31544821ffcbc7bc9964a6ad391", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e40e6663aebb382a365a12fe181d560f51c0c50398399786dd351160070a61f7", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1670677894, "similarity": 0.5680473372781065, "source_content_hash": "e770b82e56c6f4ce3414db53137dd6bc5cc477e77ad24af2f498b31b4d7b77d6", "source_hash": "964cb6905fa7c8ce613d09373bf63602ed18e7d677234a441a0bdc77f2ac43f2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2b5b18d46cdd9bc205516b88374ba87847169e3b1ff768ca592bfe969db02ac1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc81884", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "As leader of the Yishuv, David Ben-Gurion was the first person to sign the Israeli Declaration of Independence. The declaration was due to be signed by all 37 members of Moetzet HaAm, though twelve members could not attend, including eleven trapped in besieged Jerusalem and one abroad. The remaining 25 signatories present were called up in alphabetical order to sign, leaving spaces for those absent. Although a space was left for him between the signatures of Eliyahu Dobkin and Meir Vilner, Zerach Warhaftig signed at the top of the next column, leading to speculation that Vilner's name had been left alone to isolate him, or to stress that even a communist agreed with the declaration. However, Warhaftig later denied this, stating that a space had been left for him (as he was one of the signatories trapped in Jerusalem) where a Hebraicised form of his name would have fitted alphabetically, but he insisted on signing under his actual name so as to honour his father's memory and so moved down two spaces. He and Vilner would be the last surviving signatories, and remained close for the rest of their lives. Of the signatories, two were women (Golda Meir (Meyerson/Myerson) and Rachel Cohen-Kagan).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1148029547, "similarity": 0.9605704697986577, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ae16cdd2772fee2665b0c198b73a7c73d6fee0945c0228688cb7656a96f5917b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "David Ben-Gurion", "matched_aliases": ["David Ben-Gurion"], "query_id": "test2367", "question_hash": "008f98a6b3b35da435cb0c36a88f6f13427168b11d2c2287ae3ee78d2d3cd353", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a5fe2f933b277d5d64675161ec5cb30388af030b7885855e8f30e1e53628ba05", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 278926501, "similarity": 0.4040139616055846, "source_content_hash":