{"doc_id": "doc82163", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In vivo, chymotrypsin is a proteolytic enzyme (Serine protease) acting in the digestive systems of many organisms. It facilitates the cleavage of peptide bonds by a hydrolysis reaction, which despite being thermodynamically favorable occurs extremely slowly in the absence of a catalyst. The main substrates of chymotrypsin are peptide bonds in which the amino acid N-terminal to the bond is a tryptophan, tyrosine, phenylalanine, or leucine. Like many proteases, chymotrypsin will also hydrolyse amide bonds in vitro, a virtue that enabled the use of substrate analogs such as N-acetyl-L-phenylalanine p-nitrophenyl amide for enzyme assays.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1275463682, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d41722176c27802e024d5b70a139e488edda1a788ccdea47e076470115658ce2", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "digestive systems", "matched_aliases": ["digestive systems"], "query_id": "test2379", "question_hash": "5529e1a3efa93d49f9762dee8c6f8984ad9d8bffd67b528093b9d48046c4e8cc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "766320f0d41f52a8f89c41e7cab8c45f473df1f75f01f0674b3eda1a9e6e5cd3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 95035773, "similarity": 0.05154639175257732, "source_content_hash": "b54bc3420280debac40844fca2afadd3412383eaee7762ade6084818404bd6af", "source_hash": "e2af2340e84bd01a08cf9541edb776ec8b664d41fde2e22907399b1d1efbbf42", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3a055fb78e7d075bd6addeed5fc2d48cd690298ad2a9948c304f201db7dcd221", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc82212", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Based on a mark in an interior chamber naming the work gang and a reference to the fourth dynasty Egyptian Pharaoh Khufu, Egyptologists believe that the Great Pyramid was built as a tomb over a 20-year period concluding around 2560 BC. Initially at 146.5 metres (481 feet), the Great Pyramid was the tallest man-made structure in the world for more than 3,800 years. Originally, the Great Pyramid was covered by limestone casing stones that formed a smooth outer surface; what is seen today is the underlying core structure. Some of the casing stones that once covered the structure can still be seen around the base. There have been varying scientific and alternative theories about the Great Pyramid's construction techniques. Most accepted construction hypotheses are based on the idea that it was built by moving huge stones from a quarry and dragging and lifting them into place.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1489447913, "similarity": 0.9926512153759186, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "22acae03b1b3ebeb543263099d00e838d6cc215ecae06d8d24c4d3961130009b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "20-year period", "matched_aliases": ["20-year period"], "query_id": "test2381", "question_hash": "f9370fd4027e50c7b7dfce49f0ef716a161eb16b07fcad367a52359b27c44158", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c7a3a4a43cedd5363f25dadeca8dac731862fabb59c8fe7f84893ba24b34a564", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 264793079, "similarity": 0.2515991471215352, "source_content_hash": "8ee983d467a92c99f3d3ed0c4a56d4990f5906ec48bb51bad889325d3b98f0dd", "source_hash": "f736a03bf06b7d13aa83ef6f62a0425a4be3363186a1f32c54c632f118c51695", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2c07d5357ea365768ca2cfcabfe23aa9ce7f7ffa44f347cc6625a69192a17b74", 