{"doc_id": "doc82930", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "There's a Riot Going On is the fifteenth full-length studio album by the American band Yo La Tengo, and was released through Matador Records on March 16, 2018.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 490378223, "similarity": 0.9814814814814815, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "There's a Riot Going On is the fifteenth full-length studio album by the American band Yo La Tengo, and it was released through Matador Records on March 16, 2018.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1247601084, "similarity": 0.9724770642201835, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "735eb87af3b24d9081ce31ccbea91a9bb7863c08f05f1c55850e6224ef67abcb", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "March 16, 2018", "matched_aliases": ["March 16, 2018"], "query_id": "test2401", "question_hash": "e5454fd4baa02038ec3c29f3b10fb1658827040f4606b618f95e85ecf2ed9652", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "10f163932da0c417465101ca213e5c334427d42c9dfcab3aa465932eec30f4c8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 382556618, "similarity": 0.9258160237388724, "source_content_hash": "b7aa05f6b3a6e2c767c2a05e20484f72c7a46f0b94d214e71076537da621230e", "source_hash": "13e8a36f536e536b136cc5e98ea48fb4c6e57293dbdb770ca5dc3049c19aa958", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9cfa87d9b1a7bad4c87d434dcf2bc7f92434bb651f0e29a244a6c6fd9ee8fbbe", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc83019", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "By the late 1960s \"classic rock\" period, a number of distinct rock music subgenres had emerged, including hybrids like blues rock, folk rock, country rock, raga rock, and jazz-rock, many of which contributed to the development of psychedelic rock, which was influenced by the countercultural psychedelic and hippie scene. New genres that emerged included progressive rock, which extended the artistic elements; glam rock, which highlighted showmanship and visual style; and the diverse and enduring subgenre of heavy metal, which emphasized volume, power, and speed. In the second half of the 1970s, punk rock reacted by producing stripped-down, energetic social and political critiques. Punk was an influence in the 1980s on new wave, post-punk and eventually alternative rock. From the 1990s alternative rock began to dominate rock music and break into the mainstream in the form of grunge, Britpop, and indie rock. Further fusion subgenres have since emerged, including pop punk, electronic rock, rap rock, and rap metal, as well as conscious attempts to revisit rock's history, including the garage rock/post-punk and synth-pop revivals at the beginning of the 2000s.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1949341710, "similarity": 0.9987206823027719, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2685cd35c3880c134289253d7a30dcc8558fbb953e90400a06f5383a639d5c31", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "alternative rock", "matched_aliases": ["alternative rock"], "query_id": "test2404", "question_hash": "8a1119a7488740e486298559481e490cae5e8ffcd31d039dd1089c1aee500e62", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "67434f632c2377a5c339b681dd795e31f382410f40e9fb995bf9857f175341a8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2095852491, "similarity": 0.7476459510357816, "source_content_hash": "6a2954c1aca8acd89aac11c0ca62f815cbfbbfd3cf3e9ff388bc8ee141d92298", "source_hash": "33005013a922bddb2b9d62f774b4c430e6e1b1b0addc4d093382b662f4c7a8be", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "18370c2c0225c28de745e684938be37ba2be44379ccd016759ba6455e78d9377", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc83148", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Qing dynasty was founded by the Jurchen Aisin Gioro clan in Manchuria. In the late sixteenth century, Nurhaci, originally a Ming vassal, began organizing \"Banners\", military-social units that included Jurchen, Han Chinese, and Mongol elements. Nurhaci formed the Jurchen clans into a unified entity, which he renamed as the Manchus. By 1636, his son Hong Taiji began driving Ming forces out of Liaodong and declared a new dynasty, the Qing. In 1644, peasant rebels led by Li Zicheng conquered the Ming capital, Beijing. Rather than serve them, Ming general Wu Sangui made an alliance with the Manchus and opened the Shanhai Pass to the Banner Armies led by the regent Prince Dorgon, who defeated the rebels and seized the capital. Resistance from the Southern Ming and the Revolt of the Three Feudatories led by Wu Sangui extended the conquest of China proper for nearly four decades and was not completed until 1683 under the Kangxi Emperor (r. 1661â€\"1722). The Ten Great Campaigns of the Qianlong Emperor from the 1750s to the 1790s extended Qing control into Inner Asia. The early rulers maintained their Manchu ways, and while their title was Emperor, they used \"Bogd khaan\" to the Mongols and they were patrons of Tibetan Buddhism. They governed using Confucian styles and institutions of bureaucratic government and retained the imperial examinations to recruit Han Chinese to work under or in parallel with Manchus. They also adapted the ideals of the tributary system in dealing with neighboring territories.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 980819023, "similarity": 0.9976950938426078, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b481c26aea4ca16084792bf1bfd6f6ececda6f85fe68e7f4129e22f84821849e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Manchuria", "matched_aliases": ["Manchuria"], "query_id": "test2407", "question_hash": "8885ba3b12b7c17b9dce343da3e3346a83e5ed94d34aafff11bcd6da31efe939", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1d6c2a9a520d3325494d0477343b9af54b220f7149fc523558fe4a45d7b967bd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1199843174, "similarity": 0.05419354838709677, "source_content_hash": "0a3fdf8e472b2617e207e99cca2ce2f0ff63bd8d501d3f8f062439b114d0a1f5", "source_hash": "30951ef22b8e0d14803c9810464e49498c4f0828a4f92fea0527d6ba93dbd96f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7bb4d936d80cc1c4fd7442b8c6dde2ca1c1a5600ddbd3b0969de17b73f017035", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc83346", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Dictionary of Greek and Roman Antiquities of Sir William Smith claims that the scythe, known in Latin as the falx foenaria as opposed to the sickle, the falx messoria, was used by the ancient Romans. According to ancient Greek mythology it was believed that Gaea the Greek goddess mother of Titans gave 'a sickle was made out of the strongest metal' to her youngest son 'Kronos' who is also youngest of Titans (also known as God of Harvest) to seek vengeance against her Husband Ouranos for Torturing their oldest sons. To illustrate this, Smith cites an image of Saturn holding a scythe, from an ancient Italian cameo. The Grim Reaper and the Greek Titan Cronus were often depicted carrying or wielding a scythe. According to Jack Herer and \"Flesh of The Gods\" (Emboden, W.A., Jr., Praeger Press, NY, 1974.); the ancient Scythians grew hemp and harvested it with a hand reaper that we still call a scythe.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 488462538, "similarity": 0.999450247388675, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a3ef106c0a1126379771eb7ed769049e17218ca46705445ff8fbe819cb570063", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "scythe", "matched_aliases": ["scythe"], "query_id": "test2410", "question_hash": "71391658e0ca1456e8add6cc18cd29700403a4ab474a5f39b378688a55009d46", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5eedf66b44521e6b53fd14e2daaa9c3e8941896e4b841145b140bd7591466607", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1048526835, "similarity": 0.10121168923734854, "source_content_hash": "0064d4c7f92e9bf0cf770105b63c017a68923be1cba6c098498731a3af78c6b5", "source_hash": "6c4eb47aa3779ea1dbc455e02ee78b2339f7bd2595abfc42f5891f39762348ef", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "852abece866789672866fc6ef4d2e520ad4d0b8dcddac76dfcb571f