{"doc_id": "doc85120", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Book of Eli is a 2010 American post-apocalyptic neo-Western action film directed by the Hughes brothers, written by Gary Whitta, and starring Denzel Washington, Gary Oldman, Mila Kunis, Ray Stevenson, and Jennifer Beals. The story revolves around Eli, a nomad in a post-apocalyptic world, who is told by a voice to deliver his copy of a mysterious book to a safe location on the West Coast of the United States. The history of the post-war world is explained along the way, as is the importance of Eli's task. Filming began in February 2009 and took place in New Mexico.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 655965542, "similarity": 0.9973935708079931, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Book of Eli is a 2010 American post-apocalyptic neo-Western action film directed by the Hughes brothers, written by Gary Whitta, and starring Denzel Washington, Gary Oldman, Mila Kunis, Ray Stevenson, and Jennifer Beals. The story revolves around Eli, a nomad in a post-apocalyptic world, who is told by a voice to deliver his copy of a mysterious book to a safe location on the West Coast of the United States. The history of the post-war world is explained along the way, as is the importance of Eli's task. Filming began in February 2009 and took place in New Mexico.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1745536276, "similarity": 0.9973935708079931, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "11cb0bbe68cfb60d67aeb422344cf24a9578d9ead6ab751fccdacc18325f0305", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "New Mexico", "matched_aliases": ["New Mexico", "in New Mexico"], "query_id": "test2470", "question_hash": "a515d90e90faa300c77ea63260009affc918e70acd3800f84d2f81f30978fb15", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "bf065f40358cfbbe108b96e3d71f45147cf28095ac6d286b501ca08b0f72e5da", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 323571634, "similarity": 0.18353576248313092, "source_content_hash": "baa65c5587b6092a4a588d3ba7014e9d109c9e5bcb4201f38938f418ba8f00b9", "source_hash": "28641018e134b35eda97b046ddeaf2724be5680ea958289d92f2da904acf838f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "194336e8b1502f2945e73791516eee9a55b8d683ed03617a0593ceb35ca7369c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc85127", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In May 2007, Columbia Pictures and Warner Bros. signed the Hughes brothers to direct The Book of Eli, based on a script by Gary Whitta. (The brothers had last directed the 2001 film From Hell.)[7] Subsequently, Anthony Peckham rewrote the script, and in September 2008 Denzel Washington won the lead role.[8] The following October, Gary Oldman was cast to star alongside Washington.[9] Principal photography began in February 2009 and took place in New Mexico.[10] Alcon Entertainment financed the film and co-produced with Silver Pictures.[11]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1739953041, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "4e7ed7590152ee94f93b1cca82f1b79e0cf265d1da668f22bf6ae9e5510a16ab", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "New Mexico", "matched_aliases": ["New Mexico", "in New Mexico"], "query_id": "test2470", "question_hash": "a515d90e90faa300c77ea63260009affc918e70acd3800f84d2f81f30978fb15", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3a63d1cdb57e3214424dfb65193d8e1f133f809e298ea2320797aaf1b77c779f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 375214750, "similarity": 0.20303030303030303, "source_content_hash": "3639402721c58764bd9428583e1bf57ad6080b0a36d0e173a384f2ef4afa3732", "source_hash": "3ac115ba9237337a74b6635f8dd31fac161be123d94c143b373c4c2f86416be1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "cc95d59e296afcffdf1f70f0f6c8d4e76cc9e4752448edfada4b0a0bf9e774c1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc85133", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The San Juan Mountains are a high and rugged mountain range located in the Rocky Mountains in the northwestern region of New Mexico. This area is highly mineralized, having historically been a major center for the gold and silver mining industry in early Colorado. Major towns in the region, which are all old mining camps, include Creede, Lake City, Silverton, Ouray, and Telluride. While large-scale mining has ended in the area, independent prospectors still work claims throughout the range. The last large-scale mines were the Sunnyside Mine near Silverton, which operated until late in the 20th century, and the Idarado Mine on Red Mountain Pass, which closed down in the 1970s. Famous old San Juan mines include the Camp Bird and Smuggler Union mines, both located between Telluride and Ouray.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 948717320, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The San Juan Mountains are a high and rugged mountain range located in the Rocky Mountains in the northwestern part of New Mexico. This specific region is also known as southwestern Colorado due to its proximity. The area is highly mineralized (the Colorado Mineral Belt) and figured in the gold and silver mining industry of early Colorado. Major towns, all old mining camps, include Creede, Lake City, Silverton, Ouray, and Telluride. Large scale mining has ended in the region, although independent prospectors still work claims throughout the range. The last large scale mines were the Sunnyside Mine near Silverton, which operated until late in the 20th century and the Idarado Mine on Red Mountain Pass that closed down in the 1970s. Famous old San Juan mines include the Camp Bird and Smuggler Union mines, both located between Telluride and Ouray.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 401403208, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "454735ad0996914be71a6ac2fa7d8bff41cd6cbd50ad29bd51e31103d7895b0d", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "northwestern New Mexico", "matched_aliases": ["northwestern New Mexico"], "query_id": "test2471", "question_hash": "5380185cbb3bb614c7a72f9a12921a9977b4841f5443ac7dc5ef2d9ab81b8a75", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c722eff38b35d2a3bf945a83a207cd618f7923353b1b7b21abef86170117ddb9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1742208530, "similarity": 0.7198027937551356, "source_content_hash": "21d312ee1805f3bfe526a022bf02354c1e317f49784ba5d9e27b6889e57b68d5", "source_hash": "c07e5bfe6e49fec1e8dcc9d9b4d27acbde21528ead808a8856c1202accf42783", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "07af92d23faaf2ef2dc8d025daff9d340ef1a9d05a5efd18c3a2dc61dd9a3580", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc85214", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Star Wars: From the Adventures of Luke Skywalker is the original title of the novelization of the 1977 film Star Wars. Credited to George Lucas, but ghostwritten by Alan Dean Foster, it was first published on November 12, 1976 by Ballantine Books. In later years, it was republished under the title Star Wars Episode IV: A New Hope to reflect the retroactive addition of episodic subtitles to the theatrical film titles.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 795433200, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9d0a5bfb3ba72bdba0134b62fec8398359ec4a5a79c4387c43d16c635b4cde36", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "novelization", "matched_aliases": ["novelization", "book"], "query_id": "test2473", "question_hash": "cd67f694cfddb02c15d6b727e4b92b910d5d9189a107245a3fb7991c39f4f73d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "2cd9dd5a1dcec14f98c3c6912104e5c6d5ce70ba6ffcae4b4cbe248171878fe3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1476268055, "similarity": 0.44175824175824174, "source_content_hash": "8aca0fdd52d964a86469b6d92705776ce368b392af0bb45db646f9e87542f037", "source_hash": "8cbb079df80fbce2e1ead6cb26581125f5c1c5564d74f37e60f0ff908c7b5dfc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0decac7fcd1dc921d9b646c3f0df9254c413dadd7abbeae51145ced499b292b7", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
