{"doc_id": "doc86839", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the 2000 United States presidential election, the intense recount process in Florida resulted in a decisive victory for the candidate who carried the state by a margin of only 537 votes out of almost six million cast. This outcome made the candidate the president-elect, as the process was extremely divisive and led to calls for electoral reform in the state.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 479632253, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "450ec664abd6f42b91cccdae859ba84159063503a45341790379e417614687d6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "George W. Bush", "matched_aliases": ["Bush"], "query_id": "test2523", "question_hash": "89b6dabdc1592a43fddb86d3b7b714477ad51125bf2ae8555217b371c2f0b827", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fdcc5d9cdb60dbe6c178089ae9406dbe6c6968455dd30403a69f2cb83bc06647", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1973108539, "similarity": 0.7323481116584565, "source_content_hash": "f11eb38ed44714210a294cad5d8ebb8dd2f8dc992c55ec360612d3c1af18a00e", "source_hash": "dd0a815d6a9a32999c1c6532984414abd0a70358fd55c97953da90bc705c1e3d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b384446f65caa5934af3855886798ae3a9a9234809a957a6e76965ef10e76e8a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc86931", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "David Joseph Madden (December 17, 1931 – January 16, 2014) was a Canadian-born American actor whose most famous role came on the 1970s sitcom The Partridge Family, in which he played the group's manager, Reuben Kincaid, opposite Shirley Jones's character. Madden later had a recurring role as diner customer Earl Hicks on the mid-1970s to mid-1980s sitcom, Alice.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 683570275, "similarity": 0.9793672627235214, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1add7af35962e286ab10af17fbbdc609f7cb20554c595f09b5e70b6cc101c90a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "David Joseph Madden", "matched_aliases": ["David Joseph Madden"], "query_id": "test2527", "question_hash": "e164e6fa5e867d5baec435775243d3a401f9f8b3040429e94d88b60a4eabea9a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "46c2d7aaf70a9de2f73b9a44ce15e040c58df13485e71788e5925d3a1d4906ca", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1302577836, "similarity": 0.38126009693053314, "source_content_hash": "4c61865c67bab560d171e56577710ded79ea68df516f8652f9ba36e458d0c99d", "source_hash": "ae8f15f0dad0e899e346a3ab21d2cbade02c5c749062eac7160250938feb7236", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "494e4f658090d3f1fccdb819106171132011cc375365d396b75917af50336511", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc86970", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Since 1718, transportation to the American colonies had been a penalty for various offences in Britain, with approximately one thousand convicts transported per year across the Atlantic.[79] Forced to find an alternative location after the loss of the Thirteen Colonies in 1783, the British government turned to the newly discovered lands of Australia.[80] The western coast of Australia had been discovered for Europeans by the Dutch explorer Willem Janszoon in 1606 and was later named New Holland by the Dutch East India Company,[81] but there was no attempt to colonise it. In 1770 James Cook discovered the eastern coast of Australia while on a scientific voyage to the South Pacific Ocean, claimed the continent for Britain, and named it New South Wales.[82] In 1778, Joseph Banks, Cook's botanist on the voyage, presented evidence to the government on the suitability of Botany Bay for the establishment of a penal settlement, and in 1787 the first shipment of convicts set sail, arriving in 1788.[83] Britain continued to transport convicts to New South Wales until 1840.[84] The Australian colonies became profitable exporters of wool and gold,[85] mainly because of gold rushes in the colony of Victoria, making its capital Melbourne for a time the richest city in the world[86] and the second largest city (after London) in the British Empire.[87]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1631150665, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "59d1ca4e47e2118c2d2fdfc7c573b321baec267106a4d92f48f68de01c5c9c58", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Australia", "matched_aliases": ["Australia"], "query_id": "test2528", "question_hash": "36e1ea42ad42b702a3f2a074e9a39e221ed2eea064799c946e46bfbea2792642", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "6656811799e07edb73f25435f9da4e54fcf433a61c0277adc7a16c