{"doc_id": "doc90765", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Chromosomes are normally visible under a light microscope only when the cell is undergoing the metaphase of cell division (where all chromosomes are aligned in the center of the cell in their condensed form). Before this happens, every chromosome is copied once (S phase), and the copy is joined to the original by a centromere, resulting either in an X-shaped structure if the centromere is located in the middle of the chromosome or a two-arm structure if the centromere is located near one of the ends. The original chromosome and the copy are now called sister chromatids. During metaphase the X-shape structure is called a metaphase chromosome. In this highly condensed form chromosomes are easiest to distinguish and study. In animal cells, chromosomes reach their highest compaction level in anaphase during segregation.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 307400890, "similarity": 0.980438648488441, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "100c7b44961ac585fef0ecf6fc9128efdbbef00d13f2135f49501cc734db7fe9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "metaphase", "matched_aliases": ["metaphase"], "query_id": "test2650", "question_hash": "9aa18c3dc6105d2f1ad09ae1f14b705d84dd44c1a8e249649aecf77a70a84ed1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "faac3b89482f2c444d70567b33765f135aca492be975ff186334775163aafb27", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 18564432, "similarity": 0.30925050641458474, "source_content_hash": "5102b9a151902e63a99491d4e5f9ab48bea9132d4f2fdad34185b3ab77f29ef9", "source_hash": "75e75cc02e1b0f4b4b697bae22d62ccee226e36824b0de3bf72ceb1332c11031", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0aa867ab7152cc6b99d1912d1935bcbe4af4ad4d2f181979690c7d2b1a828a31", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc90807", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Bat Masterson is an American Western television series which showed a fictionalized account of the life of real-life marshal/gambler/dandy Bat Masterson. The title character was played by Gene Barry and the half-hour black-and-white shows ran on NBC from 1958 to 1961. The series was produced by Ziv Television Productions.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1499443438, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "80c98c7c70e1c4a860141d02b153a4e0fb4e678203f4b621ec29064925346939", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Gene Barry", "matched_aliases": ["Gene Barry"], "query_id": "test2651", "question_hash": "4a035fa26db4ea330196b33e77568b1b10b1f635f6393d18dd504a2f33841aaa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "2057158c47ce6d35cfc630391e9c9bf35eaf2413c15745f904eeeab97a961ebf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 541539292, "similarity": 0.3727598566308244, "source_content_hash": "5fe1ef38bf388546bce1aa9abcda9b4d1d9f0e4832e3444c24659799ad388145", "source_hash": "c7b5f547873c0b7c2e49e31ca9278a794c24eebf09292c0ad98d30785d0e014b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "43a99f5af3c9730889f5e37f6d90ed9cc94b3e60cd719b6710bed9e5691a129f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91092", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"White Flag\" is a song by English singer-songwriter Dido, released as the lead single from her second studio album Life for Rent on 1 September 2003. The song is considered one of her signature songs, and helped Life for Rent sell over ten million copies worldwide. The song was nominated for the Best Female Pop Vocal Performance at the 46th Grammy Awards, but lost to Christina Aguilera's \"Beautiful\". It won the Best British Single at the 2004 Brit Awards.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1146184478, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ea5c76c3155fb2b3ad5e2b428316c94ef4fcc62cd45728aa3fdfe446464bf623", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Dido", "matched_aliases": ["Dido"], "query_id": "test2656", "question_hash": "2a9e86de476bf3f4c1086042c1dfe7ba8d0f11763b6cf052fb544b34fb1e0848", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c34d32e454d64e1eb8ff46d1280f7067d096c459e2cabcbb0c0efd71e0c27b35", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1742005942, "similarity": 0.031746031746031744, "source_content_hash": "dff4a7740eaf9084f1ca25e63a00dbd5811a0fc15bf12efbfe6ab119dc309f26", "source_hash": "ca4d02167139115f7acdcb17be8073ea6173b0b305960ce2e185e6b3fe13b1ed", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d4cf00b30bf77bcd225b16fc7453c8ccf2895856683836c5101e14ade30c13cf", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91109", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Beginning almost immediately, the singer and a co-worker decide to \"steal\" a Cadillac by way of using their assembly line jobs to obtain the parts via salami slicing. He takes the small parts home hidden in his unusually large lunch box; larger parts are smuggled out in his co-worker's motorhome.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 223976319, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ff7d55deee31a8c7a6b4a3ec5b4ebfd843e9ea7e016b2f3f806a0f0b29d648d9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Cadillac", "matched_aliases": ["Cadillac"], "query_id": "test2657", "question_hash": "841151351def861a09ba1ee20aaa4a418066b8e2a52aebefd13720e02c2d66bb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "90ea50a250a9e6b4aff6a47768b82ebaa9dfe05fb513c4ce963eea4061f03435", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2008604187, "similarity": 0.057245080500894455, "source_content_hash": "76e14a28749bb612a115b07dfaed3e93184bd705f3d2cc7bffc9663dbf64920c", "source_hash": "945134ee49dbcd15f040df763df10520a65d796b333a6de818475c5dbddf81d3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "eef17916c5a759609aa76f83bca2cdf21502c694ea21781ef2c50474e4954b90", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91116", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Canadian Pacific Railway was originally built between Eastern Canada and British Columbia between 1881 and 1885, fulfilling a promise extended to British Columbia when it entered Confederation in 1871. It was Canada's first transcontinental railway, but no longer reaches the Atlantic coast. Primarily a freight railway, the CPR was for decades the only practical means of long-distance passenger transport in most regions of Canada, and was instrumental in the settlement and development of Western Canada. The CPR became one of the largest and most powerful companies in Canada, a position it held as late as 1975. Its primary passenger services were eliminated in 1986, after being assumed by Via Rail Canada in 1978. A beaver was chosen as the railway's logo in honor of Sir Donald A Smith (1st. Baron Strathcona and Mount Royal) who had risen from Factor to Govenor of the Hudson's Bay Company over a lengthy career in the beaver fur trade. Smith was a principal financier of the C.P.R. staking much of his personal wealth. In 1885 he drove the last spike to complete the transcontinental line.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 162073897, "similarity": 0.9580943978826643, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "6a74c70a0b26273a5a328b6a58cf24a9ec994bd93732ea5cdf2434c7d260e2db", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "between 1881 and 1885", "matched_aliases": ["between 1881 and 1885"], "query_id": "test2658", "question_hash": "638a43e61a8b8e6040799d160719d1f0b0b3ce61cd997732e3a525f2e05542d1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a445943762f48e19b450443ad75a6273271a242806569053b517281f4d273604", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2046740746, "similarity": 0.3981042654028436, "source_content_hash": "db6844ca0264be3ed9dac8684a64875a3f06c36ea104159d4269e8e1e197cac7", "source_hash": "1ed0954c94