{"doc_id": "doc91220", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Heart and Soul\" is a song by British pop band T'Pau. Featuring vocalist Carol Decker performing overlapping lyrics, the song was released as the group's first single in 1987 from their debut album Bridge of Spies. Following its inclusion in a Pepe Jeans advert, the single reached No. 4 in both the US and UK charts.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1146373657, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "978226f4cd9192dc12550eead5b9e7204136b4c1ad36da787a4a3b529577fbcf", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "British pop band T'Pau", "matched_aliases": ["British pop band T'Pau", "T'Pau"], "query_id": "test2659", "question_hash": "0ddd567daa3c7cac7de04d70dd01fa5c0f887460d48f5d69a3ddba756a539faa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "95320bfa09bf5cfdfcb83655b36f9c264f475c2487631c012f63e8b85d28a8a6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 940988048, "similarity": 0.11164274322169059, "source_content_hash": "1b242305369c97d2f11cdda9f62893e847817cfd102ff6c9c1884777ff8bfcbb", "source_hash": "0b8c4c1762bc8ed8a4a48fd253f1cf7dedd470baa87ac74961e677c6cd8df9c5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "684e9408ba0bea70a107329a5e6a0e1e3d427d85ef8110408360c90db4bca88a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91227", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The prince-electors (or simply electors) of the Holy Roman Empire (German: Kurfürst, pl. Kurfürsten, Czech: Kurfiřt, Latin: Princeps Elector) were the members of the electoral college of the Holy Roman Empire.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 833384198, "similarity": 0.95, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d66c4b3d2ba4a569a9a65cfa504b4195fd35535c92ab9fc4fd965db10be84ea3", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "prince-electors", "matched_aliases": ["prince-electors"], "query_id": "test2661", "question_hash": "fc9ae10739f87c7931a7ca1bcb8b4170943ff518433874aee65958f6c68d5ee3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "69d03fbc38de17e43139fdc9fe09117e9612a59b5069aa043f8557d69978a468", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1672901920, "similarity": 0.5029239766081871, "source_content_hash": "66c95bae56ff73cc83675e7a4a1aa02a0b5d667de5d947510f704e012b3f9adf", "source_hash": "93e41d6022b4fc987ad1610011958df114a5c4aa58368df7ff04e106a0bdace7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d86624bb0b02ccdf452e58b25d3140713c9b802aeadf3d3e22b9dbb8e4d35a44", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91228", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "From the 13th century onwards, the Prince-Electors had the privilege of electing the King of the Romans, who would be crowned by the Pope as Holy Roman Emperor. Charles V was the last to be a crowned Emperor (elected 1519, crowned 1530); his successors were elected Emperors directly by the electoral college, each being titled \"Elected Emperor of the Romans\" (German: erwählter Römischer Kaiser; Latin: electus Romanorum imperator). In practice, all but one Emperor (Charles VII from the House of Wittelsbach) from 1440 onwards came from the Austrian House of Habsburg, and the Electors merely ratified the Habsburg succession.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1607944494, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "47f40695372cddc7a51e68541a249c1672144fd32671db25326e6db62a3fad4c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "prince-electors", "matched_aliases": ["prince-electors"], "query_id": "test2661", "question_hash": "fc9ae10739f87c7931a7ca1bcb8b4170943ff518433874aee65958f6c68d5ee3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "97071f177f35b168a6c0a414450651021fc635efb2ca75fba9f3d5146ad195a8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 258352876, "similarity": 0.13123359580052493, "source_content_hash": "5a1634f2d7aa5c97305e2d9e4f7d8bad878fb7779675f7a97362dceea32df27e", "source_hash": "74f5920f5f2db4d91e16e85651570da99ffab8c5bcae8570b5de47e3fa3ecd5c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "f834af3a160c501553bfce2a1d792db6070f3ad9a8705bc45de405d02fbb559a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91277", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"I Knew the Bride (When She Used to Rock 'n' Roll)\" is a song written by Nick Lowe and first popularized by Dave Edmunds. It was released on Edmunds's 1977 album Get It and a year later in a live version by Nick Lowe's Last Chicken in the Shop on Live Stiffs Live.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 627409289, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "27225a11442cd861bf00a6f96a194795b3efa777f70692e5e203241432a313de", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Dave Edmunds", "matched_aliases": ["Dave Edmunds"], "query_id": "test2662", "question_hash": "a59929ccbaa33418fb4910ebdfe746a1aa5835aa3acf77bbfe760bb0b39ead55", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f71a0744a06f852916fb9e337a059920919c4d3d68c046745147943b55e66b2f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1865416419, "similarity": 0.5175438596491229, "source_content_hash": "0dc2c510f00428d476dc390f2dc405715ba84ce6b55821e7113e08c23efcff4d", "source_hash": "e0358729b9d792d0b79ff8b1aa7b0901ad924de110af34f847c7ee65073b8643", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a7e2d0597535063d18b3b71bc92320b039b1625e7635068f9bc8ed45396c9901", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91359", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "There has been much speculation about what the Titanic band played when it sank. A first-class Canadian passenger, Mrs. Vera Dick, and several other passengers, alleged that the final tune played was that of the hymn \"Nearer, My God, to Thee\". Hartley reportedly once said to a friend if he were on a sinking ship, \"Nearer, My God, to Thee\" would be one of the songs he would play. But Walter Lord's book A Night to Remember popularised wireless operator Harold Bride's 1912 account (New York Times) that he heard the song \"Autumn\" before the ship sank. It is considered Bride either meant the hymn tune known as \"Autumn\" or the tune of the then-popular waltz \"Songe d'Automne\" but neither was in the White Star Line songbook for the band. Bride is one of only two witnesses who were close enough to the band, as he floated off the deck before the ship went down. Some consider his statement to be reliable. Mrs. Dick had left by lifeboat an hour and 20 minutes earlier and could not possibly have heard the band's final moments. The notion that the band played \"Nearer, My God, to Thee\" as a swan song is possibly a myth originating from the wrecking of SS Valencia, which had received wide press coverage in Canada in 1906 and so may have influenced Mrs. Dick's recollection.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1949480763, "similarity": 0.96953125, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d24f0190d872408f814f0a52c799d43bafb40e96b322717a286ef168c4875327", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "\"Autumn\"", "matched_aliases": ["\"Autumn\""], "query_id": "test2665", "question_hash": "a640af8ddc67a5714946b44e5a1fa9f71dec88734ad64cf99618621291ebf2f2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c7f6dde879d39b517014c25131cc8f1c2a61e695587ac83c6292f7af49b0848b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 360989185, "similarity": 0.03297872340425532, "source_content_hash": "a47f76e7276de52a54b45d733451ba78c2ceded11c9e4452df5fe6d4ff93ec38", "source_hash": "c5cc585f02d87a23e45428a643b7cfb8bb14bc914f0f1b555539916bc0561864", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bd23a0cd9c063d0ae96fba08e61d88c9e981b920de23f2eb2fe3984209b08af1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
