{"doc_id": "doc91704", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Originally, Top Hat customers would park their automobiles anywhere on the gravel parking lot and walk up to place their orders. However, on a trip to Louisiana, Smith saw a drive-in that used speakers for ordering. He suspected that he could increase his sales by controlling the parking and having the customers order from speakers at their cars, with carhops delivering the food to the cars. Smith borrowed several automobiles from a friend who owned a used-car lot to establish a layout for controlled parking. He also had some so-called \"jukebox boys\" come in and wire an intercom system in the parking lot. Sales immediately tripled. Charles Woodrow Pappe, an entrepreneur, chanced upon the Shawnee drive-in and was impressed. He and Smith negotiated the first franchise location in Woodward, Oklahoma, in 1956, based on nothing more than a handshake. By 1958, two more drive-ins were built, in Enid and Stillwater.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 540590112, "similarity": 0.9983739837398374, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a2873c12914dc2160083f93d7fdccb0aa5057915710d9b583f5f3ab66b0edca7", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Woodward, Oklahoma", "matched_aliases": ["Woodward, Oklahoma"], "query_id": "test2676", "question_hash": "35513f0024a79ff8e11dc77a8ded1f6b0c6dc478e84301a0873057cd3ef215e9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "cf562bdae64130570c2cd825a10dbccc88a2f5d498a41ac35abba0925e2d901f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2071632040, "similarity": 0.13302397525135345, "source_content_hash": "517ffb27065ca10648a29d3cfcc971cab4860dbff92738cd65967c11d29538da", "source_hash": "918c16cdeeab1f22e96a8f8808b21c15e50f156e0ea0cef3b8eecad78a107c9d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9cae60d0d63c4028e08