{"doc_id": "doc95082", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Rings are not traditional in an Indian wedding. However, in modern society it is becoming a practice to wear rings for engagements and not for actual marriage. Though the left hand is considered inauspicious for religious activities, a ring (not to be called wedding ring) is still worn on the left hand. Men generally wear the rings on the right hand and the women on the left hands. If a wedding ring is worn, the ring is worn on the left ring finger mostly for men.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1383401704, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2f575dfec986cafffe998af4b738106d3a1e7f7fedacc300ff6b2194de1b7e37", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "the left ring finger", "matched_aliases": ["the left ring finger"], "query_id": "test2765", "question_hash": "1a67eb6d3c52bac60f6f574d5c76bb35e66d489c125bccac2641dce4ee70ba84", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e1dc438b60cb7c5a46f2f2b3cfb979908bc7c2128a6960ccd8ffae1ff9ac955b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2068002273, "similarity": 0.010834236186348862, "source_content_hash": "20d367c823535c5c6ec7c202e988012206c98807a1c9b91ad8a2a43e170f3823", "source_hash": "01aa4716b3549e80212935b8f626009279442476f0208b2da4c1a2ca04e1d4dd", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "78ba17ff7cddcaffbf88db2c74f893a63a244e047329f67f54d0b74bb778dbfd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc95083", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Bernard Hill (born 17 December 1944) is an English film, stage and television actor. He is known for playing Yosser Hughes, the troubled 'hard man' whose life is falling apart in Alan Bleasdale's groundbreaking 1980s TV drama Boys from the Blackstuff and, more recently, as the Duke of Norfolk in the BBC adaptation of Dame Hilary Mantel's Wolf Hall. He is also known for roles in blockbuster films, including Captain Edward Smith in Titanic, King Théoden in The Lord of the Rings film trilogy and Luther Plunkitt, the Warden of San Quentin Prison in the Clint Eastwood film True Crime.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1296766186, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "78023e3778cac97bd3e0abf0e76d5be9560d151a181c784f573b425c0efcb298", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Bernard Hill", "matched_aliases": ["Bernard Hill"], "query_id": "test2766", "question_hash": "5da82ce45b6d2d325ee8d6ae41ef4d46f195ac2a9fa7bf58dadd8a0cefc081d9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ddfaed7327a0d169de290d2dff0177b2f880bd4e77750a9a6cf32bbbb6411e53", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 22217241, "similarity": 0.15807560137457044, "source_content_hash": "11f6a00b5e2f5f104dfeb01b1d7e3e05fde47c1a810181e3b8af5022af95f328", "source_hash": "7d078caf7315b6c8ed0c5ccfcacfbe518d85ec6750ce90851984119303e987fc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "96525c562f246101d1e0cf47b7a8010b0e58aa297a1c26f1260792a06c002a7e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e4