{"doc_id": "doc95733", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The recorded history of Maryland dates back to when Europeans began exploring the area, starting with the Italian/Venetian John Cabot (c. 1450 – c. 1500), who explored the coast of the continent of North America for England in 1498. The first European settlements were made in 1634, when the English arrived in significant numbers and created a permanent colony. Maryland was notable for having been established with religious freedom for Roman Catholics. Like other colonies of the Chesapeake Bay, its economy was based on tobacco as a commodity crop, cultivated primarily by African slave labor, although many young people came from Britain as indentured servants in the early years.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2124770553, "similarity": 0.9854651162790697, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "History of Maryland\n\nThe recorded history of Maryland dates back to when Europeans began exploring the area, starting with the Italian/Venetian John Cabot (c. 1450 – c. 1500), who explored the coast of the continent of North America for England in 1498. The first European settlements were made in 1634, when the English arrived in significant numbers and created a permanent colony. Maryland was notable for having been established with religious freedom for Roman Catholics.[1][2][3] Like other colonies of the Chesapeake Bay, its economy was based on tobacco as a commodity crop, cultivated primarily by African slave labor, although many young people came from Britain as indentured servants in the early years.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1502060527, "similarity": 0.9772403982930299, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "11612e1be6dac7f8fbca563b82bc39f24730d6dde178fa2833f85810232c1425", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "the English", "matched_aliases": ["the English"], "query_id": "test2788", "question_