{"doc_id": "doc96820", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Deposition is a thermodynamic process, a phase transition in which gas transforms into solid without passing through the liquid phase. The reverse of deposition is sublimation and hence sometimes deposition is called desublimation.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1775959128, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "0f68ec4a18ee2d7ee1508ddd82114efcc6528ecb79f111c47b054dbdf8d7f208", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Deposition", "matched_aliases": ["Deposition", "desublimation"], "query_id": "test2820", "question_hash": "ab2323509bd22a71ad0744c641360f2cf53480a8b4111ec3991077005fbe2cbe", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "136400f76eb4b34c30c5df5b33e531fb683c5fa11bbc262a1df4496a1fe39db4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2143481488, "similarity": 0.648068669527897, "source_content_hash": "c1850056ec31d586637f5ae9c7a901aba69bda12beb880b6fc3deb772145a5c0", "source_hash": "ef52b1e2e3117f3fb9a693eee5dabb0f715831e48208d0a0660f39e9b42f4d50", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c41c36fe31fb6de21d42bbbf307295295d071c242898ad6b2850501a62d3c57a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc96828", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In chemistry, pH (/piːˈ(h)eɪtʃ/) (potential of hydrogen) is a numeric scale used to specify the acidity or basicity of an aqueous solution. It is approximately the negative of the base 10 logarithm of the molar concentration, measured in units of moles per liter, of hydrogen ions. More precisely it is the negative of the base 10 logarithm of the activity of the hydrogen ion.[1] Solutions with a pH less than 7 are acidic and solutions with a pH greater than 7 are basic. Pure water is neutral, at pH 7 (25 °C), being neither an acid nor a base. Contrary to popular belief, the pH value can be less than 0 or greater than 14 for very strong acids and bases respectively.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1067230316, "similarity": 0.9985185185185185, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In chemistry, pH (/piːˈ(h)eɪtʃ/) serves as a numeric scale used to specify the acidity or basicity of an aqueous solution. This value is approximately the negative of the base 10 logarithm of the molar concentration, measured in units of moles per liter, of hydrogen ions. More precisely, it represents the negative of the base 10 logarithm of the activity of the hydrogen ion. Solutions with a pH less than 7 are acidic, while those with a pH greater than 7 are basic. Pure water is neutral, at pH 7 (25 °C), being neither an acid nor a base. Contrary to popular belief, the pH value can be less than 0 or greater than 14 for very strong acids and bases respectively.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1070548028, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "508248364003af8c5c153572faf4948bfbebc7f8481cd7be3606568b2192376c", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "potential of hydrogen", "matched_aliases": ["potential of hydrogen"], "query_id": "test2822", "question_hash": "17080e8a81858a18eb8699983bc69c10dae6c2360c910d5d1b5f5a9e7310c50a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "df47b777de1f7dfeaf3689216bd9bbc10bb1250ab036e97a94323adc8c62c748", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 118240046, "similarity": 0.9478390461997019, "source_content_hash": "cd373843d8aa88adcded92a7854ed4ebf95cb18f5b48998272a51338be1fd0dc", "source_hash": "40b8f558400cedd233bd877cb543204a6e1c99ca0abba529b79d5080604fed9a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1b2176930073ecdd67f2c002d6745352668818a2501e829447123105969ff227", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
