{"doc_id": "doc96975", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Alfred P. Aldrich, a South Carolinian politician from Barnwell, stated that declaring secession would be necessary if a Republican candidate were to win the 1860 U.S. presidential election, stating that it was the only way for the state to preserve slavery and diminish the influence of the anti-slavery Republican Party, which, were its goals of abolition realized, would result in the \"destruction of the South\".", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 36811283, "similarity": 0.9975845410628019, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Alfred P. Aldrich, a prominent South Carolinian politician from Barnwell, argued that secession was essential to prevent the loss of slavery. He claimed it was the sole method for the state to safeguard its institution while simultaneously reducing the power of the anti-slavery Republican Party.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1365345708, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "bbe5c36d3ef8fa36a68f813e70cf8f629e720948316f44c4ad1872b139e19c09", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "to preserve slavery", "matched_aliases": ["to preserve slavery"], "query_id": "test2827", "question_hash": "8899e396e494f7f36b0a3be96fb7fc7e27d250bbc8ad8539f48ad15be4641d45", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "59a8f7b71c3d04276a10c9d24e1472091e2b733045a8b0f7245b805c08804e3f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 774425880, "similarity": 0.9452054794520548, "source_content_hash": "d118df35df4ed64f7875ac238daeff0fdc7492e558e33a35bd4ec2217f9b85c2", "source_hash": "0685beebcab86644e19444204dfa0b9cd10ea1f27002ca30f49cfcbf869829ef", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b75cc963b5a752e9b8f26b3985c2a2bcca842c6729a61de2495b202e60b3536b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment"