{"doc_id": "doc97482", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Christmas 2009 was a white Christmas in some parts of Britain, with thick lying snow which easterly winds had brought over the previous week. Travel over much of Britain was badly affected by ice and snow on roads, and was made more slippery by partial daytime thaw followed by overnight refreezing. It was the first white Christmas anywhere in the United Kingdom since 2004.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1956311319, "similarity": 0.9894459102902374, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9d4feeb900b1f65cd416e9a429cb7a18f5e29c5afdb07fcef2338fa51229169f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "2009", "matched_aliases": ["2009"], "query_id": "test2848", "question_hash": "e9b64bd66f284cc5d1fe88bb44895af662a0977af9a2821cb0606fc7f2452383", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fa7c3dd8bca06b4cb971c71568c2c333490a9528ab3f0e67c18f42eb7328dd60", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1224097359, "similarity": 0.28027681660899656, "source_content_hash": "4f948cf4bc0bd0cc9101898184973e42fba03d311a315f10219b1f0628c12a2e", "source_hash": "6b9d20d069a959a137a546cada2bd1acb1fe26c8b5cc3795fdcb4c978dbe4da8", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2d07969a9b1b106d7a5542b5e6b876fd0757e9a5fb71bc830e5c690f83885bea", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc97490", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Clay was born and raised in Louisville, Kentucky, and began training as an amateur boxer when he was 12 years old. At age 18, he won a gold medal in the light heavyweight division at the 1960 Summer Olympics in Rome and turned professional later that year. At age 22 in 1964, he won the WBA, WBC, and lineal heavyweight titles from Sonny Liston in a major upset. Clay then converted to Islam and changed his name from Cassius Clay, which he called his \"slave name\", to Muhammad Ali. He set an example of racial pride for African Americans and resistance to white domination during the Civil Rights Movement.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 906563258, "similarity": 0.9934533551554828, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Clay was born and raised in Louisville, Kentucky, and began training as an amateur boxer when he was 12 years old. At age 18, he won a gold medal in the light heavyweight division at the 1960 Summer Olympics in Rome and turned professional later that year. At age 22 in 1964, he won the WBA, WBC, and lineal heavyweight titles from Sonny Liston in a major upset. Clay then converted to Islam and changed his name from Cassius Clay, which he called his \"slave name\", to Muhammad Ali. He set an example of racial pride for African Americans and resistance to white domination during the Civil Rights Movement.[11][12]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 251437003, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "f25a6ccd3dbcf545d4c7d27327d4d7a85f3b118db50721811adfc286f7b7d700", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "1960", "matched_aliases": ["1960"], "query_id": "test2849", "question_hash": "7bf2c2cbf48a119cc391f6685c12a1a517b96d10ee3dc6792798c6e34b977382", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "0e8eb884fdd645081880bb406a0fd889d8abb12d2e22ca83