{"doc_id": "doc98149", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Alpha Centauri (α Centauri, abbreviated Alpha Cen, α Cen) is the closest star system to the Solar System, being 4.37 light-years (1.34 pc) from the Sun. It consists of three stars: Alpha Centauri A (also named Rigil Kentaurus[13]) and Alpha Centauri B, which form the binary star Alpha Centauri AB, and a small and faint red dwarf, Alpha Centauri C (also named Proxima Centauri[13]), which is loosely gravitationally bound and orbiting the other two at a current distance of about 13,000 astronomical units (0.21 ly). To the unaided eye, the two main components appear as a single point of light with an apparent visual magnitude of −0.27, forming the brightest star in the southern constellation of Centaurus and is the third-brightest star in the night sky, outshone only by Sirius and Canopus.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1006500276, "similarity": 0.9974874371859297, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "fb3fb0ae4ea05feaa54f254b2a78c4f3f165bcbcbf6fe72ab0b19ffb1ace2f1c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "4.37 light-years", "matched_aliases": ["4.37 light-years"], "query_id": "test2870", "question_hash": "9cfe4dd5f4e5c8aa00320ce56df10a77ab34a3303b05b7caff4d01d5be0da291", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "589947c0505c8714534e69ced97d95d5e17cb655ff4235e453c540a234cacefe", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 201274825, "similarity": 0.2630480167014614, "source_content_hash": "8cb36ce343835ddc58085977479676ce1b738130e4abf2427d8030ab5f699491", "source_hash": "2d87a17e8282ab189a407dca327c83b01845e6abdb7988802d062aaac8120531", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5d5c27c55bfde58677f7b30d08524ad56f28e5696f11f412a0151c970c921421", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc98381", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Taylor is a surname used in the British Isles of French and Latin origin which originated as a Norman occupational surname (meaning tailor) in France[1][2] It is derived from the Old French tailleur (\"cutter\"),[3] which is in turn derived from the Late Latin taliator, from taliare (\"to cut\").[4][5] The first historical evidence of the surname dates to the County of Somerset, South West England in 1182.[6] \"Taylor\" is the fifth-most common surname in England, the 11th-most common in Scotland and the 22nd-most common in Wales.[1][7] It is also common in other English speaking countries (especially Australia, Canada, New Zealand, and the United States, where it was the tenth most frequently encountered surname in the 2000 US Census),[8] but has a low incidence in Ireland, where it is mostly concentrated in the North.[1] It is often the anglicized form of the German surname Schneider.[9]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1327253705, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d9e9cb0af54a70d08b3285b93b079d95ff546b77964974669913cfc03d511383", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Old French", "matched_aliases": ["Old French"], "query_id": "test2876", "question_hash": "e1e28043d7616f967344fa4b6bfe00fd71a0f089b92edeb04136106970583160", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "bc0b4e0ad35fb48d1b18fe0d9e5b7f4868a938e17747cce75ae995aefab20cab", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 158554325, "similarity": 0.3810694529809465, "source_content_hash": "e86296d5e0ea4fa3597551f5c8d1315727e76426e4a66ee380ec484b05db4faf", "source_hash": "eaab574a81780b5746363cdd0ec169e6da16413dc7ff8d0cbfee30fd89f1ebad", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0d772d266cecb9ba0c766c0add0818d93bab50166d8ec2a9ce7ff128fbea2dba", "form