{"doc_id": "doc98582", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "By daylight, only 120 experienced infantry remained in the Mexican garrison. Cos called Sanchez Navarro to the Alamo and gave him orders to \"go save those brave men. ... Approach the enemy and obtain the best terms possible\". Sanchez Navarro first returned to his post at the plaza to inform the soldiers of the imminent surrender. Several officers argued with him, explaining that \"the Morelos Battalion has never surrendered\", but Sanchez Navarro held firm to his orders. Bugle calls for a parley received no response from the Texians, and at 7 am Sanchez Navarro raised a flag of truce.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 55549777, "similarity": 0.9841004184100418, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "By daylight, only 120 experienced infantry remained in the Mexican garrison. Cos called Sanchez Navarro to the Alamo and gave him orders to \"go save those brave men. ... Approach the enemy and obtain the best terms possible\".[60] Sanchez Navarro first returned to his post at the plaza to inform the soldiers of the imminent surrender. Several officers argued with him, explaining that \"the Morelos Battalion has never surrendered\", but Sanchez Navarro held firm to his orders.[60] Bugle calls for a parley received no response from the Texians, and at 7 am Sanchez Navarro raised a flag of truce.[60]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1766151395, "similarity": 0.9942004971002486, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "2ff645a59b25f57bf1cd5631d0fe2e7afebc403e213192a05db30a655eac42e0", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Sanchez Navarro", "matched_aliases": ["Sanchez Navarro"], "query_id": "test2882", "question_hash": "9eba54bd37c257d099e625ac8ccaf1e2639f8d49ae256f2406cb955cf9459e6a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "28d4d18b2aa9eb0de5a0589ef24b59eefb79e6f