{"doc_id": "doc100242", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Thousands of drum players, dancers, vendors and visitors come together every Sunday afternoon throughout the temperate months, occupying much of the open space on the eastern edge of Mount Royal Park (also known as Fletcher's Field). Jeanne-Mance Park, located directly across Avenue du Parc from where the Tam-Tams take place, serves as the city's main outdoor sporting ground. As such, the entire area is generally quite popular on Sundays in the summertime, drawing an exceptionally diverse crowd to myriad activities. The Tam-Tams typically start around 10:30am and continue until sunset. It is not an officially sanctioned nor sponsored event, simply a regular if technically spontaneous event. As such, it's difficult to pinpoint when it started or what motivated the first drum circle.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1904183116, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "24f910e6e29ccdd502798cf56141d81c5631670699d3bb7d0d729ad67515ac67", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "around 10:30am", "matched_aliases": ["around 10:30am", "10:30am"], "query_id": "test2930", "question_hash": "67d07b9542a25914e8994e2af02c5fc5419c808273e777e77955b8b990f883f5", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ba7374f590d32774c05b3f545e81a696a594462a50531fd428a3704b38c6dbac", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1965373004, "similarity": 0.04040404040404041, "source_content_hash": "59aa7de5623c46bb342b997b00acf999ef2dfd957478b4e72a5bd32d2ffbecd2", "source_hash": "5a1f43a993e2e9cd7cdd20f6da3c2aa78cf5d6d594733cdd43ca551fe14a6600", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3d97da7bba8a00021a1895cf736a274893643bc95ad79ff64bfb8f447e9a5bc1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc100251", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The term \"train of thought\" comes from Thomas Hobbes in his work Leviathan, where it was introduced and elaborated in 1651. Although the term was used with a somewhat different meaning similar to that of British associationists, the original source text confirms that Hobbes is the primary originator of the phrase.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 506676497, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The term \"train of thought\" originated from Thomas Hobbes in his *Leviathan*, where he introduced and elaborated on the concept as early as 1651, though with a somewhat different meaning similar to that used by the British associationists.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 237239457, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "509dcca34c347dca6703ef8e0dbaab1b6c1034523cbfbe0dac10e1f8b8ed627c", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Thomas Hobbes in his Leviathan", "matched_aliases": ["Thomas Hobbes in his Leviathan"], "query_id": "test2931", "question_hash": "9bbf8191e9c58284f7ec3bf534da2ab517e518a9f45f2917a8e76553960f512d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "55fa3aae5e09d5fbbc5deb9da9e1a38b2068fe9d126efe93d1e0a32bb74cf24d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1410424447, "similarity": 0.4405594405594406, "source_content_hash": "af38be4f0c0f01bf4a616681916c41a79817df09cab63b1b9251a294154c8b57", "source_hash": "be4f90db7dc1301b8eef3780dc897619bf2126b1894e243ca08c64a9a9fded7d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3d1d7ab1bd127c8329bf480a4d3b23772ca594ed62bc3c02df89d9fc1ed2a145", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "st