{"doc_id": "doc101204", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Human anatomy, physiology and biochemistry are complementary basic medical sciences, which are generally taught to medical students in their first year at medical school. Human anatomy can be taught regionally or systemically; that is, studying anatomy by bodily regions such as the head and chest, or studying by specific systems, such as the nervous or respiratory systems.[3] The major anatomy textbook, Gray's Anatomy, has been reorganized from a systems format to a regional format, in line with modern teaching methods.[41][42] A thorough working knowledge of anatomy is required by physicians, especially surgeons and doctors working in some diagnostic specialties, such as histopathology and radiology. [43]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1013250490, "similarity": 0.9903047091412742, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "526393d7e273e105cd40538fed7bd3f5d6af2c4e7afab6585aaf7e281b43ae1b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Anatomy", "matched_aliases": ["Anatomy"], "query_id": "test2958", "question_hash": "a527b251ce60b5e1f5a83246c4b7d66dd24331ea08267e8aa6f3bd9d6e551180", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "3003d27f184416e9a980ec581c0aa3c63c5432be207b63253349b23c7caf0356", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 506948447, "similarity": 0.06834300451321727, "source_content_hash": "5b0e53a122ec6cde82160502be10bafa4d1cd7aabcce2171e2c45953616b5d6c", "source_hash": "872d232891655369c3853ee22061247c5e74e3fd3f6359fd851f2af1d6959d92", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4f3afcdda81196d6c6de59662b924aa061fae1eede79dc5bf2666577456ca73d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "s