{"doc_id": "doc101357", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series premiered on Sunday, August 11, 1991, as the second Nicktoon after Doug and preceding The Ren & Stimpy Show. Production initially halted in 1993 after 65 episodes, with the last episode airing on May 22, 1994. From 1995 to 1996, the only new episodes broadcast were \"A Rugrats Passover\" and \"A Rugrats Chanukah\", two Jewish-themed episodes that received critical acclaim; during this time, well-after the end of the show's production run, Rugrats began to receive a boost in ratings and popularity, due to constant reruns on Nickelodeon. In 1996, Klasky Csupo Animation began producing new episodes, and the show's fourth season began airing in 1997. As a result of the show's popularity, a series of theatrical films were released; The Rugrats Movie, which introduced Tommy's younger brother Dil, was released in 1998, Rugrats in Paris: The Movie, which introduced Kimi and Kira, released in 2000, and Rugrats Go Wild, a crossover film with fellow Klasky Csupo series The Wild Thornberrys, released in 2003. The final episode aired on August 1, 2004,[3] bringing the series to a total of 172 episodes and 9 seasons during a 12-year run.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1167829645, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "551fbfaef4ae9abfbb0c066b40b0cb8d9216894c8219aa9e9880c581b7089652", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "9 seasons", "matched_aliases": ["9 seasons", "9"], "query_id": "test2964", "question_hash": "e1e6823bbbad49d2fee65f59542141863dd89b98d916ea7636bddd77e5b9ca41", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5d97365f95891c42df403d663a68043983fbd8202e37f9bf87780407e56e8441", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1543638914, "similarity": 0.18862275449101795, "source_content_hash": "d875d9ca4ad0bda3a1f05f44307e651d524f750e34d275ed79f4e3eadc67fac1", "source_