{"doc_id": "doc102220", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "PDCA was made popular by W. Edwards Deming, who is considered by many to be the father of modern quality control; however, he always referred to it as the \"Shewhart cycle\". Later in Deming's career, he modified PDCA to \"Plan, Do, Study, Act\" (PDSA) because he felt that \"check\" emphasized inspection over analysis.[4] The PDSA cycle was used to create the model of know-how transfer process,[5] and other models.[6]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1032565341, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d961535223c51754b06927213c2bb8684bf8fa4e7402cb6d3ecab34c0d043f99", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "W. Edwards Deming", "matched_aliases": ["W. Edwards Deming"], "query_id": "test2979", "question_hash": "30f20cbf40cf65eac8db1d5db27a8656904940d360904f6f26d554a1acd49519", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f509795cf7f708baad19bf706aebdb9f0003a86e3fdffea48b7fde2814f318fa", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 582373977, "similarity": 0.1871713985278654, "source_content_hash": "4958969f9074d9d979855967cf152a70e2f78bb3fefd1b8807917c674743bccc", "source_hash": "68be21f652828d4f5245ceda34301907e507e14604cc41ac107e9037c628ce88", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a2515dabca42a52dba4879cea371bc192ff8f4db4981cd9b9043ed2bf376faf6", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc102301", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Joseph Nye Welch (October 22, 1890 – October 6, 1960) was an American lawyer who served as the chief counsel for the United States Army while it was under investigation for Communist activities by Senator Joseph McCarthy's Senate Permanent Subcommittee on Investigations, an investigation known as the Army–McCarthy hearings. His confrontation with McCarthy during the hearings, in which he famously asked McCarthy \"At long last, have you left no sense of decency?\" is seen as a turning point in the history of McCarthyism.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 565414340, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "fde7db23c565a3dd87a234cc24b5598a11c3062d7beb8d1f1ab7d478d2a00cee", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Joseph Nye Welch", "matched_aliases": ["Joseph Nye Welch"], "query_id": "test2982", "question_hash": "d2937b3d35c98fecc5029e96ce7334edbba2d880f16f7ad2367e311e6f212b6e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ee0549f597934c892b7f6158f40b4850be1c6a182d14e00b84e725797ce86dad", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1258742945, "similarity": 0.2680628272251309, "source_content_hash": "d683c67672dfac69b7f6d8d694eb977f44622c4d621395404f47e504d69e1c9b", "source_hash": "4c7ab7ac1a660416719b74924c460875546b196b1c103f82a1cb81fed92ed3cc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b1eccf51cc825afc7ce66dd321d50d389a32ab5d73b6dc85d6ba9aa70afe79a0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_g