{"doc_id": "doc103840", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Walter Egan (born July 12, 1948) is an American rock musician, best known for his 1978 gold status hit single \"Magnet and Steel\" from his second album release, Not Shy, produced by Lindsey Buckingham and Richard Dashut.[1] The song reached #8 on the Billboard Hot 100 and #18 on the Easy Listening chart.[2] Overseas, it peaked at #32 on the Australian Singles Chart, Kent Music Report.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 887593355, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e79ce148282c6e74232f5fcadafc843ff9a433ff33cf50e392992c4d11ce73db", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Walter Egan", "matched_aliases": ["Walter Egan"], "query_id": "test3030", "question_hash": "83fc3de6f465a44a3811692ec96abe2251e97737a1cc2141eeb0dfcd9f8a4c7a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ed9865d8b46395fc7ef1c47c88c219d0872c85f1e566671a4ad96bd421e64a12", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1134564987, "similarity": 0.37449118046132973, "source_content_hash": "ac256d79f000d91cc4234e2270c0d382670fcde004a2927a6d4c954706a9bc2a", "source_hash": "eb79e649369903ed549a34691c94152bc3de8e6f84f92d2852ab38a9f0ba41d8", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "25e516279a436a60888c3fd7e448c3fe74a39c960ee11dfc89c38a01b37333cc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc103872", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "While Karnataka became independent with the rest of the country on 15 August 1947, this did not occur in some parts of the state that were under the rule of the Nizam of Hyderabad. Hyderabad consisted of large portions of what were later to be the north eastern districts of Bidar, Gulbarga and Raichur of Karnataka state. The Lingayat minority in these regions also largely believed that they had been neglected and resented the oppression of the Nizam and the Razakars. The Nizam refused to accede to India until his rule was overthrown by force. Following the 'police action' against the Nizam, Hyderabad province and its citizens became independent on 17 September 1948. This day is celebrated by the Karnataka government as the Hyderabad-Karnataka liberation day.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 832933630, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "67e381239f26be8eceef459a00c0fdb85093f36a7f71755f355b57cd924bcc37", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Hyderabad", "matched_aliases": ["Hyderabad"], "query_id": "test3031", "question_hash": "d5f3948ca9893eee96db8737b0df45e7f00d76856cd62857c8427e2a315881fe", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "770ab8a585f37d79186cafa6610188ce92ee59859baed1ff33331c456d40d8bf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1233454831, "similarity": 0.19341840161182, "source_content_hash": "fd17291b9aff43528584dc4fdc54ee541070fdfe1018b96f1801c32cc684ea8c", "source_hash": "49d91867349bf419058713a848fc26cf2c16956f31ee47670212b1e530a06900", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6cedfdcba9862fdc9bb0386e1781c175a95ffe8cfd8e7cfbab53b74b8f383849", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provi