{"doc_id": "doc104417", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The feminist theory underlying the Duluth Model is that men use violence within relationships to exercise power and control. This is illustrated by the \"Power and Control Wheel,\" a graphic typically displayed as a poster in participating locations. According to the Duluth Model, \"women and children are vulnerable to violence because of their unequal social, economic, and political status in society.\" Treatment of abusive men is focused on re-education, as \"we do not see men's violence against women as stemming from individual pathology, but rather from a socially reinforced sense of entitlement.\" [8] The program's philosophy is intended to help batterers work to change their attitudes and personal behavior so they would learn to be nonviolent in any relationship.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 321945541, "similarity": 0.9916506101477199, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The feminist theory underlying the Duluth Model posits that men utilize violence within relationships to assert power and control, a dynamic often visualized through the \"Power and Control Wheel.\" While the program acknowledges that women and children face vulnerability due to their unequal social, economic, and political status, its primary focus shifts to the rehabilitation of abusive men. Unlike approaches that might attribute violence to individual pathology, the Duluth Model emphasizes that such behavior stems from a socially reinforced sense of entitlement. Consequently, the program's philosophy aims to assist batterers in modifying their attitudes and personal conduct so they can learn to be nonviolent in any future relationship.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 566311853, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "470a8fff7d51c6d8ccc19ed0cfd8c3c23a2a5c69a198ccd1509db64bdfcb4cc0", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "re-education", "matched_aliases": ["re-education"], "query_id": "test3047", "question_hash": "ec4e2b8ee6316642aaac1a60a58cffc2141a9ee7d028ab88bd7092269c6be687", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "dde6e760c94000e6fd27fe2b38fd20462b364a858a19654c4f12c90b3d2ae5a2", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2113356131, "similarity": 0.48484848484848486, "source_content_hash": "c9488d554300355e7783fc74f849723b99cd09dc94989dfdf0ec21cebd366f8a", "source_hash": "417aa9a5887ba841984ddd05830d3c5d2f21a99b1eb7f7652ca1d632a4e8a5d5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "de04842227f95aa2db7abadbe9cf209fcad072a152d1b3bf29e0aea23ff1d329", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc104443", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Both ethnic affiliation (e.g. Pathan, Sindhi, Baloch, Punjabi, etc.) and membership of specific biraderis or zaat/quoms are additional integral components of social identity. Within the bounds of endogamy defined by the above parameters, close consanguineous unions are preferred due to a congruence of key features of group- and individual-level background factors as well as affinities. McKim Marriott claims a social stratification that is hierarchical, closed, endogamous and hereditary is widely prevalent, particularly in western parts of Pakistan. Frederik Barth in his review of this system of social stratification in Pakistan suggested that these are castes.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 495203351, "similarity": 0.9881656804733728, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "832473b475b66c91e943c59ace281a20f4e9c3f6bf79d199a0a0ef53081703e4", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Frederik Barth", "matched_aliases": ["Frederik Barth"], "query_id": "test3048", "question_hash": "b93b742cb2fc4be002cf672afef26911558912b9e9222a525c9bd125c12ec741", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "058042fa60476d1d3d3de23531fef6cd9965abbf1bef38a03245bfcc439e02b4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1747580813, "similarity": 0.24756189047261815, "source_content_hash": "b6aebb81a7927c5fe27587bc91b5a9d926f4b861a8958f4af1dcd21072657325", "source_hash": "f6d1e4b7056ea56d262e4e39ad8fdf7135c6c43f4cf3ef81030258cf937976a2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3043f0e24249ed5dbf8ac5dc97affa4c3094a0298e3a39dc48ec7b26cd6b9c7d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "val