{"doc_id": "doc106812", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The management team is especially important because it coordinates the recovery process. The team assesses the disaster, activates the recovery plan, and contacts team managers. The management team also oversees, documents and monitors the recovery process. It is helpful when management team members are the final decision-makers in setting priorities, policies and procedures. Each team has specific responsibilities that are completed to ensure successful execution of the plan. The teams have an assigned manager and an alternate in case the team manager is not available. Other team members may also have specific assignments where possible.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 988502176, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9f7821279363e853c94a1a262aaa10005efeca37b23126eb2822162eb58d0540", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "management team", "matched_aliases": ["management team"], "query_id": "test3123", "question_hash": "7f648966669b4690bd44842060cce257a9481ed75bcef80bc06f7f068900f120", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ac919cb23496bf6be44688421e8019f0e91b887d8a436cf1345e70aa30ebfea0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1796523007, "similarity": 0.08340016038492382, "source_content_hash": "d6c22825cfd533d8adb70d064dc74a6138e2b593ace9ac57d21b1796f895e425", "source_hash": "09d308706923f54f3bcade27deacdaf79b4956419bc86f8bf7524f2d3f060010", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a33255c8a50994db97143c1ca734454ce7d125d74327084d4b794c868aba1ca6", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc106826", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In a cell, DNA replication begins at specific locations, or origins of replication, in the genome. Unwinding of DNA at the origin and synthesis of new strands, accommodated by an enzyme known as ligase, results in replication forks growing bi-directionally from the origin. A number of proteins are associated with the replication fork to help in the initiation and continuation of DNA synthesis. Most prominently, DNA polymerase synthesizes the new strands by adding nucleotides that complement each (template) strand. DNA replication occurs during the S-stage of interphase.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1139721331, "similarity": 0.9974025974025974, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "669dfe3ce337f4934bbbe2b7611aabaf1b054f7a2314eccade7e1a70e2c73b15", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "origins of replication", "matched_aliases": ["origins of replication"], "query_id": "test3124", "question_hash": "6578b8ee71204672cb23202d90bf83309df435b780024ab0051cedf1523f7a2a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5fa3d934d2a2455f9a2027fd4930a21ffc4bec6057d7c6949d664897b3920c1e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 712681324, "similarity": 0.08544027898866609, "source_content_hash": "acc6a0d33d1cc3f1cd454edef89a6cf372e09499fa857b601f41c7775f965bf0", "source_hash": "e71f9784d8cdf7232e7bcbb36b82e8245b2f025c7ca55d67e3ca51077d34aef9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9b51f56cc33152bcaafbe27d7b5163531e7c17a284fdb24ac68d56e725b75c91", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1aca