{"doc_id": "doc107524", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "However, it is possible to narrow the date further. A terminus ante quem for A Shrew seems to be August 1592, as a stage direction at 3.21 mentions \"Simon,\" which probably refers to the actor Simon Jewell, who was buried on 21 August 1592.[29] Furthermore, The Shrew must have been written earlier than 1593, as Anthony Chute's Beauty Dishonoured, written under the title of Shore's wife (published in June 1593) contains the line \"He calls his Kate, and she must come and kiss him.\" This must refer to The Shrew, as there is no corresponding \"kissing scene\" in A Shrew.[30] There are also verbal similarities between both Shrew plays and the anonymous play A Knack to Know a Knave (first performed at The Rose on 10 June 1592). Knack features several passages common to both A Shrew and The Shrew, but it also borrows several passages unique to The Shrew. This suggests The Shrew was on stage prior to June 1592.[29]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1119752909, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "491d14acb5571b49f96b9db6b24cbf2a35b304f461e37fa3253df24207263dcf", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "prior to June 1592", "matched_aliases": ["prior to June 1592"], "query_id": "test3148", "question_hash": "8cb721957048bc437ac218750486edb3e870c4b6086ea54ab9eeb2e09739ff23", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1cf54dd7fd882a77b2a11540d809bdc78e177380823ad5a2e8432e7ba12255a4", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 971159549, "similarity": 0.6875, "source_content_hash": "695d6f1920b6b2a1edc4f64503d8d0007bbe204b54ae00694916158b278e1ac5", "source_hash": "c811791d65ae0f5dd9023b560c93cf3aea99edd9a2858946b7ea1164bde8ea9b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "c6654f7680c41e2f11e60a2c1f1730b542455236bc71207fbf06e8139829ea90", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107699", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Book of Esther, also known in Hebrew as \"the Scroll\" (Megillah), is a book in the third section (Ketuvim, \"Writings\") of the Jewish Tanakh (the Hebrew Bible) and in the Christian Old Testament. It is one of the five Scrolls (Megillot) in the Hebrew Bible. It relates the story of a Hebrew woman in Persia, born as Hadassah but known as Esther, who becomes queen of Persia and thwarts a genocide of her people. The story forms the core of the Jewish festival of Purim, during which it is read aloud twice: once in the evening and again the following morning. The books of Esther and Song of Songs are the only books in the Hebrew Bible that do not explicitly mention God.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 614816655, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e014dfb1fee238ab5e9d78bfba54d603c6f9de1aa947c442851488a99464deaa", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Persia", "matched_aliases": ["Persia"], "query_id": "test3153", "question_hash": "620690976375c12040a02e10e3a6eaf360e5a15f0750689f0b3e632c3bc0fccd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5333dfe8c1a26dac02a24e8308164591843651f9ce5a16907ccac9430ad2a0c9", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2057979741, "similarity": 0.18435321456235476, "source_content_hash": "419152c5c836117ea24ae4ab6bb8da8bf953131721b78f4a859038e0d1d3b4bb", "source_hash": "2064bd46375b417d406a541bf10e5efdbc45d5aa9c4a5297584a9f6592928470", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4b9db294d3351c0f3ab0970ede371321f6f70f2c6210a116896fd739890b5428", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107770", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "==Land borders of India==there are only seven land borders of india with neighbouring countries.india doesn't make land border with srilanka.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 19332661, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a608dd293e206515eda733d84015ee026e70544fbddf3ebda9df5f038a8763f6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "seven", "matched_aliases": ["seven"], "query_id": "test3156", "question_hash": "af0ab3958008c92f8b815b0737d0da82ee50eb0452f007c89f6d9d5b4250db62", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "4e8880c353ec02717baa44d57fec11a58a8ff47e1692048f6274d2a4d0f6700a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 12739587, "similarity": 0.7508305647840532, "source_content_hash": "f6289392c20d815e5c1ee068e247094dace73f58f88c11542feffa7a61ff5f01", "source_hash": "6c1a5c2a66eab8118cf808144ddba2ad943fb17d25aaa8d433db9ce1f8befe03", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e4d166051c63c1516934852fa7d4a49eaa33f570ca1a88678c2c3caf81b348b2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107778", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Youngstown's economy has been impacted by a loss of the steel industry jobs which started on September 19, 1977, on what became known to locals as \"Black Monday\", and continued into the mid-1980s. While the loss of steel industry jobs in the region coincided with the general deindustrialization of Rust Belt cities such as Youngstown as well as the United States as a whole, Youngstown's economic struggles have been well documented. In the Mahoning Valley region, where Youngstown is located, the city's population was halved, while non-industrial businesses were forced to close or relocate due to cascading effects resulting from Youngstown's deindustrialization.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 520489648, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "03e808a5fe6fbbe1a54101255bd9197dd016fd40c6d37157c74c385e1de7cf62", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "September 19, 1977", "matched_aliases": ["September 19, 1977"], "query_id": "test3157", "question_hash": "794cba07649836025e00ebfca5c7551f3689ce11ab5640a0ad888ea9843b8fb8", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "d1a6e1d7a7902482584af55223802f578dacfb7b07eeeab14910ebbcb2863f17", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2019486062, "similarity": 0.10112359550561797, "source_content_hash": "f0a516e81d6f1ba6c24b65f8efe8a3bc65f091b6f00d3b3a1c94110930054b76", "source_hash": "b5821819d50d43ba13ea66c6bce454a45d24c5a190b82c08bd2b83914e537476", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d4c07d46e287246fd0917704179bccbbea094b7bb2ba46348a0238ba703113a3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107852", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Automobile drivetrains generally have two or more major areas where gearing is used. Gearing is employed in the transmission, which contains a number of different sets of gears that can be changed to allow a wide range of vehicle speeds, and also in the differential, which contains the final drive to provide further speed reduction at the wheels. In addition, the differential contains further gearing that splits torque equally between the two wheels while permitting them to have different speeds when travelling in a curved path. The transmission and final drive might be separate and connected by a driveshaft, or they might be combined into one unit called a transaxle. The gear ratios in transmission and final drive are important because different gear ratios will change the characteristics of a vehicle's performance.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 864183347, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "3f8cfb0bb00837620e078e7764cfc23165c3d8c0dc6cb049600b577e84e6814f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Automobile drivetrains", "matched_aliases": ["Automobile drivetrains"], "query_id": "test3158", "question_hash": "d4b139847633db5925e0cddfe9ff6d9d0bdf94e046b24abecf02ebe2c75680e2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "527db0ccd026a7f8823ee7eedf0ddecc9b4c610158c22fbea6e61168e2cee787", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 881152709, "similarity": 0.08260524225575853, "source_content_hash": "489669794467f988ae84162fb3bb9268c1298c6d4e79d5b68259d153f945ecb1", "source_hash": "5a8036183a67eaef606af871433af0c48d6bd8cb00c6421da6430f369f781ff5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "26f4c922ef0c074528e581ea91a7e66cd0d367799f60bc0d9ebed294d56720af", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107870", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series follows a family of six, and later seven, and stars Frankie Muniz in the lead role of Malcolm, a somewhat normal boy who tests at genius level. While he enjoys his intelligence, he despises having to take classes for gifted children, who are mocked by the other students who call them \"Krelboynes.\" Jane Kaczmarek is Malcolm's overbearing, authoritarian mother, Lois, and Bryan Cranston plays his immature but loving father, Hal. Christopher Kennedy Masterson plays eldest brother Francis, a former rebel who, in earlier episodes, was in military school, but eventually marries and settles into a steady job. Justin Berfield is Malcolm's dimwitted older brother Reese, a cruel bully who tortures Malcolm at home, even while he defends him at school. Younger brother Dewey, bitter about his ruined childhood, smart, and musically talented, is portrayed by Erik Per Sullivan. At first, the show's focus was on Malcolm, but as the series progressed, it began to explore all six members of the family. A fifth son, Jamie, was introduced as a baby at the end of Season 4.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 544983872, "similarity": 0.9990714948932219, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f6d41ff671c89f34bbccc79f60996a0e09935d8faf34809d550463a441b99394", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Bryan Cranston", "matched_aliases": ["Bryan Cranston"], "query_id": "test3159", "question_hash": "60a36372f98ec946cf9dec151852a44b98eb146c707649d8fc71a50c9a47c88d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "b13b328122a6ff3b8686934ab17a8dd00ce8054e6608541988a80acf2a6394db", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1573841190, "similarity": 0.1096579476861167, "source_content_hash": "8e1dd7b7d70c70b9ff3b1fdc18cb96e7a2c73f23ca52664c7d3a0523e30cf6c6", "source_hash": "836a7366fdf52e1d1d843c0792c46eb294d625c7d799b199688afb88fca45ad4", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "43ebf707e4367dd72cf9538e8487ebfcd5f032b5b6b92c0c2e014e913f4c5c23", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107873", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series stars Frankie Muniz as Malcolm, the third of four and later five boys, his brothers, and their parents, Lois (Jane Kaczmarek) and Hal (Bryan Cranston). Their first child, Francis (Christopher Masterson), was sent away to military school, leaving his three younger brothers at home, Reese (Justin Berfield), Malcolm, and Dewey (Erik Per Sullivan) with Malcolm being the middle child still living at home. In season four, the character Jamie (James and Lukas Rodriguez) was added to the show as the fifth son of Hal & Lois. The show's early seasons centered on Malcolm dealing with the rigors of being an adolescent and enduring the eccentricities of his life. Later seasons gradually explored the other members of the family and their friends in more depth, including others such as Craig Feldspar, Lois' coworker at the Lucky Aide drugstore, Malcolm's friend Stevie Kenarban, and Stevie's dad Abe.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1800720598, "similarity": 0.9608465608465608, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7775aa3bba5b7b0d663aad6508b97c2e525b564d1141ed30382453983e4142ed", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Bryan Cranston", "matched_aliases": ["Bryan Cranston"], "query_id": "test3159", "question_hash": "60a36372f98ec946cf9dec151852a44b98eb146c707649d8fc71a50c9a47c88d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "102277a77e25759470a3e6c3b665378b6394f213736fef590c679c1f6c0612e3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 320345584, "similarity": 0.17531305903398928, "source_content_hash": "b267f146680987ce2d2acb245dcb9472ed4c38e507edf85c97dd7fbde539e9e3", "source_hash": "63d0ee35f4025afff84e9e435c749073dfc095cd9870893f2d475cf2ac203742", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bb2af980135f445326160695d3b6ad076bfa47784