{"doc_id": "doc109414", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "God of War: Ghost of Sparta is a third person action-adventure video game developed by Ready at Dawn and Santa Monica Studio, and published by Sony Computer Entertainment (SCE). It was first released for the PlayStation Portable (PSP) handheld console on November 2, 2010. The game is the sixth installment in the God of War series and the fourth chronologically. Loosely based on Greek mythology, Ghost of Sparta is set in ancient Greece with vengeance as its central motif. The player controls the protagonist Kratos, the God of War. Kratos is still haunted by the visions of his mortal past and decides to explore his origins. In Atlantis, he finds his mother Callisto, who claims that his brother Deimos is still alive. Kratos then journeys to the Domain of Death to rescue his brother. After initial resentment from Deimos, the brothers team up to battle the God of Death, Thanatos.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1438242987, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "8efe3a3fa2a2a2bf9dedaf3891315e17d28670d7bb17317c65d0ed9adbb01743", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "ancient Greece", "matched_aliases": ["ancient Greece"], "query_id": "test3202", "question_hash": "1f0e4bfafea4cef2462aa7cf91865a38c790b988621158ecf910b2e1ac36c0b0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "a9352677b05f1e8f1472137cb541b23a9af0f786053a55e29943d0c772e959dc", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1141430684, "similarity": 0.3795440542205792, "source_content_hash": "2cd5194e8015e85acd413d662a1b8070e0a44af5317085d6def6ec30e9c4f559", "source_hash": "65d2437a891e900051e0f50f78566e68f8d452bf369f19fcf0a413344a5f08f2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "06f0fc1758a87003a5ff9286e359ae392e97666f5e8aedc6a66301ca6429720e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc109446", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "After the first season of Everybody Loves Raymond ended in 1997, the series' creator, Philip Rosenthal, asked Ray Romano what he was going to do over the summer. When Rosenthal suggested he go to Italy, Romano did not accept because he was \"not really interested in other cultures.\" According to Rosenthal, \"After I got up off the floor, I realized: Here's an episode.\" Directed by Gary Halvorson, \"Italy\" guest stars Silvana De Santis as Colletta, Pierrino Mascarino as Giorgio, Alex Meneses as Stefania, David Proval as Signore Fogagnolo, Enzo Vitagliano as the Bocce player, Sergio Sivori, Vanni Bramat, Luca Francucci and Alessandro Francucci.[1] It was filmed in July 2000 in the town Anguillara Sabazia outside of Rome.[2] Romano first hinted of the episode in an interview published that same month in the Rome News-Tribune.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 899296964, "similarity": 0.9982046678635548, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "208f8e937bc4105406971edaf8e5399981da0e0c9f110d3341bbdc4b1b5df0cf", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Anguillara Sabazia outside of Rome", "matched_aliases": ["Anguillara Sabazia outside of Rome"], "query_id": "test3203", "question_hash": "d1db8bc787ecf4e494b85e32475c1031e9a9f6b77a60c613e684619690b817db", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "00ab510b97b18ee54fd33dcfe11a48763f95469bf3abd6c290a1b9db16df02ac", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 928526203, "similarity": 0.17092768444119796, "source_content_hash": "e6cf7a5d598c21e3fcf5dfbd512764e62abe9773cb6c2c8be3fc35f9a51a6a5a", "source_hash": "70357c0e402bf5936c20931ec7f50de56ec02e9ee0ebb4c0dd8fb5ba1687f8b9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "376965160eeb1422cbee7f01766d2ac604f6be6847310fee1d069dc3fe4191f2", "fo