{"doc_id": "doc110061", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The fifth season of America's Got Talent, an American television reality show talent competition, premiered in the United States on the NBC network and on Canada's Global on June 1, 2010. Soul singer Michael Grimm was named the winner on September 15, 2010, beating 10-year-old classical crossover singer Jackie Evancho. Piers Morgan and Sharon Osbourne returned as judges. After four seasons on the show, David Hasselhoff left to host a new show and was replaced by Howie Mandel.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1010143685, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2f37804380c0f339666d258eacc95cd1d54fb15dbfbe39efb8832faa48c9f0c0", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Michael Grimm", "matched_aliases": ["Michael Grimm", "Soul singer Michael Grimm"], "query_id": "test3215", "question_hash": "6a9010b54b84bc943a265febff9575a1a1f35bdd5ae55d5242cc9006577935f6", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "c78257a723fb42663067e4d25decb16ea6f48c93a82f9bb194938c5c365c7986", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1040989259, "similarity": 0.625, "source_content_hash": "f826fba44bfa8685b90bbe62accba9e8b98db63995284e788f8f04b963313b4a", "source_hash": "11762bc17b984e4bdf20fbb92333203a718dc965f0a1d82c80fb230b194a8f6f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "52dcf6752c36b540519ab0b6cecb186458595d0941a67b33d1121ce10afd11eb", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110107", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the year 2026, the Augma is released to the public as an alternative system to the AmuSphere, due to its function to simulate reality while the player is conscious rather than using FullDive. The most prominent combat-based game is Ordinal Scale, in which a player's abilities are ranked by ordinal numbers.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1173747205, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the year 2026, the Augma is released to the public as an alternative system to the AmuSphere, due to its function to simulate reality while the player is conscious rather than using FullDive. The most prominent combat-based game featured in this setting is Ordinal Scale, in which a player's abilities are ranked by ordinal numbers.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2081579859, "similarity": 0.9612403100775194, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "d6845330f54d6e0d4b4a3e1239dd9be7805dce10337c4fe36b2d6b404f0b5f2a", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "2026", "matched_aliases": ["2026", "the year 2026"], "query_id": "test3217", "question_hash": "5040114c7b899a8083d39ca60c89b925a90f96df5afd2de2a647d83a0df508a2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "fb79c552ccd76630160e14ed7be1590fe904b5d4296affe32f3e96fb73abdd98", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1855702114, "similarity": 0.0732484076433121, "source_content_hash": "18b779c334d2673b3f7e9574bcb6b1058673b85b3cb923cd75dc83ef6e24e30c", "source_hash": "5f65ac99e46d342eef34d18d217a0a6d5c978d36f08a8d643e4403aeff8909fc", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b9f9d094e8df6bbc6ea707e8166d43448a9c0725acbfab805aa06529fd704dbd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110123", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Neuropsychology is the study of the structure and function of the brain as they relate to specific psychological processes and behaviors. It is an experimental field of psychology that aims to understand how behavior and cognition are influenced by brain functioning and is concerned with the diagnosis and treatment of behavioral and cognitive effects of neurological disorders. Whereas classical neurology focuses on the physiology of the nervous system and classical psychology is largely divorced from it, neuropsychology seeks to discover how the brain correlates with the mind. It thus shares concepts and concerns with neuropsychiatry and with behavioral neurology in general. The term neuropsychology has been applied to lesion studies in humans and animals. It has also been applied to efforts to record electrical activity from individual cells (or groups of cells) in higher primates (including some studies of human patients). It makes use of neuroscience, and shares an information processing view of the mind with cognitive psychology and cognitive science.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 398830740, "similarity": 0.996742671009772, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1f2dd01dd7754a7566e715b7bfd9eb7af0d6f5acbd662245ebda59e73d5ac9e3", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "neuropsychology", "matched_aliases": ["neuropsychology"], "query_id": "test3218", "question_hash": "f803a4c9e2b097093e5c5c60a5618acd638747ddd256e30e0e637c6465eeff74", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "393ad181871a9735d67f486dc1e15f8f87a697fe3febf397d8e12e5e836b132b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1752884831, "similarity": 0.09124668435013263, "source_content_hash": "71c6d50530842c36f1d5509d13180ce19ae84b3335ce2d82ce258229e576bd08", "source_hash": "807d3b3c9c9c2217c82356a32d5c04c6cf3dff04989cae2c027fa82492a69dea", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "197c610fff70c81fefc3112863e6e81046cd4a60529ed37f9cd0d93fc95462d3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110134", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Experimental neuropsychology is an approach that uses methods from experimental psychology to uncover the relationship between the nervous system and cognitive function. The majority of work involves studying healthy humans in a laboratory setting, although a minority of researchers may conduct animal experiments. Human work in this area often takes advantage of specific features of our nervous system (for example that visual information presented to a specific visual field is preferentially processed by the cortical hemisphere on the opposite side) to make links between neuroanatomy and psychological function.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 958667348, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5c40d718cd1a254ab0e0d61707814d35488d6c45d8770d5a01c1b38c81d6ad5f", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "neuropsychology", "matched_aliases": ["neuropsychology"], "query_id": "test3218", "question_hash": "f803a4c9e2b097093e5c5c60a5618acd638747ddd256e30e0e637c6465eeff74", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5970710a4032f73e5bb2944a1d44777ed69eb691ebf61640a0145a644c2af16e", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1440864768, "similarity": 0.34234234234234234, "source_content_hash": "2531dc0661b6fd531506d066a9ce48a1f146de7a5d15ff3dc33b02e8a60afeb0", "source_hash": "4f6708c0309d43166b9f8f7b57def2c2cff27c1d2e91240358c9c2505fd7e1d7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "fa57043cfdcd011d254a5968674aa32dc3a4c0cf58a29324a04ca25724ec20b1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110251", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"Go Outside in the Rain\" is a R&B song by Milira released in 1990. The track is from her debut album, Milira, and reached number thirty-six on Billboard's Hot R&B Singles chart.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 29198598, "similarity": 0.9915966386554622, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b68119f031ec4d4d0148af80f671da3d8a5317f8b76755a01e8bbfec0576f69e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Milira", "matched_aliases": ["Milira"], "query_id": "test3222", "question_hash": "ddfc24dd093cac7a78a48fe1e6326c1d6971ff0d067c37bef16d110b37723a62", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "53e094c2606236fee344e2b8f52049c2c1d47b7d0f790dfd6efb71c8d05cd531", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 122312026, "similarity": 0.38961038961038963, "source_content_hash": "c61d72824330ab89f720e501d27527ba9a54cf5a11edc42f054d0e142c946c02", "source_hash": "024ee276077eb23a41af64800d355e6f415eb710912d9b9f4164323e0eea0971", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5bcd4efd217a61c760ff289ad8c90e89cfda68384edd6ca3f7a41d9b04e6ae9c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110577", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Gimme Gimme Gimme is a BBC television sitcom by Tiger Aspect Productions that was first aired in three series from 1999 to 2001. It was written by Jonathan Harvey, who developed the series with Kathy Burke.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1284414919, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5c39a5ba37699a1e754258ca07d4f97114294ee010b926f5f4eec0ded0fe13cc", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "8 January 1999", "matched_aliases": ["1999"], "query_id": "test3229", "question_hash": "482be9160d7f16b3fae9ab56f7143972007af38c7f1bf2555d0b7c925528baad", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "45a737942c68bfb971dcbf723072843908b4060e8e0386c6c460f1a39532aab1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 139692196, "similarity": 0.3314285714285714, "source_content_hash": "5d4c7de3ba6ee679fdf5e5a6a824be8de250c83894f34866bf9ad05d9f613b8f", "source_hash": "7a31de15aec13c8350346af301761b3ee7b0202b7d70114e283abc139d1bd7cb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a1a31a94325ac775b71f07cf8b82235d6aac083664c4c465a54a9035cf489f3c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110596", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Gimme Gimme Gimme has broadcast three series and 19 episodes in total. The first series premiered on BBC Two on 8 January 1999 and lasted for six episodes, concluding on 12 February 1999. Following this, a Millennium special was screened at the end of the year on 29 December 1999. A second series commenced on 14 January 2000 and finished on 18 February 2000, again including six episodes. A short sketch included as part of Comic Relief was broadcast on 16 March 2001. Due to the high viewing figures and success the show received, it was moved to BBC One for a six-episode third series which was the last. Each episode was written by Jonathan Harvey and directed by Liddy Oldroyd for the first two series and the special; the third series was directed by Tristram Shapeero.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1372311478, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7353945462f8a9572745b75b03006a8661b3e69c9d5d9515384942a1c6200919", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "8 January 1999", "matched_aliases": ["8 January 1999", "1999"], "query_id": "test3229", "question_hash": "482be9160d7f16b3fae9ab56f7143972007af38c7f1bf2555d0b7c925528baad", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "50655aa48b527e58cd511b2dc4832cb8f8ff3a9f0ea40cbf47c98bbe56efc15f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2133285014, "similarity": 0.15384615384615385, "source_content_hash": "8fb7875cba28c203cbf6274c19ad7a3214e868ba2b6f433067d124c3345f9073", "source_hash": "a54ec41f06adb93ce003b4fd573ea4b305c06d5e4d32f7ffae332fdfa45799af", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "580c6570ad6c5095588fd78c12728f7a1d91b6301ceb38f4dbcdf14702eb4fda", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "determinis