{"doc_id": "doc110879", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Virginia Dare (born August 18, 1587, date of death unknown) was the first English child born in a New World English overseas possession, and was named after the territory of Virginia, her birthplace. Her parents were Ananias Dare and Eleanor White (also spelled Ellinor or Elyonor).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 334074098, "similarity": 0.9894736842105263, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f9f2c268ccf94781b511c284eca60f356a4bbe5150702f2f49983c75e4648bde", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Virginia Dare", "matched_aliases": ["Virginia Dare"], "query_id": "test3244", "question_hash": "2b786391ce0d87e18d7c8d15fbe911bab5d4954cb7bbd6e87db65bc5e8a2bdb7", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "8e3a304b239b4619f4eaa902012e7e1de3b811cb4d331cbf1af3bbbc4cdcf1bf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 837934950, "similarity": 0.13636363636363635, "source_content_hash": "f8223f8f10305536dd38ad45c3ca0966ae3187431b427242708eb4b14aab1d77", "source_hash": "1b65a8f61574ba30d17bb880f782f4ca1d633b8b52341f42813d89eb5e92dca0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4965aae587890387ab139bfa3d5f00e2e99f8de3b94bd1a16653894c0c1a9e35", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110911", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Originally, abiding by the recommendations and prohibitions of the Word of Wisdom was not considered mandatory: it explicitly declares itself to be \"not by commandment or constraint\".[20] In February 1834, however, Joseph Smith proposed a resolution before the high council of the church that stated, \"No official member in this Church is worthy to hold an office after having the word of wisdom properly taught him; and he, the official member, neglecting to comply with and obey it.\"[21] This resolution was accepted unanimously by the council.[21]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1280660674, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "1731362da1d3cea22aec81e4218235575dcd0efe9b19c0760732f8299496174c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "February 1834", "matched_aliases": ["February 1834"], "query_id": "test3245", "question_hash": "ba2a060b68fb408be38c4dcfa5dbb9b14aef113a518755a872508ce0755573ca", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5b1235e46abde8751f41e0b3e5c28610f7b8ec8b52974e73be52bdc08963c147", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 996434909, "similarity": 0.6259842519685039, "source_content_hash": "c53f676da6b8ef3c6220555f1d9742b10d6853fb3c8081406bdd4e2856479bff", "source_hash": "e8d48f29eb8044af2f5e1e5f6f2a92a617a1d620a479e83c1acad98c207b9f88", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "41eed0332384b276f252d03e687b4bfc9dfea791a8307135dc32ca2443bb2041", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc110971", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "A tradition on the \"kettle\" started in 1891, in San Francisco, by Salvation Army officer Captain Joseph McFee. Captain McFee, resolving to provide a free Christmas dinner to the poor of San Francisco, remembered a sight he saw in Liverpool, England. From his days as a sailor McFee remembered a large pot displayed on the Stage Landing, called \"Simpson's Pot.\" The pot took in donations put in by passersby. Taking this idea, McFee asked for permission from San Francisco city authorities to place a crab pot and tripod at the Oakland ferry landing. The kettle - and McFee's call of \"Keep the Pot Boiling!\" - drew in passengers and donations.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 461840265, "similarity": 0.9976689976689976, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ea06df81c487469cc7f8912081dcaa3242c362851dcf196dd29af4f63fd38439", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "San Francisco", "matched_aliases": ["San Francisco", "in San Francisco"], "query_id": "test3248", "question_hash": "3a0a9c6fbb84bec871c7e7cc5b5e99f926101f1dd1f6a52b8a5d5c4bc79b8cdd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "5d06b81b2c619ed44c9c00ebf3b8f8cb5370ce448e6fae1c42b401d9b927ddfe", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 730853640, "similarity": 0.32592592592592595, "source_content_hash": "edf2f6fd89ce65d5d553ca02d81ddb27a23dbdf33613f1785b3b04a3cc5f0d13", "source_hash": "d2989fbbbb305d690a35ff5bab8882e992b5f6c06c4074fdc979342bd6d2abb9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "19f0fe53f307f2d4fc0bb506194cd1f0358b890989a9f4a1e6f7476d6ae2784f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "valida