{"doc_id": "doc111607", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Written by Wayne Brathwaite, Barry Eastmond, Mutt Lange and Billy Ocean, the song was used as the theme song for the Michael Douglas film, The Jewel of the Nile, the sequel to the hit blockbuster film, Romancing the Stone. The saxophone solo is by Vernon Jeffrey Smith.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1142414451, "similarity": 0.9944547134935305, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b55d2d784d8506d79111b68191c516518c88bf0824b8a054d11e762a0f238aed", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "The Jewel of the Nile", "matched_aliases": ["The Jewel of the Nile"], "query_id": "test3265", "question_hash": "90151630bcd91b5745a9358362e0bb64fd93b33880a5acb028a31b549fb6d205", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "54dd4f470118068565bf6894f64aa57070b47498efb584905e3655d9dde084d5", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 629266834, "similarity": 0.6612903225806451, "source_content_hash": "2f89cf25579abb08b5dc281bac8c845198aaff00602d87be5b4d275a53a94b6d", "source_hash": "d52970db0201073e4669263cb6d308e39705aed3c35849ff9b2bb1869c2590f4", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e743fca442d252014017bf3f2fdc67b80320d66b02b5c8ededc19cc8cf9cabb3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc111663", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Great Lakes is the largest group of freshwater lakes on Earth by total area, and second largest by total volume containing 21% of the world's surface fresh water by volume.[2][3][4] The total surface is 94,250 square miles (244,106 km2), and the total volume (measured at the low water datum) is 5,439 cubic miles (22,671 km3)[5], a bit less than the volume of Lake Baikal (23,615 km³). Due to their sea-like characteristics (rolling waves, sustained winds, strong currents, great depths, and distant horizons) the five Great Lakes have also long been referred to as inland seas.[6] Lake Superior is the second largest lake in the world by area, and Lake Michigan is the largest lake that is entirely within one country.[7][8][9][10]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 521442342, "similarity": 0.9972862957937585, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "eadabb30b075c05654468d81471bf92c357df92ceeadaceac04816dde55ff7f7", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Lake Superior", "matched_aliases": ["Lake Superior"], "query_id": "test3270", "question_hash": "ab14091ffe3fb9c85f8a8ac719d00ef32b45894f72d0d698cd3dbe0594125801", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ea429ced078cca54584c5dc717d898adfa71bd550ed3120deea3b21dd90e97df", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1741954801, "similarity": 0.07510917030567686, "source_content_hash": "45877b1f42a59cc7ac357daff1fd011cde78fddd0e712c53e9cc8370678906ee", "source_hash": "70047927422f9c6c3016b8d4a5f17a2191c9f7e4455bfe8fe6197b15f99b9340", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e9592cc33630b7db5567ba094e48384ef4189bb6b4129503fea22b781b5fac62", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc111735", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "During World War I, the German Empire was one of the Central Powers that lost the war. It began participation in the conflict after the declaration of war against Serbia by its ally, Austria-Hungary. German forces fought the Allies on both the eastern and western fronts, although German territory itself remained relatively safe from widespread invasion for most of the war, except for a brief period in 1914 when East Prussia was invaded. A tight blockade imposed by the Royal Navy caused severe food shortages in the cities, especially in the winter of 1916–17, known as the Turnip Winter. At the end of the war, Germany's defeat and widespread popular discontent triggered the German Revolution of 1918–19 which overthrew the monarchy and established the Weimar Republic.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1250319422, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d9a9f57e92f5f9de1a4b896e1c650cdb7662d699c2480126fc8627eaa9e29b29", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Austria-Hungary", "matched_aliases": ["Austria-Hungary"], "query_id": "test3271", "question_hash": "201b13be7543d59ba1969ac1cefa3fc4513e6f69f206f47961f8584153ec01bc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e68af9393d0e86d3103e543bb206896376cc283517759bc272538b4f8bdc13c7", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1718443194, "similarity": 0.1627260083449235, "source_content_hash": "33d6b51daf8a389988e9a68dd517190ac6a0d78d1b077e6d3711d1b87e8e5cff", "source_hash": "9daabe983c9291eaf2dc1898f1b0b1d34bd4df716b5f91fb933b3120ac96cf7a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4cc97cea6ada747cf59d568ed80eb1e6a7f929607f9cb722898b49c81cdba80b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "m