{"doc_id": "doc112806", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Erika Mitchell Leonard (born 7 March 1963),[1] known by her pen name E. L. James, is an English author. She wrote the bestselling erotic romance trilogy Fifty Shades of Grey, Fifty Shades Darker, and Fifty Shades Freed,[2][3] along with the companion novels Grey: Fifty Shades of Grey as Told by Christian and Darker: Fifty Shades Darker as Told by Christian; and under the name Snowqueen's Icedragon the Twilight fan fiction \"Master of the Universe\" that was the basis for the Fifty Shades trilogy.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 535120116, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "03fda103dbd60d0560d69aa3a128ad8a7c5700dcf59283706ee560b517739c31", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Erika Mitchell Leonard", "matched_aliases": ["Erika Mitchell Leonard", "E. L. James"], "query_id": "test3299", "question_hash": "700cd2cdd9a0ca9e067922f017e25d753ea23e6da2ece731155376d78f476549", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "135c5286c9a47810e96f960fbce0b7fd7faefc2f4adb4c0aa97fe8bc3d244f62", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1160420604, "similarity": 0.315893385982231, "source_content_hash": "6509424d471213bf792209367de66ee3acaa3ad268b4fe496d15963df5728fc0", "source_hash": "1e8a5c915db3d1e7fb418fe3601364afc3807ca97372abc9420ff971798ad057", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0a5f4c1c0cf0af9ba2f576c07b43230620b8aa62d764f737b4967af12b1176a9", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc112841", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Until the 1980s media relied primarily upon print and analog broadcast models, such as those of television and radio. The last twenty-five years have seen the rapid transformation into media which are predicated upon the use of digital technologies, such as the Internet and video games. However, these examples are only a small representation of new media. The use of digital computers has transformed the remaining 'old' media, as suggested by the advent of digital television and online publications. Even traditional media forms such as the printing press have been transformed through the application of technologies such as image manipulation software like Adobe Photoshop and desktop publishing tools.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1718341087, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Until the 1980s, media relied primarily upon print and analog broadcast models, such as those of television and radio. The last twenty-five years have seen the rapid transformation into media which are predicated upon the use of digital technologies, such as the Internet and video games. However, these examples are only a small representation of new media. The use of digital computers has transformed the remaining 'old' media, as suggested by the advent of digital television and online publications. Even traditional media forms such as the printing press have been transformed through the application of technologies such as image manipulation software like Adobe Photoshop and desktop publishing tools.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1773765134, "similarity": 0.9992942836979535, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5fce3e1e4aca8851337eef558ebba58f37cbc5666124161357f86118727ef3bd", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "the 1980s", "matched_aliases": ["the 1980s"], "query_id": "test3302", "question_hash": "695176598c0695bfbd8f9a9764501e1786b64a4784a0152eb9b07dad18ce54e4", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "93359b93c0e03857eaf0e805cac632522913da84820efee70876c03899829956", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1089206570, "similarity": 0.4484038604305865, "source_content_hash": "b59621b43184148e6123430e7829da207d6679872d72b34107dc732a940991ca", "source_hash": "1d9fd1cef1c43330200335cb6a9ef06f7633d99e897936da4db1e242c60b5875", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d73fced4f63d27b3b1b9085742f65e804ee9e7bd9aab14acdc7874b6ff003fd1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc112884", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "\"It's Gonna Take a Miracle\" is a popular song written by Teddy Randazzo, Bobby Weinstein, and Lou Stallman. It was first an R&B hit in 1965 for The Royalettes, who reached the Top 30 on the U.S. R&B chart[1] and peaked at number 41 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 and number 37 on Cash Box.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 9885256, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "10b7d63b46bdad4c42c8b5e73526a1a19c20827605e97baf6e868a3ef7b6d366", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "The Royalettes", "matched_aliases": ["The Royalettes"], "query_id": "test3303", "question_hash": "0cfd26176c4db94a21f54027d1f86894e124b94711e19510602c8132aca96c19", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "ad5d8aed94513440b89f5b9a13888313f3a1d3e832541a32f426af90c27b9071", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1343008353, "similarity": 0.49914529914529915, "source_content_hash": "9232ac188a56d8d53513d54634615668882fbce0a25675b4a12349b40432f422", "source_hash": "de43cd610941c1169b7e9566e374a6527b224862897497e3d540218e7b63ed0f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a10d1b066a5e050f764bd85b88177334d45a215abc657ec06b661a327bd880e0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc112941", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Space Shuttle was a partially reusable low Earth orbital spacecraft system operated by the U.S. National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA), as part of the Space Shuttle program. Its official program name was Space Transportation System (STS), taken from a 1969 plan for a system of reusable spacecraft of which it was the only item funded for development.[10] The first of four orbital test flights occurred in 1981, leading to operational flights beginning in 1982. In addition to the prototype whose completion was cancelled, five complete Shuttle systems were built and used on a total of 135 missions from 1981 to 2011, launched from the Kennedy Space Center (KSC) in Florida. Operational missions launched numerous satellites, interplanetary probes, and the Hubble Space Telescope (HST); conducted science experiments in orbit; and participated in construction and servicing of the International Space Station. The Shuttle fleet's total mission time was 1322 days, 19 hours, 21 minutes and 23 seconds.[11]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1368164711, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7489ce223685c6fa7fad63bb4088646057807c5acd29a6340adfeb5573e72c4e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Florida", "matched_aliases": ["Florida"], "query_id": "test3307", "question_hash": "5d226efd1ad2a11a1b6fa8d8f90e97b2b8847a9dec2f49adbc9aecf29a3140f3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f54f3fc3f333a3b3b22362fd3ee5b3e5ab6038143bca43f6a2b8e9e4ed428487", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 846874524, "similarity": 0.36013986013986016, "source_content_hash": "4863628da455d73a23055fc89163a64bde3f04a0180fef923f840a5a19096c3a", "source_hash": "eba4c1783d87fe55d26f8adf1097cc7c8848baa270acf46c42404eb617fa1495", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "8056d48908e6e1891a402002cb82245c4c014c3219a923fc85359dbdc25f03d0", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc113096", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Buckwheat Boyz was an American musical group founded by Marcus Bowens and Jermaine Fuller, with the later addition of J.J. O'Neal and Dougy Williams. The Buckwheat Boyz were signed by Koch Records, and recorded their first and only full-length record. From this self-titled album, the song \"Peanut Butter Jelly Time\" became popular on the Internet after a flash music video featuring an animated dancing banana was created. The popularity of the song increased as it was featured on television shows such as The Proud Family, Family Guy, and Regular Show.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 506597692, "similarity": 0.9973238180196253, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ffd40a29959a611ed9a58081697bbbfae123e1869ba5c4a23db95fb19e13fbd0", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Buckwheat Boyz", "matched_aliases": ["Buckwheat Boyz"], "query_id": "test3309", "question_hash": "da80180897b7e30f94694c1b999f54ff470dd6713b1852bda6ff35be247f9d08", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e59967bcb7e00eece52479bd819a8dee098bf6d5b3e63bf509726fd04e543a32", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 229933354, "similarity": 0.15866797257590598, "source_content_hash": "fa4d91c47b28d0405357cc3c4b937852f88ec6b36ec02f6c99b909c6d9f5d104", "source_hash": "a2649e1c18b001b20da0ff6e39aff83a257b5194baeca968c571b35a8416a82e", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ed7e3e40ff06b9fd174b5c54cdc94c29e0f5c8fb908a8045716d81f685b2238c", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231