{"doc_id": "doc114060", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Eyjafjallajökull (Icelandic pronunciation [ˈeɪjaˌfjatlaˌjœːkʏtl̥] (listen)), (English pronunciation: ei-ya-fyat-LA-yer-kitle), English Island Mountain Glacier,[2] is one of the smaller ice caps of Iceland, north of Skógar and west of Mýrdalsjökull. The ice cap covers the caldera of a volcano with a summit elevation of 1,651 metres (5,417 ft). The volcano has erupted relatively frequently since the last glacial period, most recently in 2010.[3][4]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1788830237, "similarity": 0.9944506104328524, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "91386b157a8ff9281d2b937176977196dba932d9110d0fa1bcf922ea30e7dc11", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Eyjafjallajökull", "matched_aliases": ["Eyjafjallajökull"], "query_id": "test3336", "question_hash": "638b48bba4ca6d92bc76ae5b39ddf55a2cb8a81bf963e8914755c40170ff32a0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "00662bdf5615e6c82a87394e7c4eb2ad89a5680424d99f8b9a6c098123c97149", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 72722023, "similarity": 0.300709219858156, "source_content_hash": "1b53326a59c315489e219f1d2dec4751d44155ddafdd8fde27eb9738a6f62c0e", "source_hash": "e62c062772727221ab7fbcbdc301d706bce47eb68ad44ea480b5e2763209c9e1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a23a73c78500e84f2c1b466cf69b995790214b824d8413120b199a585708027b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc114114", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Orinoco River is one of the longest rivers in South America at 2,140 kilometres (1,330 mi). Its drainage basin, sometimes known as the Orinoquia, covers 880,000 square kilometres (340,000 sq mi), with 76.3 percent of it in Venezuela and the remainder in Colombia. It is the fourth largest river in the world by discharge volume of water. The Orinoco River and its tributaries are the major transportation system for eastern and interior Venezuela and the llanos of Colombia. The Orinoco River is extremely diverse, and hosts a wide variety of flora and fauna.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1870230250, "similarity": 0.9928952042628775, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Orinoco River is situated within South America, where it stands as one of the continent's longest waterways, stretching a total of 2,140 kilometres. This major fluid body drains an area known as the Orinoquia, which spans 880,000 square kilometres and is divided between Venezuela and Colombia. The river ranks as the fourth largest in the world by the volume of water it discharges.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1630703831, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "47ba2e7970f1c6e765a6ad58c40f8baa2ab7b556f60040515bc73b87de462eb5", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "in South America", "matched_aliases": ["in South America"], "query_id": "test3339", "question_hash": "4f732217ef868d5f54f7e38b69bcf92d4de357654c85a1172b4f24595637e02a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "f5661fe885cc61f083ae06deacd61490bc9cbef89d11753507a34421aa191950", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 287336824, "similarity": 0.3203342618384401, "source_content_hash": "0f7e9f3fadc68ad6b2f3702c933c385668f6d8a2cdf0cd2cf131dcb80d9c2578", "source_hash": "7fadec0f4eec5a71c03d0be3ff08301a9880379ba