{"doc_id": "doc114683", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Of the companies amalgamated to form CTR, the most technologically significant was The Tabulating Machine Company, founded by Herman Hollerith, and specialized in the development of punched card data processing equipment. Hollerith's series of patents on tabulating machine technology, first applied for in 1884, drew on his work at the U.S. Census Bureau from 1879 to 1882. Hollerith was initially trying to reduce the time and complexity needed to tabulate the 1890 Census. His development of punched cards in 1886 set the industry standard for the next 80 years of tabulating and computing data input.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 727842190, "similarity": 0.989247311827957, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e0d33816f3db3527cb60515398a2caff408f855fd46be658dfc017bfb8ddcc6c", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Herman Hollerith", "matched_aliases": ["Herman Hollerith"], "query_id": "test3360", "question_hash": "602f1c4f594a39ec01af0397db2b9899118301e6db2094cad800b36882d247cd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "928a456a84c9d062dab5eb142ac28307c283c6c2c70ae33fff2c8e15fec29c4c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1223541341, "similarity": 0.5190713101160862, "source_content_hash": "39e0ee5545c2907e1be3dc2d7c827da62591b0748368de7f3f14c4296f230c94", "source_hash": "3d6acecd19c3b378c50c2bcf3863f940fa2a4b6b54cc53619283eeef0a5620ca", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "fb37cca54acb8dacc05fb08813202388d6db642711562d30992614774adbed42", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd