{"doc_id": "doc116565", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "H. L. Hunley, often referred to as Hunley, was a submarine of the Confederate States of America that played a small part in the American Civil War. Hunley demonstrated the advantages and the dangers of undersea warfare. She was the first combat submarine to sink a warship (USS Housatonic), although Hunley was not completely submerged and, following her successful attack, was lost along with her crew before she could return to base. The Confederacy lost 21 crewmen in three sinkings of Hunley during her short career. She was named for her inventor, Horace Lawson Hunley, shortly after she was taken into government service under the control of the Confederate States Army at Charleston, South Carolina.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1420943432, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "H. L. Hunley, often referred to as Hunley, was a submarine of the Confederate States of America that played a small part in the American Civil War. Hunley demonstrated the advantages and the dangers of undersea warfare. She was the first combat submarine to sink a warship (USS Housatonic), although Hunley was not completely submerged and, following her successful attack, was lost along with her crew before she could return to base. The Confederacy lost 21 crewmen in three sinkings of Hunley during her short career. She was named for her inventor, Horace Lawson Hunley, shortly after she was taken into government service under the control of the Confederate States Army at Charleston, South Carolina.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 131866194, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "2ded30cd3b65ffc33b4e1c976abb6d0458a5f1082d4fe8f149629c6bd08382e0", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Horace Lawson Hunley", "matched_aliases": ["Horace Lawson Hunley"], "query_id": "test3428", "question_hash": "a75952f5a390b4aa1538624140bc3c4af395f422cb91145fba4021e24b3fa4bc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "83e0cde5b694dc0b9cd6db8288bd8d751943d3cf593bee52c887187d3a980aec", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1859472359, "similarity": 0.0141287284144427, "source_content_hash": "c0d57ac183cba8364ce63f1a1f999bdf092166496a6319eddaacdbaa0c9a04b9", "source_hash": "2518ddd0a9a0ddbea494221242aacdbbb5bddf52a15449dac8ead2fc943a122a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a2400cbbb8df20469e606e22592b4dd163a9dc6c152b5ebf7201a53ba0b7687e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc116605", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the general election on November 7, 2017, Democratic nominee Ralph Northam defeated Republican nominee Ed Gillespie, winning by the largest margin for a Democrat since 1985. Northam will become the 73rd governor of Virginia, and take office on January 13, 2018.[4] The election had the highest voter turnout percentage in a Virginia gubernatorial election in twenty years with 47% of the state's constituency casting their ballot.[1]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 579902230, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the general election on November 7, 2017, Democratic nominee Ralph Northam defeated Republican nominee Ed Gillespie, winning by the largest margin for a Democrat since 1985. Northam will become the 73rd governor of Virginia, and take office on January 13, 2018.[4] The election had the highest voter turnout percentage in a Virginia gubernatorial election in twenty years with 47% of the state's constituency casting their ballot.[1]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1412827222, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "c77cf7e05e45cbc5a46443b542eea918950fc46507c9f3b65ea343bc196dc243", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Ralph Northam", "matched_aliases": ["Ralph Northam", "Democratic nominee Ralph Northam"], "query_id": "test3429", "question_hash": "1b947046257166d0052d2fbe8a99fa6ccb763e3fcaf46600e567ab1e78a599f6", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "e9124dee6a5c6d2eb9e246d925cbed752c562045819b5086643024ff4348b339", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 646699254, "similarity": 0.7960308710033076, "source_content_hash": "0c1faa28b3a66b93463e48d7b2283b5aaf43c5acb0e6b7e4b1719dbd32160647", "source_hash": "e3b1c270d65d64f71ea00fe9bbd5ee90e3191c0513f37134a23c701fc06570ce", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e1f39c626f412ad9f6aa4b4d68d0df1e551966f18efc97dceb2aae2cd9380933", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc116741", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On election day, as the districts were drawn to favor Douglas' party, the Democrats won 40 seats in the state house of Representatives, and the Republicans won 35. In the state senate, Republicans held 11 seats, and Democrats held 14. Stephen A. Douglas was reelected by the legislature, 54-46, even though Lincoln's Republicans won the popular vote with a percentage of 50.6%, or by 3,402 votes. This election occurred during a period when widespread media coverage of the debates greatly raised Lincoln's national profile, making him a viable candidate for nomination as the Republican candidate in the upcoming 1860 presidential election. He would go on to secure both the nomination and the presidency, beating Douglas (as the Northern Democratic candidate), among others, in the process.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 414232355, "similarity": 0.9608220937700707, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e34edae9a74dbc149abe7a63d724a9a67fb71bea42745d13fed55d3023da55d6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Stephen A. Douglas", "matched_aliases": ["Stephen A. Douglas"], "query_id": "test3433", "question_hash": "a4d6be32b44b538bd25351498290b6c33245ea0393c98b635054d0f8a07b4563", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "08dfd2d781e5be00defd6b80055d79ecbc7a8d1fb7c4065ca94ef3d39036b110", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 289631083, "similarity": 0.08821502412129566, "source_content_hash": "dde8bf95d97bf2302229f53a47bb72ac332bec0e8236d6a4be08e613dd0c884c", "source_hash": "bd998dc6afc528dad8c8de3f105221171390b515a984695255d0760249e7cdcf", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5f1400c5c7298796490af256d14a6d6aa6be0b594888020a3fb4c1ef24982739", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc116745", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The University of Wisconsin–Madison (also known as University of Wisconsin, Wisconsin, UW, or regionally as UW–Madison, or simply Madison) is a public research university located in Madison, Wisconsin, United States. Founded when Wisconsin achieved statehood in 1848, UW–Madison is the official state university of Wisconsin, and the flagship campus of the University of Wisconsin System. It was the first public university established in Wisconsin and remains the oldest and largest public university in the state. It became a land-grant institution in 1866.[6] The 933-acre (378 ha) main campus includes four National Historic Landmarks.[7]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1742907081, "similarity": 0.9921630094043887, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "59a01a3834e1e2a0e653d98aaebafc878df8577618ef0d2eeebac6c97a03c599", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Madison, Wisconsin", "matched_aliases": ["Madison, Wisconsin"], "query_id": "test3434", "question_hash": "0f4ffb4afd505f490d973fe12e9cd73788e886e5ac78de5a6a2b524a389da547", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "2d3641f1ad89f5c8830fbe83727ca42f2ad72b579182b4c40273862fa1b8cfda", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 292174166, "similarity": 0.3613655287260616, "source_content_hash": "e7925c7a59e0c179f36988ce1d96d2a21c1396a66249bf0b06b6ac596e5413f5", "source_hash": "2a48e189d321a4107e5a34a339c96638481d2eae7b7ba965b6cac7e5246ab09f", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6c7aeca442d6513e84020edd5f5cae157660a156d54c6e778138103ea8eca8bd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc116825", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The signing of the United States Declaration of Independence took place primarily on August 2, 1776, at the Pennsylvania State House, Independence Hall in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. The 56 delegates to the Second Continental Congress represented the 13 former colonies which had declared themselves the \"United States of America,\" and they endorsed the Declaration of Independence which the Congress had approved on July 4, 1776. The Declaration proclaimed that the former Thirteen Colonies then at war with Great Britain were now a sovereign, independent nation and thus no longer a part of the British Empire. The signers' names are grouped by state, with the exception of President of the Continental Congress John Hancock; the states are arranged geographically from north to south.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1340523410, "similarity": 0.9853782581055308, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2551c97a7cecb7e8275f8e2bcc2334a53c81eecdbf9f1fbb90b649d56a911347", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "August 2, 1776", "matched_aliases": ["August 2, 1776"], "query_id": "test3435", "question_hash": "2ea2909df18f22e7f24e4e76c1a392ed4df26dfe1f47df24b0f9c348b5eb6f35", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "69b5e1655e157997af5d8773fe33bed330a7cc4bd3bad39e1c181fea95dadb33", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1641817629, "similarity": 0.3149480415667466, "source_content_hash": "667a7f6d2e539a88e189893e556d19f6e4633207e3c18ef8ac978a2e30e66d4b", "source_hash": "1d07b98c4cbd7a65c487f4f5447535157f917284ff7ea581c996417c88c9bfaf", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "32534f36ed0b30d92414a21751cd83ad22105e976616885ded42ea919f383299", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc116826", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The final draft of the Declaration was approved by the Continental Congress on July 4, although the date of its signing has long been disputed. Most historians have concluded that it was signed on August 2, 1776, nearly a month after its adoption, and not on July 4 as is commonly believed.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 224019597, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "d1ffdcbf5ec56f00c24cb94051e612ff3ad7cc7d4f373fd4ac9bb25c6db3c207", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "August 2, 1776", "matched_aliases": ["August 2, 1776"], "query_id": "test3435", "question_hash": "2ea2909df18f22e7f24e4e76c1a392ed4df26dfe1f47df24b0f9c348b5eb6f35", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "1c589efff508588234fe7f597c8905017739fcb208a1b1bc7492e86c898e07dd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 818563558, "similarity": 0.21233859397417504, "source_content_hash": "c1ffd0f051423dd8f6f8be3b40b512b21bf2915f35e5e7d7cf659a98d399fff6", "source_hash": "f44df0b4ca695b7989c270c9bea75104541e43e8af237e3c2ae97c53f9b42bd3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ede9866ede2201be459fbe4b4059389503244b6359d701187b3da0c0355631c3", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc117036", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Henry Purcell (/ˈpɜːrsəl/ or /pɜːrˈsɛl/; c. 10 September 1659 – 21 November 1695) was an English composer. Although incorporating Italian and French stylistic elements into his compositions, Purcell's legacy was a uniquely English form of Baroque music. He is generally considered to be one of the greatest English composers; no other native-born English composer approached his fame until Edward Elgar, Ralph Vaughan Williams, William Walton and Benjamin Britten in the 20th century.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 186982177, "similarity": 0.9887640449438202, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b28d9a33b48a28e661f82bdaafaf083415deab40aad20dc0233b3c758e4ff725", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Henry Purcell", "matched_aliases": ["Henry Purcell"], "query_id": "test3437", "question_hash": "edc33fd56718f31e4f77d413abe0d7b98de94edc8fe6a5253caa1820d9023f7d", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "row_hash": "79afe882a70ffca9f5718356a8808bd9037f9915e6dca0b90405c7db43b96ebf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1079098092, "similarity": 0.24242424242424243, "source_content_hash": "fa401a50cf88bf278eb5625c72379195149891a79bc3a66312b0fdd081809c7c", "source_hash": "c8d601f60abf2e6d0e5e350777b54be9eb70b03b8ca38c9f75a4a1392c8ff5f3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "66ce16905606b526d39426aa6c4174850814c5fb50f4aa1b091307a0a2706bb4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
