{"doc_id": "doc6916", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "A 7-kilometer (4 mi) road named the \"Spirit Way\" (pinyin: Shéndào) leads into the complex, lined with statues of guardian animals and officials, with a front gate consisting of a three-arches, painted red, and called the \"Great Red Gate\". The Spirit Way, or Sacred Way, starts with a huge stone memorial archway lying at the front of the area. Constructed in 1540, during the Ming dynasty, this archway is one of the biggest stone archways in China today.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 320459145, "similarity": 0.9978021978021978, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f259f096bfaa7b94b060bb58e3365b5022303156746c9f5e92ddf40c74c55517", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "\"Spirit Way\"", "matched_aliases": ["\"Spirit Way\""], "query_id": "test189", "question_hash": "1415389fc62e1b71d48b2198c119a9ff1bf30a5ef12cb88947523567ef902257", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "e20abac6a14b6b30b00a9975a1b1c5b27fed1dc8ad2806121465a608fd12718f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 41065659, "similarity": 0.4980744544287548, "source_content_hash": "b83d136f949b545b9d63450c2112784dfee0eaaba81608fa4e366062a11ad41d", "source_hash": "4a4345194470bdc35bffc70afdb398c9b5b376e4156ca6007822e7ee58338a6b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0c96f7446f32c4be1a92db40bb8d1901d48d80620781b51326d04e5cdd2dc549", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc16678", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The lingam is a column-like or oval (egg-shaped) symbol of Shiva, the Formless All-pervasive Reality, made of stone, metal, or clay. The Shiva Linga is a symbol of Lord Shiva – a mark that reminds of the Omnipotent Lord, which is formless.[7] In Shaivite Hindu temples, the linga is a smooth cylindrical mass symbolising Shiva. It is found at the centre of the temple, often resting in the middle of a rimmed, disc-shaped structure, a representation of Shakti.[3]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 945794449, "similarity": 0.9967637540453075, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "137b3d02f386de16a84ef8bb3b4e13f3104cee2cd02a6739668f5cc6cfe13d48", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "reminds of the Omnipotent Lord", "matched_aliases": ["reminds of the Omnipotent Lord"], "query_id": "test448", "question_hash": "948b5f0ed52e3ea53daec3af37e2a43bb1ffb9926b5b67086ea90d4864780f06", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "069d112d5a0003843e5968515b5bbce4aa2f44eef1495edbee7dace1e8a23cb5", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 893469119, "similarity": 0.12888377445339472, "source_content_hash": "e4e02e484b7d61d0263e79fa99dd49d5ef23b153e5c89fdd30c9452ca2039860", "source_hash": "46892ef16b82f6830e9f6ec1967fc2f4a89e5e4b527b99e1efe588d3a626a3d8", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "90431a8d82e6b11438cba8d4ba195cdeb8028a531a9551ea6f083bb9fcb8278a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal"