{"doc_id": "doc20449", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Wurtz reaction, named after Charles-Adolphe Wurtz, is a coupling reaction in organic chemistry, organometallic chemistry and recently inorganic main group polymers, whereby two alkyl halides are reacted with sodium metal in dry ether solution to form a higher alkane:", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1477717123, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "ee4adf2735bdbcbb5e182f5ca0840f89f68943dce51092e962e9fa15821b2e22", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "to form a higher alkane", "matched_aliases": ["to form a higher alkane"], "query_id": "test563", "question_hash": "8af00b5ea1f5673ac1f389d30ea75700f0059e961a594c71d63ec7bd6359ff02", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "aea226e2379df215ea4b6e4d23fc64b598841ced723845c37e323d1ad25b3c92", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 234861167, "similarity": 0.4644808743169399, "source_content_hash": "42d19dc1c44c8f5a91a2e9225d2ceaf93b34d91c1470d2b462583cc507c4d842", "source_hash": "02ab39fbf41dde29bcfb7e9473fa779d7c16fc9137e9db28bed1353ceeb2c806", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0ab7cfaf046e855dc78381f11bc649015223fad4720a410e48b2a788da6b8ca4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc22915", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Robinson is an English language patronymic surname, originating in England. It means \"son of Robin (a diminutive of Robert)\". There are similar surname spellings such as Robison and Robeson. Robinson is the 15th most common surname in the United Kingdom.[1] According to the 1990 United States Census, Robinson was the twentieth most frequently encountered surname among those reported, accounting for 0.23% of the population.[2]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2040155069, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The surname Robinson is an English language patronymic, which indicates it means \"son of Robin,\" where Robin is a diminutive form of the name Robert. This specific name derives from England, and it is the 15th most common surname in the United Kingdom. According to the 1990 United States Census, Robinson was the twentieth most frequently encountered surname among those reported, accounting for 0.23% of the population.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1139963847, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "22fbcc41d5d90f73bc69a3b4cfdb98a060d20b35f8bf244cea002dcba89f6823", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "English language patronymic surname", "matched_aliases": ["English language patronymic surname"], "query_id": "test639", "question_hash": "97bb26fd7aae47cfc7ccf0a7fe83f3ae272950e0ab3b74860fe4cae82bcaabf9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "7178d8de88d590b08ad00b08949002faec09ac75c7382ca3fafbb7bc0f76fb2f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 710567637, "similarity": 0.43037974683544306, "source_content_hash": "930d2d827eaa402727e0ed6ada5c39654c88dccaea1937f07ee2957c1f9cad50", "source_hash": "18f71e41c0841420b1f9421ccc3c56dfe6e9c6f64158fecf4be2111243633b35", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "12e8a418b6714115d79ea407a2f52e01238080e1223f21e20bfbcd7cb4985732", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc25371", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "At first, the government was reluctant to engage in propaganda campaigns, but pressure from the media, the business sector and advertisers who wanted direction persuaded the government to take an active role. Even so, the government insisted that its actions were not propaganda, but a means of providing information. These efforts were slowly and haphazardly formed into a more unified propaganda effort, although never to the level of World War I.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 787481095, "similarity": 0.9900771775082691, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "At first, the government was reluctant to engage in propaganda campaigns, but pressure from the media, the business sector and advertisers who wanted direction persuaded the government to take an active role. Even so, the government insisted that its actions were not propaganda, but a means of providing information. These efforts were slowly and haphazardly formed into a more unified propaganda effort, although never to the level of World War I.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1686759265, "similarity": 0.9900771775082691, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5768e618ce9fb737ab61337d20fe5ccbb262563a4aa1ef8f0f2222086055d6c4", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "the government", "matched_aliases": ["the government"], "query_id": "test710", "question_hash": "d6ba20ecc579832d5986f51b8ae305f6e5d71598fbd88a1e2a0c506520fddbdc", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "ccfd9eadb681df060f14498d9011662589bcf1afd9bf2d8291c9e9cd07a122f8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 608742605, "similarity": 0.02491506228765572, "source_content_hash": "02bf1486e7b94b53629241c9e9ae1c19318b3a4819615105757c816ac8eab2d0", "source_hash": "2a9d674cfcf8c9e44683efc7fac67aa72ce4dfa1dd8d135f7f069599f742822