{"doc_id": "doc45919", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In later seasons, it is revealed that he is a member of a group known as the Syndicate, a shadowy organization within the United States government. The episode \"Two Fathers\" reveals his birthname or alias as C.G.B. Spender, and that he was formerly married to Cassandra Spender, with whom he had a son, Jeffrey Spender. He recruits FBI Special Agent Diana Fowley to be a subordinate of his because she has a close relationship with Mulder. In \"One Son\", Jeffrey finds out that his father, the Smoking Man, forced his mother Cassandra to undergo medical treatments that led to several nervous breakdowns during his childhood years. When the Smoking Man finds out, he seemingly kills Jeffrey. Knowing of the colonization plan, the Alien rebels return to Earth to try to persuade the Syndicate to join their side against their war with the Colonists. Not believing in the strength of the Alien rebels, the Syndicate members meet at El Rico Air Base to be transported to a spaceship to survive the colonization. However, the rebels appear instead of the Colonists and kill all remaining chief members of the Syndicate. Together with Fowley, the Smoking Man escapes the destruction of the Syndicate. Later in the sixth season, there is more evidence that suggested that the Smoking Man is Mulder's biological father. Eventually in \"The Sixth Extinction II: Amor Fati\", Fowley comes in disagreement with him. Because of his plans to kill Mulder, Fowley helps Scully in her investigation to locate Mulder, which leads to her death. After the destruction of the Syndicate, the Smoking Man starts to operate as he wishes. However, his cancer resurfaces, and he begins using a wheelchair and has a tracheotomy. In the end, Alex Krycek and Marita Covarrubias betray him in the episode \"Requiem\", throwing him down a flight of stairs, where they presume him to be dead.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 311122148, "similarity": 0.9951768488745981, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "06a5a5c0a13162c7c63b2608578a36d22c2f21333f8d9aa5ee4671f3cba03876", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Later in the sixth season", "matched_aliases": ["in the sixth season"], "query_id": "test1295", "question_hash": "cec94ee7756602595380a3c80a8cbfe6ba150743a91deb754ddd0342d44be7a7", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "de274a9b63b2fccfc9813e8ace173877215ee0531895862143994dee150d19bb", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 899733049, "similarity": 0.09117361784675072, "source_content_hash": "a2ba9a51f5998020d56a8d6ebb91058a64e3e1dbdb4bc867941d49662c2ab338", "source_hash": "d82a5b06cd8349f06dae70a60db8a22099e7ad785f4b4b9ec0c55c3225520a5c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7601867ecd2d03d1565b4c18b6228f51103533213e2e89a1d22a43b3bc3feec2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc49209", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "As of 2017[update], the Bora Bora group has a permanent population of 10,605.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 87890732, "similarity": 0.9808917197452229, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "As of 2017[update], the Bora Bora group has a permanent population of 10,605.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1367229953, "similarity": 0.9808917197452229, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "3c0e792c93b3ba4d1b73d449a3e2ed62798e3b66df4acf66b4c2857bad63b63f", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "10,605", "matched_aliases": ["10,605"], "query_id": "test1387", "question_hash": "60f0fe073e490f90d79ce9d9c3aaea260f248c276ae6d22bbdfc160ea327d1f0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "4795373e4e26900f33e85add41e96320f6a31c5ba647a626ab4fe9835149094f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 117994515, "similarity": 0.6103896103896104, "source_content_hash": "fe30194726fc8e058c743321c374cb3eb6200a0428a55439e942e51c5cb1ba5b", "source_hash": "c8f03a2422916bc09f93be1ea9089c2dd330198eb119f9bad0674ccde22e22bd", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "123613abf7969767ad18986ecab5b32481ffa13627349fd7d64e740cf6f84d30", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc56020", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "A primary ossification center is the first area of a bone to start ossifying. It usually appears during prenatal development in the central part of each developing bone. In long bones the primary centers occur in the diaphysis/shaft and in irregular bones the primary centers occur usually in the body of the bone. Most bones have only one primary center (e.g. all long bones) but some irregular bones such as the os coxa (hip) and vertebrae have multiple primary centers.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1193413093, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "A primary ossification center represents the initial region where bone tissue begins to ossify. This developmental process typically occurs during the prenatal period, specifically located in the central portion of each developing bone. In long bones, these centers generally arise within the shaft, whereas in irregular bones they usually form in the main body of the bone. While most bones possess a single primary center, certain irregular bones like the hip and vertebrae may contain multiple centers.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 693210193, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "7c812f4ac86808b39882d987315bd27437a25fd8d1fe55ce007a494c8477dfae", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "prenatal development", "matched_aliases": ["prenatal development"], "query_id": "test1569", "question_hash": "b65c68e6347eb717252f459cb02084af34cd828c390b2141f2e95dab254ee414", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "178e47bd845ff1fef5bca1facb0e8550f3259445b65d6920a1e77fc5ea1a658a", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 631449726, "similarity": 0.05263157894736842, "source_content_hash": "5ba2c62820b1fa18a9cca4cc12ce505397343ca37de56d6394f04fba4af268e2", "source_hash": "926355df04a248fe6b571a514cd17ef49c445af49cdabdc72e4561b4bb75c5c2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "3a0c126e1f339e0de31a5b85d4d23d873560c005c8bfb4fc126d4c424e7bdd07", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc57962", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Large denominations of United States currency greater than $100 were circulated by the United States Treasury until 1969. Since then, U.S. dollar banknotes have only been issued in seven denominations: $1, $2, $5, $10, $20, $50, and $100.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1429053330, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Large denominations of United States currency greater than $100 were circulated by the United States Treasury until 1969. Since then, U.S. dollar banknotes have only been issued in seven denominations: $1, $2, $5, $10, $20, $50, and $100.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 373635262, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "7bc2db20d9fbc12b0bf96f0de4c49b54b1e8525d48d34a7294bd8e4d8d570c9c", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "$100", "matched_aliases": ["$100"], "query_id": "test1633", "question_hash": "9603dc68cacd6e397b71764fe5e71aea581ec22d407c385ed167364cb0680f9c", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "a2a043815e4dd538c83008f80234336d6bfc2efdb07dd2312a9bebd69d71e182", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 15661279, "similarity": 0.4019370460048426, "source_content_hash": "a05955d6b5ff75dd84c75ee467e9efbcdde776fa8cb2665b0e4f6c958eacec52", "source_hash": "69ee670c7315f437ff624856d8cc12a2fe1fbb8768476b920ac30ebab26ce3ed", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4a893ca84643f3cbf4e6036ee4a02d0e8dbda7919eebeb13e7a14a36bb301b8f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa72