{"doc_id": "doc70743", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Kelly Reno (born June 19, 1966, in Pueblo, Colorado) is a former child actor who was cast at age 11 in the role of Alec Ramsey, the young boy who is marooned on a deserted island along with a horse, in The Black Stallion (based on the novel by Walter Farley). The film was made in 1977.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1780280580, "similarity": 0.9711375212224108, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Kelly Reno (born June 19, 1966, in Pueblo, Colorado) is a former child actor who was cast at age 11 in the role of Alec Ramsey, the young boy who is marooned on a deserted island along with a horse, in The Black Stallion (based on the novel by Walter Farley). The film was made in 1977.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 111940500, "similarity": 0.9711375212224108, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "1baea73d8c16d2344098c666c5b8b2138c9d93f0886e7e3e0aa16e3c2f1cb7d8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Kelly Reno", "matched_aliases": ["Kelly Reno"], "query_id": "test2024", "question_hash": "3d0e1ba4fe29466466fa199835d826cec1a968e84ce03670adafeb86b5c7f94a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "da285187da00c3a84c9cfb13976b925b9cbfdfff0e099274098a7854a560004b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 196537622, "similarity": 0.5522875816993464, "source_content_hash": "410ad54e5372f2977b08fffa21e73d9aa9cfbb9d7190f98356f8a8cd1190fa44", "source_hash": "fd3a39bac82b6eeaf5dab4d8b5b073d392aefc1f80bb167eae7d01f9b250f347", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "949d56abbaba555ebd795832d631e067d4f533638ef8f84d7e44a0bd6cfcb3fc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc71418", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Despite the immediate area of Jamestown being uninhabited, the settlers were attacked less than two weeks after their arrival on May 14, by Paspahegh Indians who succeeded in killing one of the settlers and wounding eleven more. Within a month, James Fort covered an acre on Jamestown Island. By June 15, the settlers finished building the triangular James Fort. The wooden palisaded walls formed a triangle around a storehouse, church, and a number of houses. A week later, Newport sailed back for London on Susan Constant with a load of pyrite (\"foolsâ€™ gold\") and other supposedly precious minerals, leaving behind 104 colonists and Discovery.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 990307325, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Although the immediate vicinity of Jamestown was not previously inhabited, the first settlers were attacked within two weeks of their arrival on May 14. This attack was led by Paspahegh Indians, who managed to kill one of the new arrivals and wound eleven others. By June 15, the settlers had completed constructing the triangular James Fort on Jamestown Island. This wooden structure featured palisaded walls enclosing a storehouse, a church, and several houses. Additionally, a week later, the ship Newport returned to London via the Susan Constant carrying pyrite and other minerals, while leaving behind 104 colonists and the explorer John Smith.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1796346666, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "d638c4849e7247a1d7ea284bd372e725226e57236d8b4ccec5aeb6797c8a7e62", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "uninhabited", "matched_aliases": ["uninhabited"], "query_id": "test2051", "question_hash": "9571546504a605ea7591af837cae11bdb8668d0af072bef5cc4b519f623b5e43", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "59b34879f98b14150cc98b0954fd02b4b600fd7f13e7b8ebcca556fe8ea18a9b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1836559873, "similarity": 0.1971356360572873, "source_content_hash": "8f2daa84a53641b8061ad4f231637fd521bbedaba2f0500f1232c2cc62d57293", "source_hash": "ddebaad9def816b24eba7ab2347b4b40be8d08b5a4e0f207ea2974c50cb2087d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "8e169bc428c1a964b9f09a75118c3040a2a28942c624f5b89068632faeb01716", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc73468", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The season seven premiere reveals that JJ has returned to the Behavioral Analysis Unit, having received the training to become a full-time profiler, instead of the Media Liaison, a position which has been split between Hotch and Garcia.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1361063725, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The episode featuring Jennifer Jareau confirms that she has been promoted to a full-time profiler at the Behavioral Analysis Unit, a shift from her previous role as a media liaison that was shared between Hotch and Garcia.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 659378935, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "a4e096cffaa9200cb7ea8b345ed27068d64fe105b25b5a25320bbb0b19486384", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "season seven premiere", "matched_aliases": ["season seven premiere"], "query_id": "test2111", "question_hash": "d8cedae50bc19b8e2f5fb589b003f6a85efca560e93a237193e875098bc9aa37", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "d5d25a95864221d2d89fd235696e87c4e860079aedd10675e1e3c48ab701ea1d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 434617880, "similarity": 0.7892976588628763, "source_content_hash": "f3e263a691ef50975030b5315266d4958829c41331e8c1af7398da0eca6ed777", "source_hash": "e3813a51674200b869b2b2a5f4112254e438d8d760726cbf3e80d4a0e03dbb4a", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "9920d18461bd11af3ffcbdc4ec7a919c2370bac22b68f88b06e6c62e04359a65", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc75892", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In logical argument and mathematical proof, the therefore sign (∴) is generally used before a logical consequence, such as the conclusion of a syllogism. The symbol consists of three dots placed in an upright triangle and is read therefore. It is encoded at U+2234 ∴ therefore (HTML &#8756; · &there4;). For common use in Microsoft Office hold the ALT key and type \"8756\". While it is not generally used in formal writing, it is used in mathematics and shorthand. It is complementary to U+2235 ∵ because (HTML &#8757;).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1264217815, "similarity": 0.9942196531791907, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the realm of logical argumentation and mathematical proofs, the symbol ∴ (therefore) signals a logical consequence. This character, composed of three dots arranged within an upright triangle, is read as \"therefore.\" It corresponds to the U+2234 Unicode character (∴) and is also represented by the HTML entity &#8756; · &there4;. When typing in Microsoft Office, users can hold the ALT key and input \"8756\" to display the symbol. Although uncommon in formal writing, this notation frequently appears in mathematical contexts and shorthand. It stands in contrast to the U+2235 symbol (∵), which functions as its logical opposite.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 681677970, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "fdc3e0de8dd5f23062b4aff816eeafa7a726e8aa692cd85cc066d28cb51a951e", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "therefore sign", "matched_aliases": ["therefore sign"], "query_id": "test2175", "question_hash": "e8a27d59f3ff79cc9a4b9fc0c40527f523db4a8934e9b25077297253e3908d07", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "6a170e0838fe01969a177ede7617c8d142508b5eeba7af50a4e1c5f8958959b1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 852247964, "similarity": 0.0525328330206379, "source_content_hash": "ec60725afd8c85000817d2818d0cb68dffaa5d9d0fc7eeafe9818cbda2fd3e86", "source_hash": "724d47e1f65c6fe4cf3edf50328bed182b164f5341a5888e54566e4bece377f2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4989c3dd45818499a1673aefe61d1fbea7b47a98aa31b9f878d18cb8488286b4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc76390", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "A substitute good is one good that can be used instead of another. In consumer theory, substitute goods or substitutes are products that a consumer perceives as similar or comparable, so that having more of one product makes them desire less of the other product. Formally, X and Y are substitutes if, when the price of X rises, the demand for Y rises.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2079011246, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "02b653cc9837fa1361a7b7ada176087c81184c048a207961c08dfb6f17673ce0", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "A substitute good", "matched_aliases": ["A substitute good"], "query_id": "test2193", "question_hash": "4032332e1d2a3d33460cb0a522faf052b9cf6ffc2ad802bae1a851c13d68ff71", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "cefdbe29200dc631bf7e053e8cdea1151970c1654dedd884efb64456b3f7112c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1771722146, "similarity": 0.06408544726301736, "source_content_hash": "2ecc909dd74fcff58288901f7f0f9bce2a05d502b3aa85e261128cf9ac37ddb9", "source_hash": "d00ead247dda64e9b09671f7ce6b2029cd80eae5436a5e42fa9193da9ff84a0d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "66d181619c8e99fc70def8f8c9386f134359ccad72fb3750d1990498c2ac1f04", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc77010", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In C4 carbon fixation, the initial step in the light-independent reactions of photosynthesis involves the fixation of CO2 by the enzyme RuBisCO into 3-phosphoglycerate. However, due to the dual carboxylase and oxygenase activity of RuBisCo, some part of the substrate is oxidized rather than carboxylated, resulting in loss of substrate and consumption of energy, in what is known as photorespiration. In order to bypass the photorespiration pathway, C4 plants have developed a mechanism to efficiently deliver CO2 to the RuBisCO enzyme. They utilize their specific leaf anatomy where chloroplasts exist not only in the mesophyll cells in the outer part of their leaves but in the bundle sheath cells as well. Instead of direct fixation to RuBisCO in the Calvin cycle, CO2 is incorporated into a 4-carbon organic acid, which has the ability to regenerate CO2 in the chloroplasts of the bundle sheath cells. Bundle sheath cells can then utilize this CO2 to generate carbohydrates by the conventional C3 pathway.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 302415884, "similarity": 0.9815828770532603, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "8db7b21b5ff172037b2b99d703aef43fffe431207b33160d853411d5b24a83a7", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "3-phosphoglycerate", "matched_aliases": ["3-phosphoglycerate"], "query_id": "test2215", "question_hash": "46fe80781b5230ba011b1b48bf2dd62f0d925654bac068897dec400bd4815e58", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "1ff51b1546c2579303f9ffe32332524fdd98ac7abc90daa77ed9a48b5e87d730", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 418239944, "similarity": 0.19492025989367986, "source_content_hash": "5b49e202d116f22515b94227fa899a1143fe405a70fc95c0253c37a6bbe1f511", "source_hash": "3f408c8808b5203ebfa9f269aeb5e2a91524c7738d30911fb6db3efa684cfba5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "09b552fd3bec47baae6934446746d7e2bedb3588a0af19371f744e3b6e5a84e1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc83382", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Captain Phasma is a fictional character in the Star Wars franchise, portrayed by Gwendoline Christie. Introduced in Star Wars: The Force Awakens (2015), the first film in the Star Wars sequel trilogy, Phasma is the commander of the First Order's force of stormtroopers. Christie returned to the role in the next of the trilogy's films, Star Wars: The Last Jedi (2017). The character also made an additional appearance in Before the Awakening, an anthology book set before the events of The Force Awakens.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 2069685314, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c539f40759240cba27f1a5e1642206f9cb2b48ab60e4ab5cefcf32bdee1f8da7", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Gwendoline Christie", "matched_aliases": ["Gwendoline Christie"], "query_id": "test2413", "question_hash": "3f9f3e0995ab00b280212c5b3e0418cbfa4df46da7670494457fec7346f7953e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "c987e50bd01e6c0ed6ffdd344bc0ec06e4dfc96290273a19567d009ceb83a0fd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 266720079, "similarity": 0.3434739941118744, "source_content_hash": "d8070b2f05c4ddcebc26d7d32e573c291a45a2e17089cbc40d99e6f13b72d4be", "source_hash": "409c4e752126bdc6810661acabf6d356823f3ae717c3d36bd49d05a72eeaab85", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "d2b81ec0260569c3ddbf030fd1b9592b9365e59b0473c33e5a1756e1923b4884", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91419", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Jesse Wesley Williams (born August 5, 1981) is an American actor, director, teacher and activist, best known for his role as Dr. Jackson Avery on the ABC Television series Grey's Anatomy. He also appeared in the 2013 film The Butler as civil rights leader Rev. James Lawson. His other roles have included Holden in The Cabin in the Woods (2012); Officer Eddie Quinlan in Brooklyn's Finest (2009); and Leo in The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants 2 (2008).", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1930913762, "similarity": 0.9967141292442497, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "9e6bf286fde35c394195dad9fcacdca97d072f3d986841591b9470dec12f7431", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Jesse Wesley Williams", "matched_aliases": ["Jesse Wesley Williams"], "query_id": "test2668", "question_hash": "3398b0564e8d4534dccc874d31873ea94a348374ae56ff9c99e206e4762d3970", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "89d88cc32aaf00f49a4e8f0c4ef82e96ce6ed4bc1a535adf675be8b8e3348521", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1857731716, "similarity": 0.5053598774885145, "source_content_hash": "7f5d8c63e33ebe068c77503d77f305a0972754a019c4a2c225312c4bc85d81b7", "source_hash": "19ba71721ee66204f7cce63608c83e83be44ca82f6f4e7f8840636ec180de143", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "30ea215e40db035b06244f03dc1ce259aeca2cdb08b9d7e432e8e67c9cc1a613", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}