{"doc_id": "doc54520", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Set on the prosperous Long Island of 1922, The Great Gatsby provides a critical social history of America during the Roaring Twenties within its fictional narrative. That era, known for unprecedented economic prosperity, the evolution of jazz music flapper culture, new technologies in communication (motion pictures, broadcast radio, recorded music) forging a genuine mass culture; and bootlegging, along with other criminal activity, is plausibly depicted in Fitzgerald's novel. Fitzgerald uses many of these societal developments of the 1920s that were to build Gatsby's stories from many of the simple details like automobiles to broader themes like Fitzgerald's discreet allusions to the organized crime culture which was the source of Gatsby's fortune.[5] Fitzgerald depicts the garish society of the Roaring Twenties by placing the book's plotline within the historical context of the era.[6]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 386997388, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Set on the prosperous Long Island of 1922, The Great Gatsby provides a critical social history of America during the Roaring Twenties within its fictional narrative. That era, known for unprecedented economic prosperity, the evolution of jazz music flapper culture, new technologies in communication (motion pictures, broadcast radio, recorded music) forging a genuine mass culture; and bootlegging, along with other criminal activity, is plausibly depicted in Fitzgerald's novel. Fitzgerald uses many of these societal developments of the 1920s that were to build Gatsby's stories from many of the simple details like automobiles to broader themes like Fitzgerald's discreet allusions to the organized crime culture which was the source of Gatsby's fortune.[5] Fitzgerald depicts the garish society of the Roaring Twenties by placing the book's plotline within the historical context of the era.[6]", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1198468882, "similarity": 1.0, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "242afabfd938a5d45ead276e4127894de25e00b3d1bb210156379848a2abf7ac", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Long Island of 1922", "matched_aliases": ["Long Island of 1922"], "query_id": "test1524", "question_hash": "8678d35f8b1702656bf8bfb0fa1a752e095d990c283c40a8195da14defd75c61", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "11a0b020dbed60298b333fd846c66f1d23fae98ec74d343bc270d40531aa356d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1271697787, "similarity": 0.23460790667530784, "source_content_hash": "0c24a8531050c52ab7387d8201656372589877024bb8d44186f997f63b4a70ae", "source_hash": "1d1ff0976d6e47afe6cbbce60c62c574b0f8562bb452c65643e77666b5acddd5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e860cf6c9ebdf86317defaf0f3a62f2bb36784a41f2bf05483a22d4be7c1e3d1", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc84302", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "City & Guilds is an awarding body offering a large number of accredited qualifications mapped onto the Regulated Qualifications Framework (RQF), Credit and Qualifications Framework for Wales (CQFW) and Scottish Credit and Qualifications Framework (SCQF). As of November 2016, City & Guilds offers 2312 different regulated qualifications, more than any other awarding body. These cover entry level to level 7 on the RQF, with most qualifications falling in the entry level to level 3 range.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 250994145, "similarity": 0.9939024390243902, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "fe6061e117ddab9ba8458bb92ed66c05167ce744ef87181d79831c36fe614d47", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "entry level to level 7", "matched_aliases": ["entry level to level 7"], "query_id": "test2443", "question_hash": "fffb5aa31754e26835e405c03728d9f303d88d2b2ca1c2052e738770547e11bd", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "c4806a4846d3b03c44ff7ed617afe30666f3ffc4c652d1bf3553b14457031824", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 870369532, "similarity": 0.15752212389380532, "source_content_hash": "f02bca23cc7d6fcefe09cf8a494cdb4344aa760f09028379374ef88a7d073172", "source_hash": "68d95a65247a72044f0333f34ce4aca6d98d11b605d3a9474a20f8a48afbf817", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "bda99ef696e50e8f071524ce66de26f3b86fc884c8980e4554267382b319298d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "valid